name aastex
shortdesc Macros for manuscript preparation for AAS Journals
longdesc The package provides a document class for preparing papers for
longdesc American Astronomical Society publications. Authors who wish to
longdesc submit papers to AAS journals are strongly urged to use this
longdesc class in preference to any of the alternatives available.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/AASJournals/AASTeX7/issues
catalogue-contact-home https://journals.aas.org/aastex-package-for-manuscript-preparation
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/AASJournals/AASTeX7
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/aastex
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics astronomy class journalpub
catalogue-version 7.0.1

name abbr
shortdesc Simple macros supporting abbreviations for Plain and LaTeX
longdesc The package provides some simple macros to support
longdesc abbreviations in Plain TeX or LaTeX. It allows writing (e.g.)
longdesc \<TEX> instead of \TeX, hence frees users from having to escape
longdesc space after parameterless macros.
catalogue-ctan /macros/generic/abbr
catalogue-license pd
catalogue-topics abbrev shortcut

name abc
shortdesc Support ABC music notation in LaTeX
longdesc The abc package lets you include lines of music written in the
longdesc ABC Plus language. The package will then employ the \write18
longdesc facility to convert your notation to PostScript (using the
longdesc established utility abcm2ps) and hence to the format needed for
longdesc inclusion in your document.
catalogue-also abc2mtex
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/abc
catalogue-license lppl1.2
catalogue-topics foreign-import music
catalogue-version 2.0b

name abnt
shortdesc Typesetting academic works according to ABNT rules
longdesc The ABNT package provides a clean and practical implementation
longdesc of the ABNT rules for academic texts. Its purpose is to be as
longdesc simple and user-friendly as possible.
catalogue-also biblatex-abnt abntex2
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/abnt
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics portuguese-br

name abntex2
shortdesc Typeset technical and scientific Brazilian documents based on ABNT rules
longdesc The bundle provides support for typesetting technical and
longdesc scientific Brazilian documents (like academic thesis, articles,
longdesc reports, research project and others) based on the ABNT rules
longdesc (Associacao Brasileira de Normas Tecnicas). It replaces the old
longdesc abntex.
catalogue-contact-announce https://github.com/abntex/abntex2/wiki/ReleaseNotes
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/abntex/abntex2/issues
catalogue-contact-development https://github.com/abntex/abntex2/graphs/contributors
catalogue-contact-home https://www.abntex.net.br
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/abntex/abntex2
catalogue-contact-support https://github.com/abntex/abntex2/wiki
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/abntex2
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics class dissertation portuguese-br tagged-pdf-partially
catalogue-version 1.9.7

name abntex2-ufv
shortdesc Undergraduate thesis class for UFV (Brazil), based on abnTeX2
longdesc abntex2-ufv is a LaTeX class, built on top of the abnTeX2
longdesc class, for undergraduate final theses (TCC) of the Information
longdesc Systems program at the Federal University of Vicosa (UFV), Rio
longdesc Paranaiba campus, Brazil. It implements the formatting rules of
longdesc the UFV normalization manual (2026-2 edition; ABNT NBR
longdesc 14724/2025, NBR 6023/2025 and NBR 10520/2023): page layout,
longdesc fonts, section headings, cover, title and approval pages,
longdesc abstract, lists of figures/tables/charts/code, acronym list
longdesc (via acro), glossary, figure/table/chart captions with source
longdesc and notes, and BibLaTeX-abnt tweaks. The class sets the
longdesc defaults (12pt, A4, one-sided, Brazilian Portuguese) and loads
longdesc the packages every thesis needs. The customization package
longdesc abntex2-ufv.sty is loaded by the class; using it directly on
longdesc top of abntex2 is deprecated since version 1.5 and will be
longdesc discontinued in version 2.0. The documentation (in Portuguese)
longdesc contains a complete example thesis, and an empty template is
longdesc included.
catalogue-also abntex2
catalogue-contact-announce https://github.com/Smarzaro/abntex2-ufv/releases
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/Smarzaro/abntex2-ufv/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/Smarzaro/abntex2-ufv
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/abntex2-ufv
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics class dissertation doc-templ portuguese-br
catalogue-version 1.6.1

name abntexto
shortdesc LaTeX class for formatting academic papers in ABNT standards
longdesc This is a LaTeX class created for Brazilian students to
longdesc facilitate the use of standards from the Associacao Brasileira
longdesc de Normas Tecnicas (ABNT) in academic works like TCCs,
longdesc dissertations, theses.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/ElaysonAbreu/abntexto
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/abntexto
catalogue-license pd
catalogue-topics class dissertation portuguese-br std-conform
catalogue-version 1.1

name abntexto-uece
shortdesc LaTeX class for formatting academic papers in UECE standards
longdesc This is a unofficial LaTeX class created for Brazilian students
longdesc to facilitate the use of standards from the Universidade
longdesc Estadual do Ceara (UECE) in academic works like TCCs,
longdesc dissertations, and theses.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/ElaysonAbreu/abntexto-uece
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/abntexto-uece
catalogue-license pd
catalogue-topics class dissertation portuguese-br std-conform
catalogue-version 1.0

name abntexto-ufc
shortdesc Unofficial LaTeX class for academic works following UFC-oriented formatting
longdesc This is an unofficial, community-maintained LaTeX class for
longdesc academic works at the Federal University of Ceara (UFC),
longdesc Brazil. It is built on top of the abntexto class and provides
longdesc UFC-oriented front matter, academic-work profiles,
longdesc research-project and scientific-article profiles, bibliography
longdesc integration, academic objects, and related formatting support.
longdesc The project is not an official or UFC-homologated template
longdesc unless the University explicitly grants that status.
catalogue-contact-announce https://github.com/tiagosombrra/abntexto-ufc/releases
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/tiagosombrra/abntexto-ufc/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/tiagosombrra/abntexto-ufc
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/abntexto-ufc
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics class dissertation doc-templ portuguese-br std-conform
catalogue-version 3.0.5

name aboensis
shortdesc A late medieval OpenType cursive font
longdesc The package contains the free OpenType medieval cursive font
longdesc Aboensis and a style file to use it in XeLaTeX documents. The
longdesc font is based on Codex Aboensis, that is a law book written in
longdesc Sweden in the 1430s. Since medieval cursive is very difficult
longdesc to read for modern people, the font is not suitable for use as
longdesc an ordinary book font, but is intended for emulating late
longdesc medieval manuscripts. The font contains two sets of initials:
longdesc Lombardic and cursive to go with the basic alphabet, and there
longdesc is support for writing two-colored initials and capitals. There
longdesc are also a large number of abbreviation sigla that can be
longdesc accessed as ligature substitutions. The style file contains
longdesc macros that help to use the extended features of the font such
longdesc as initials and two-colored capitals. There are also macros to
longdesc help achieve even pages with consistent line spacing.
catalogue-ctan /fonts/aboensis
catalogue-license ofl lppl1.3c cc-by-4 pd
catalogue-topics font-bookhand font-calligraphic font-display font-medieval font-otf font-proportional font-supp tagged-pdf-incompatible

name abraces
shortdesc Asymmetric over-/underbraces in maths
longdesc The package provides a character key-driven interface to
longdesc supplement new constructions of the traditional \overbrace and
longdesc \underbrace pairs in an asymmetric or arbitrary way.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/wgrundlingh/abraces
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/abraces
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics maths maths-symbol tagged-pdf-incompatible
catalogue-version 2.2

name abspos
shortdesc Absolute placement with coffins
longdesc This package lets you place contents at an absolute position,
longdesc anchored at some specified part of the contents, similar to how
longdesc TikZ nodes work, though without using the two-pass strategy of
longdesc TikZ. It also avoids messing with the order of beamer overlays,
longdesc which is what happens when one uses the textpos package with
longdesc the overlay option. The solution used is quite straightforward,
longdesc combining coffins (using l3coffins) with the placement
longdesc mechanisms of atbegshi.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/mlhetland/abspos.sty/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/mlhetland/abspos.sty
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/abspos
catalogue-license mit
catalogue-topics layout
catalogue-version 0.1

name abstract
shortdesc Control the typesetting of the abstract environment
longdesc The abstract package gives you control over the typesetting of
longdesc the abstract environment, and in particular provides for a one
longdesc column abstract in a two column paper.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/LaTeX-Package-Repositories/herries-press
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/abstract
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics abstract tagged-pdf-partially
catalogue-version 1.2a

name abstyles
catalogue abstyles-orig
shortdesc Adaptable BibTeX styles
longdesc A family of modifications of the standard BibTeX styles whose
longdesc behaviour may be changed by changing the user document, without
longdesc change to the styles themselves. The package is largely used
longdesc nowadays in its adaptation for working with Babel.
catalogue-ctan /biblio/bibtex/contrib/abstyles
catalogue-license other-free
catalogue-topics bibtex-supp

name academicons
shortdesc Font containing high quality icons of online academic profiles
longdesc The academicons package provides access in (La)TeX to 146 high
longdesc quality icons of online academic profiles included in the free
longdesc Academicons font. This package works with both Xe(La)TeX or
longdesc Lua(La)TeX by using fontspec to load the included font, as well
longdesc as with pdf(La)TeX by loading a Type 1 converted format of the
longdesc original font. The Academicons font was designed by James Walsh
longdesc and released (see http://jpswalsh.github.io/academicons/) under
longdesc the open SIL Open Font License. This package is a
longdesc redistribution of the free Academicons font with specific
longdesc bindings for (La)TeX. It is inspired and based on the
longdesc fontawesome package. The generic \aiicon macro takes as
longdesc mandatory argument the [?]name[?] of the desired icon. Icons
longdesc can also be accessed directly by their respective macro. For
longdesc example, \aiicon{googlescholar} yields the same result as
longdesc \aiGoogleScholar. The full list of icons with their respective
longdesc names and direct commands can be found in the manual.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/diogo-fernan/academicons
catalogue-ctan /fonts/academicons
catalogue-license lppl1.3c ofl
catalogue-topics font font-supp-symbol font-symbol font-ttf tagged-pdf-partially
catalogue-version 1.9.6-3

name accanthis
shortdesc LaTeX support for the Accanthis font family
longdesc Accanthis No. 3 is designed by Hirwin Harendal and is suitable
longdesc as an alternative to fonts such as Garamond, Galliard, Horley
longdesc old style, Sabon, and Bembo. The support files are suitable for
longdesc use with all LaTeX engines.
catalogue-contact-home https://arkandis.tuxfamily.org/adffonts.html
catalogue-ctan /fonts/accanthis
catalogue-license gpl2+ lppl
catalogue-topics font font-body font-otf font-proportional font-serif font-supp font-t1enc font-type1 tagged-pdf

name accents
shortdesc Multiple mathematical accents
longdesc A package for multiple accents in mathematics, with nice
longdesc features concerning the creation of accents and placement of
longdesc scripts.
catalogue-contact-home https://www.texnia.com/
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/jbezos
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/accents
catalogue-license mit
catalogue-topics maths tagged-pdf-partially
catalogue-version 1.4

name accfonts
shortdesc Utilities to derive new fonts from existing ones
longdesc The accfonts package contains three utilities to permit easy
longdesc manipulation of fonts, in particular the creation of unusual
longdesc accented characters. Mkt1font works on Adobe Type 1 fonts,
longdesc vpl2vpl works on TeX virtual fonts and vpl2ovp transforms a TeX
longdesc font to an Omega one. All three programs read in a font (either
longdesc the font itself or a property list), together with a simple
longdesc definition file containing lines such as 128 z acute; they then
longdesc write out a new version of the font with the requested new
longdesc characters in the numerical slots specified. Great care is
longdesc taken over the positioning of accents, and over the provision
longdesc of kerning information for new characters; mkt1font also
longdesc generates suitable hints to enhance quality at small sizes or
longdesc poor resolutions. The programs are written in Perl.
catalogue-also a2ac
catalogue-ctan /fonts/utilities/accfonts
catalogue-license gpl
catalogue-topics font-proc omega
catalogue-version 0.25

