name adjmulticol
shortdesc Adjusting margins for multicolumn and single column output
longdesc The package adds, to the multicol package, the option to change
longdesc the margins for multicolumn and unicolumn layout. The package
longdesc understands the difference between the even and odd margins for
longdesc two side printing.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/borisveytsman/adjmulticol/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/borisveytsman/adjmulticol
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/adjmulticol
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics layout multicol tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 1.5

name adjustbox
shortdesc Graphics package-alike macros for general boxes
longdesc The package provides several macros to adjust boxed content.
longdesc One purpose is to supplement the standard graphics package,
longdesc which defines the macros \resizebox, \scalebox and \rotatebox ,
longdesc with the macros\trimbox and \clipbox. The main feature is the
longdesc general \adjustbox macro which extends the key=value interface
longdesc of \includegraphics from the graphics package and applies it to
longdesc general text content. Additional provided box macros are
longdesc \lapbox, \marginbox, \minsizebox, \maxsizebox and \phantombox.
longdesc All macros use the collectbox package to read the content as a
longdesc box and not as a macro argument. This allows for all forms of
longdesc content including special material like verbatim content. A
longdesc special feature of collectbox is used to provide matching
longdesc environments with the identical names as the macros.
catalogue-also gincltex collectbox realboxes
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/MartinScharrer/adjustbox/issues
catalogue-contact-home https://github.com/MartinScharrer/adjustbox
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/MartinScharrer/adjustbox.git
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/adjustbox
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics box-breaking box-manip tagged-pdf-partially typesetting
catalogue-version 1.3c

