name adrconv
shortdesc BibTeX styles to implement an address database
longdesc The bundle provides a collection of BibTeX style files to turn
longdesc an address database stored in the .bib format into files
longdesc suitable for printing as address books or included into letter
longdesc classes like akletter or scrletter2. The data may be sorted
longdesc either by name or birthday and output provides files in various
longdesc formats for address books or time planners.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/adrconv
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics biblio bibtex-supp
catalogue-version 1.4

name adtrees
shortdesc Macros for drawing adpositional trees
longdesc This package provides a means to write adpositional trees, a
longdesc formalism devoted to representing natural language expressions.
longdesc The package relies on epic and cancel.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/adtrees
catalogue-license gpl
catalogue-topics linguistic tree
catalogue-version 1.1

name advdate
shortdesc Print a date relative to today
longdesc Provides macros which can add a specified number of days to the
longdesc current date (as specified in \today), to save, set and restore
longdesc the current date and to print it. Intended use is, for example,
longdesc in invoices payable within 14 days from today, etc. The package
longdesc has only been tested with Czech dates.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/advdate
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics date-time tagged-pdf

name advice
shortdesc Extend commands and environments
longdesc Like its namesake from the Emacs world, this cross-format
longdesc package implements a generic framework for extending the
longdesc functionality of selected commands and environments. It was
longdesc developed as an auxiliary package of Memoize. This is why it
longdesc is, somewhat unconventionally, documented alongside that
longdesc package. This applies to both the manual and the documented
longdesc code listing.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/sasozivanovic/memoize
catalogue-ctan /macros/generic/advice
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics macro-def macro-gen macro-supp tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 1.1.1

name ae
shortdesc Virtual fonts for T1 encoded CMR-fonts
longdesc A set of virtual fonts which emulates T1 coded fonts using the
longdesc standard CM fonts. The package name, AE fonts, supposedly
longdesc stands for Almost European. The main use of the package was to
longdesc produce PDF files using Adobe Type 1 versions of the CM fonts
longdesc instead of bitmapped EC fonts. Note that direct substitutes for
longdesc the bitmapped EC fonts are now available, via the CM-super,
longdesc Latin Modern and (in a restricted way) CM-LGC font sets.
catalogue-also zefonts aeguill
catalogue-ctan /fonts/ae
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics font font-t1enc font-virtual tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 1.4

name aeguill
shortdesc Add several kinds of guillemets to the ae fonts
longdesc The package enables the user to add guillemets from several
longdesc source (Polish cmr, Cyrillic cmr, lasy and ec) to the ae fonts.
longdesc This was useful when the ae fonts were used to produce PDF
longdesc files, since the additional guillemets exist in fonts available
longdesc in Adobe Type 1 format.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/aeguill
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics font font-t1enc font-virtual tagged-pdf

name aeskwadraat
shortdesc A-Eskwadraat package catalogue
longdesc This is the official package catalogue of the A-Eskwadraat
longdesc association. A-Eskwadraat is the study association for
longdesc mathematics and physics at Utrecht University. The catalogue
longdesc includes packages for meeting notes, a beamer theme, invoices
longdesc and letters. The beamer theme can also be used for Utrecht
longdesc University-styled presentations. Do refer to the UU website for
