catalogue-version 6.101

name anima
shortdesc Create slideshows with simple animations
longdesc The idea for this package arose from noticing that including
longdesc the \pause command from the beamer class within the \foreach
longdesc loop command from the TikZ package creates a sequence of
longdesc frames, where each slide presents a step in the construction of
longdesc the image. The purpose of the anima class is to provide macros
longdesc that simplify the use of this effect for creating animated
longdesc slide presentations. Although the functionality of this class
longdesc can be compared to the transition effects of the beamer class,
longdesc it is not a dependency of the anima class. However, the class
longdesc makes extensive use of the image creation language provided by
longdesc the TikZ package. Lastly, it is worth noting a comparison
longdesc between this class and the animate package. The animate package
longdesc can create embedded animations within the document, while the
longdesc anima class produces an animation where each frame corresponds
longdesc to a page of the document. This distinction highlights the
longdesc different design goals of the anima class.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/anima
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics class graphics-motion presentation
catalogue-version 1.1

name animate
shortdesc Create PDF and SVG animations from graphics files and inline graphics
longdesc The package provides an interface to create portable,
longdesc JavaScript driven PDF and SVG animations from sets of graphics
longdesc files or from inline graphics, such as LaTeX picture
longdesc environment, PSTricks or pgf/TikZ generated pictures, or just
longdesc from typeset text.
catalogue-contact-repository https://gitlab.com/agrahn/animate
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/animate
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics graphics-motion

name animategif
shortdesc Embed animated GIF files in PDF documents, decoded in pure Lua
longdesc The package provides \animategif{file.gif}, which embeds an
longdesc animated GIF as a PDF animation. The GIF is decoded in pure Lua
longdesc - in-process with LuaLaTeX, or with texlua through shell escape
longdesc with pdfLaTeX and XeLaTeX - so no external programs such as
longdesc ImageMagick are needed. Frames are written as compact PNG
longdesc images, storing only the pixels that change between frames, and
longdesc cached. The animate package then embeds them with a timeline
longdesc that follows the GIF's per-frame delays, disposal methods,
longdesc transparency and loop count. Options select frame ranges,
longdesc change the speed or number of plays, downsample, or include a
longdesc single frame as a still image (automatically in beamer
longdesc handouts).
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/Ramlaoui/animategif
catalogue-contact-support https://github.com/Ramlaoui/animategif/issues
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/animategif
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics graphics-incl graphics-motion use-luatex
catalogue-version 1.0.0

name annee-scolaire
shortdesc Automatically typeset the academic year (French way)
longdesc This package provides a macro \anneescolaire to automatically
longdesc write the academic year in the French way, according to the
longdesc date of compilation, two other macros to obtain the first and
longdesc the second calendar year of the academic year, a macro to be
longdesc redefined to change the presentation of the years.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/annee-scolaire
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics calendar
catalogue-version 1.6

name annotate
