name aspen
shortdesc Simple crypto notation in LaTeX
longdesc The Aspen package implements LaTeX commands closely related to
longdesc what is often called security protocol notation, standard
longdesc protocol engineering notation, standard protocol notation, or
longdesc protocol narrations. Optionally, the Aspen package also
longdesc implements LaTeX commands for Burrows-Abadi-Needham logic (BAN
longdesc logic). The name Aspen can be an abbreviation for A Security
longdesc Protocol Engineering Notation, but another possible
longdesc abbreviation is Anderson-inspired Standard Protocol Engineering
longdesc Notation, in memory of the late Professor Ross J. Anderson who
longdesc has meant so much for the fields of computer security,
longdesc distributed systems, and, in particular, security engineering.
catalogue-contact-home https://www.pg12.org/software
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/aspen
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics engineering scientific-docs security
catalogue-version 2.5

