name biblatex-abs-annote
shortdesc Annotated bibliographies with abstracts and annotations for BibLaTeX
longdesc The package extends any BibLaTeX style with an
longdesc annotated-bibliography presentation: below each reference it
longdesc renders the entry's abstract and the user's annotation, both
longdesc drawn from standard BibLaTeX fields (abstract, and annotation
longdesc or annote). Either field may be omitted on a per-entry basis,
longdesc so the same bibliography can mix plain and annotated citations
longdesc freely. The package patches the sixteen standard BibLaTeX
longdesc drivers via xpatch, so it composes with any bibliography style
longdesc that uses the standard driver names (authoryear, apa, numeric,
longdesc chicago-authordate, etc.). All visual aspects (e.g., labels,
longdesc fonts, indentation, and spacing) are controlled by redefinable
longdesc commands and lengths. The package is the LaTeX component of the
longdesc cross-format ab-annotate toolchain, which shares the same .bib
longdesc conventions with companion packages for Typst and Quarto.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/cwimpy/ab-annotate/issues
catalogue-contact-home https://github.com/cwimpy/ab-annotate
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/cwimpy/ab-annotate/tree/main/latex
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/biblatex-contrib/biblatex-abs-annote
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics biblatex
catalogue-version 0.1.1

name biblatex-accursius
shortdesc Citing features for Italian jurists
longdesc This style is primarily aimed at Italian legal jurists and
longdesc provides them with the ability to cite legal materials, such as
longdesc legislative acts, regulations, soft law, treaties and case law.
longdesc Additionally, the style codifies the most prevalent citation
longdesc practices amongst Italian legal scholars. Specifically, with
longdesc regard to the citation of legal materials, this style, instead
longdesc of developing the entry types @jurisdiction, @legal, and
longdesc @legislation, creates a new one: @itprov, which can describe a
longdesc wide range of legal sources. Furthermore, it creates a second
longdesc new entry type: @notetoprov, which is used specifically to cite
longdesc so-called note a sentenza (notes to judgement), which closely
longdesc mirrors @itprov, but is literature and, therefore, is intended
longdesc to have the same treatment as standard entry types. The
longdesc citation commands are the standard ones. The @itprov entry type
longdesc comprises the list institution to indicate which authority
longdesc adopted the cited act; the kindprov, nprov, provtitle (or
longdesc titleparties) fields to indicate the minimal ID of the act and
longdesc many others. Finally, the entry type allows to specify where
longdesc the cited act was consulted, whether from an official bulletin
longdesc (the ofbull field), an official portal or a private database
longdesc (the ofportal field), or a journal or collection.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/francesco-contini/biblatex-accursius
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/biblatex-contrib/biblatex-accursius
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics biblatex italian legal
catalogue-version 1.0

