name biblatex-greifswald
shortdesc The author-date BibLaTeX Greifswald style
longdesc Greifswald bibliographies consist of two columns: The left one
longdesc contains the publication date, while title and other
longdesc bibliographical data (the body) are printed in the right
longdesc column. The author names are printed in bold face and span both
longdesc columns. Titles are printed upright and not surrounded by
longdesc quotation marks. The body of dependent publications (@article,
longdesc @inCollection, etc.) is divided into two paragraphs: The first
longdesc contains information that relates to the dependent publication
longdesc itself, such as title, DOI and URL; data relating to the parent
longdesc publication, such as that one's title, editor and ISBN, is
longdesc printed in the second. The publisher and its location are
longdesc printed only if neither DOI, ISBN nor ISSN are known.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/biblatex-contrib/biblatex-greifswald
catalogue-license mit
catalogue-topics biblatex
catalogue-version 1

