name biblatex-opcit-booktitle
shortdesc Use op. cit. for the booktitle of a subentry
longdesc The default citation styles verbose-trad1+; verbose-trad2 ;
longdesc verbose-trad3 use the op. cit. form in order to have a shorter
longdesc reference when a title has already been cited. However, when
longdesc you cite two entries which share the same booktitle but not the
longdesc same title, the op. cit. mechanism does not work. This package
longdesc enables to obtain references like this: Author1, Title, in
longdesc Booktitle, Location, Publisher, Year, pages xxx Author2,
longdesc Title2, in Booktitle, op. cit, pages.
