name bibstyles-ru
shortdesc Russian bibliography styles
longdesc This package contains a set of BibTeX and LaTeX styles for
longdesc typesetting bibliographies according to Russian GOST standards.
longdesc Numbered bibliographies and author-year citation styles are
longdesc supported. Concise and detailed source descriptions can be
longdesc generated. The package supports the layout of two
longdesc bibliographies. This feature is designed to separate the
longdesc author's and cited works in phd theses.
catalogue-ctan /biblio/bibtex/contrib/bibstyles-ru
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics bibtex-supp russian std-conform
catalogue-version 1

name bibtex
shortdesc Process bibliographies (bib files) for LaTeX or other formats
longdesc BibTeX allows the user to store his citation data in generic
longdesc form, while printing citations in a document in the form
longdesc specified by a BibTeX style, to be specified in the document
longdesc itself (one often needs a LaTeX citation-style package, such as
longdesc natbib, as well). BibTeX knows nothing about Unicode sorting
longdesc algorithms or scripts, although it will pass on whatever bytes
longdesc it reads. Its descendant bibtexu does support Unicode, via the
longdesc ICU library. The older alternative bibtex8 supports 8-bit
longdesc character sets. Another Unicode-aware alternative is the
longdesc (independently developed) biber program, used with the BibLaTeX
longdesc package to typeset its output.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://lists.tug.org/tex-k
catalogue-contact-home https://tug.org/bibtex
catalogue-contact-repository https://tug.org/svn/texlive/trunk/Build/source/texk/web2c/
catalogue-contact-support https://lists.tug.org/tex-k
catalogue-ctan /biblio/bibtex/base
catalogue-license knuth
catalogue-topics biblio bibtex-doc bibtex-supp tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 0.99e

