name bitelist
shortdesc Split list, in TeX's mouth
longdesc The package provides commands for splitting a token list at the
longdesc first occurrence of another (specified) token list. I.e., for
longdesc given token lists s, t return b and the shortest a, such that t
longdesc = a s b. The package's mechanism differs from those of packages
longdesc providing similar features, in the following ways: the method
longdesc uses TeX's mechanism of reading delimited macro parameters;
longdesc splitting macros work by pure expansion, without assignments;
longdesc the operation is carried out in a single macro call. A variant
longdesc of the operation is provided, that retains outer braces.
catalogue-also datatool stringstrings ted texapi xstring
catalogue-contact-support https://www.webdesign-bu.de/uwe_lueck/contact.html
catalogue-ctan /macros/generic/bitelist
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics macro-supp text-manip
catalogue-version 0.1

