name chicago
shortdesc A Chicago bibliography style
longdesc Chicago is a BibTeX style that follows the B reference style of
longdesc the 13th Edition of the Chicago manual of style; a LaTeX
longdesc package (to LaTeX 2.09 conventions) is also provided. The style
longdesc was derived from the newapa style.
catalogue-ctan /biblio/bibtex/contrib/chicago
catalogue-license other-free
catalogue-topics bibtex-supp tagged-pdf

name chicago-annote
shortdesc Chicago-based annotated BibTeX style
longdesc This is a revision of chicagoa.bst, using the commonly-used
longdesc annote field in place of the original's annotation.
catalogue-ctan /biblio/bibtex/contrib/chicago-annote
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics bibtex-annote bibtex-supp

name chicagoa
shortdesc Chicago bibliography style with annotations
longdesc This is a modification of the author's chicago style, to
longdesc support an annotation field in bibliographies.
catalogue-ctan /biblio/bibtex/contrib/misc/chicagoa.bst
catalogue-license other-free
catalogue-topics bibtex-annote bibtex-supp

name chicagolinks
shortdesc Chicago bibliography style that allows annotations
longdesc This bibliography style is intended to extend the Chicago
longdesc bibliography style so that it can be annotated and at the same
longdesc allowing DOI and URL fields.
catalogue-also chicago-annote achicago-bst
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/mariabnd/miscellaneous/blob/master/LaTeX/chicagolinks.bst
catalogue-ctan /biblio/bibtex/contrib/chicagolinks
catalogue-license mit
catalogue-topics bibtex-annote bibtex-supp
catalogue-version 2.1

name chickenize
shortdesc Use Lua callbacks for interesting textual effects
longdesc The package allows manipulations of any LuaTeX document (it is
longdesc known to work with Plain LuaTeX and LuaLaTeX). Most of the
longdesc package's functions are merely for fun or educational use, but
longdesc some functions (for example, colorstretch for visualising the
longdesc badness and font expansion of each line, and letterspaceadjust
longdesc doing what its name says) could be useful in a normal LuaTeX
longdesc document.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/alt/chickenize
catalogue-ctan /macros/luatex/generic/chickenize
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics games luatex typesetting
catalogue-version 0.3

name chifoot
shortdesc Chicago-style footnote formatting
longdesc A very short snippet. Will set the footnotes to be conformant
longdesc with the Chicago style, so the footnotes at the bottom of the
longdesc page are now marked with a full-sized number, rather than with
longdesc a superscript number.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/chifoot
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics footnote page-hf
catalogue-version 1.0

