name chletter
shortdesc Class for typesetting letters to Swiss rules
longdesc The class enables composition of letters fitting into Swiss C5
longdesc & C6/5 windowed envelopes. No assumption is made about the
longdesc language used. The class is based on the standard LaTeX classes
longdesc and is compatible with the LaTeX letter class. It is not
longdesc limited to letters and may be used as a generic document class;
longdesc it is used with the chextras package.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/chletter
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics letter swiss
catalogue-version 2.0

name chngcntr
shortdesc Change the resetting of counters
longdesc Defines commands \counterwithin (which sets up a counter to be
longdesc reset when another is incremented) and \counterwithout (which
longdesc unsets such a relationship).
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/LaTeX-Package-Repositories/herries-press
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/chngcntr
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics counter-mgmt macro-supp tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 1.1a

name chordbars
shortdesc Print chord grids for pop/jazz tunes
longdesc This Tikz-based music-related package is targeted at pop/jazz
longdesc guitar/bass/piano musicians. They usually need only the chords
longdesc and the song structure. This package produces rectangular song
longdesc patterns with one square per bar, with the chord shown inside
longdesc the square. It also handles the song structure by showing the
longdesc bar count and the repetitions of the patterns.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/skramm/chordbars/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/skramm/chordbars
catalogue-ctan /graphics/pgf/contrib/chordbars
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics chords music pgf-tikz
catalogue-version 1.3.2

name chordbox
shortdesc Draw chord diagrams
longdesc This package provides two macros for drawing chord diagrams, as
longdesc may be found for example in chord charts/books and educational
longdesc materials. They are composed as TikZ pictures and have several
longdesc options to modify their appearance.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/sfranzen/chordbox/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/sfranzen/chordbox
catalogue-ctan /graphics/pgf/contrib/chordbox
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics chords music pgf-tikz
catalogue-version 1.0

name chronology
shortdesc Provides a horizontal timeline
longdesc A timeline package that allows labelling of events with per-day
longdesc granularity. Other features include relative positioning with
longdesc unit specification, adjustable tick mark step size, and scaling
longdesc to specified width.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/chronology
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics calendar pgf-tikz planning tagged-pdf-incompatible
catalogue-version 2.0

name chronos
shortdesc TikZ-based package for drawing customisable timelines with support for colour schemes, styles and memoization
longdesc The package supports drawing timelines and aims to be highly
longdesc customisable. Extensive configuration options are offered via a
longdesc standard key-value interface based on pgfkeys. Custom colour
longdesc schemes and styles are supported, and the package includes
longdesc documented examples of each. Memoization works out-of-the-box
longdesc if the memoize package is loaded. The code was developed as a
longdesc result of questions concerning difficulties in customising the
longdesc output of existing packages for drawing timelines, which
longdesc sometimes eschew pgfkeys and are often challenging to
longdesc configure, even when based on PGF/TikZ.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/cfr42/chronos
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/chronos
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics calendar diagram pgf-tikz
catalogue-version 0.9.6

name chronosys
shortdesc Drawing time-line diagrams
longdesc Macros to produce time line diagrams. Interfaces for Plain TeX,
longdesc ConTeXt and LaTeX are provided.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/chronosys
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics diagram tagged-pdf-incompatible
catalogue-version 1.2

name chs-physics-report
shortdesc Physics lab reports for Carmel High School
longdesc This package may optionally be used by students at Carmel High
longdesc School in Indiana in the United States to write physics lab
longdesc reports for FW physics courses. As many students are beginners
longdesc at LaTeX, it also attempts to simplify the report-writing
longdesc process by offering macros for commonly used notation and by
longdesc automatically formatting the documents for students who will
longdesc only use TeX for mathematics and not typesetting. The package
longdesc depends on amsmath, calc, fancyhdr, geometry, graphicx,
longdesc letltxmacro, titlesec, transparent, and xcolor.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/chs-physics-report
catalogue-license pd cc-by-sa-3
catalogue-topics physics report-like

name chscite
shortdesc Bibliography style for Chalmers University of Technology
longdesc The package, heavily based on the harvard package for
longdesc Harvard-style citations, provides a citation suite for students
longdesc at Chalmers University of Technology that follows given
longdesc recommendations.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/chscite
catalogue-license lppl1.2
catalogue-topics bibtex-supp
catalogue-version 2.9999

name churchslavonic
shortdesc Typeset documents in Church Slavonic language using Unicode
longdesc The package provides fonts, hyphenation patterns, and
longdesc supporting macros to typeset Church Slavonic texts. It depends
longdesc on the following other packages: fonts-churchslavonic,
longdesc hyph-utf8, intcalc, etoolbox, and xcolor.
catalogue-also fonts-churchslavonic
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/slavonic/cu-tex/issues
