name citeref
shortdesc Add reference-page-list to bibliography-items
longdesc The package does its job without using the indexing facilities,
longdesc and needs no special \cite-replacement package.
catalogue-also backref
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/citeref
catalogue-license bsd4
catalogue-topics bibtex-supp
catalogue-version 1.1

name citeright
shortdesc Specify accurate natbib citations for diverse naming conventions
longdesc This package provides the command \citeright for aliasing
longdesc in-text citations and specifying their appearance in the list
longdesc of references. It is specifically tailored for use with the
longdesc natbib package and is compatible with citation managers such as
longdesc BibDesk and JabRef. The package is intended to provide a means
longdesc for respecting the diverse naming conventions of cited authors
longdesc and, in this way, decolonizing academia.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/citeright
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics cite-supp
catalogue-version 1.0.0

name cje
shortdesc LaTeX document class for CJE articles
longdesc The cje article class allows authors to format their papers to
longdesc Canadian Journal of Economics style with minimum effort. The
longdesc class includes options for two other formats: review (double
longdesc spaced, for use at the submission stage) and proof (used by the
longdesc typesetters to prepare the proof authors will receive for
longdesc approval).
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/cje
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics journalpub
catalogue-version 1.07

name cjhebrew
shortdesc Typeset Hebrew with LaTeX
longdesc The cjhebrew package provides Adobe Type 1 fonts for Hebrew,
longdesc and LaTeX macros to support their use. Hebrew text can be
longdesc vocalised, and a few accents are also available. The package
longdesc makes it easy to include Hebrew text in other-language
longdesc documents. The package makes use of the e-TeX extensions to
longdesc TeX, so should be run using an e-LaTeX.
catalogue-ctan /language/hebrew/cjhebrew
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics font font-hebrew font-supp font-type1 hebrew
catalogue-version 0.2a

name cjk
shortdesc Support for Chinese, Japanese, and Korean in LaTeX
longdesc CJK is a macro package for LaTeX, providing simultaneous
longdesc support for various Asian scripts in many encodings (including
longdesc Unicode): Chinese (both traditional and simplified), Japanese,
longdesc Korean and Thai. A special add-on feature is an interface to
longdesc the Emacs editor (cjk-enc.el) which gives simultaneous,
longdesc easy-to-use support to a bunch of other scripts in addition to
longdesc the above - Cyrillic, Greek, Latin-based scripts, Russian and
longdesc Vietnamese are supported.
catalogue-also cjk-fonts
catalogue-ctan /language/chinese/CJK
catalogue-license gpl2
catalogue-topics chinese font-cjk font-use japanese korean thai
catalogue-version 4.8.5

