catalogue-license gpl2+
catalogue-topics dissertation
catalogue-version 4.8

name classpack
shortdesc XML mastering for LaTeX classes and packages
longdesc The package provides an experiment in using XML (specifically
longdesc DocBook 5) to mark up and maintain LaTeX classes and packages.
longdesc XSLT 2 styleheets generate the .dtx and .ins distribution files
longdesc expected by end users.
catalogue-ctan /support/classpack
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics class-supp package-devel
catalogue-version 1.19

name clawxiv
shortdesc Provenance typesetting for human-AI collaborative writing
longdesc The clawxiv package provides LaTeX environments for typesetting
longdesc text according to its authorial provenance in documents that
longdesc mix human and AI contributions. Three principal environments
longdesc are provided: seniorquote for the corresponding human author,
longdesc aiquote for an AI coauthor, and coauthorquote for other human
longdesc contributors. Convenient aliases humanprompt and airesp support
longdesc prompt/response interaction transcripts. The package is part of
longdesc the ClawXiv framework for archiving human-AI co-authored papers
longdesc with full provenance tracking. A white paper is available at
longdesc ClawXiv
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/clawxiv
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics doc-mgmt editorial quotation
catalogue-version 0.4.3

name cleanthesis
shortdesc A clean LaTeX style for thesis documents
longdesc The package offers a clean, simple, and elegant LaTeX style for
longdesc thesis documents.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/cleanthesis
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics dissertation
catalogue-version 0.4.0

name clearsans
shortdesc Clear Sans fonts with LaTeX support
longdesc Clear Sans was designed by Daniel Ratighan at Monotype under
longdesc the direction of the User Experience team at Intel's Open
longdesc Source Technology Center. Clear Sans is available in three
longdesc weights (regular, medium, and bold) with corresponding italics,
longdesc plus light and thin upright (without italics). Clear Sans has
longdesc minimized, unambiguous characters and slightly narrow
longdesc proportions, making it ideal for UI design. Its strong,
longdesc recognizable forms avoid distracting ambiguity, making Clear
longdesc Sans comfortable for reading short UI labels and long passages
longdesc in both screen and print. The fonts are available in both
longdesc TrueType and Type 1 formats.
catalogue-ctan /fonts/clearsans
catalogue-license apache2 lppl
catalogue-topics font font-body font-cyrillic font-greek font-proportional font-sans font-supp font-t1enc font-ttf font-type1 tagged-pdf

name clefval
shortdesc Key/value support with a hash
longdesc This package provides only two macros viz. \TheKey and
longdesc \TheValue to define then use pairs of key/value and gives a
longdesc semblance of a hash. Syntax: \TheKey{key}{value} to define the
longdesc value associated to the key, does not produce text;
longdesc \TheValue{key} to return the value linked to the key. Both
longdesc arguments of \TheKey are moving as LaTeX defines the term and
longdesc we have sometimes to protect them.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/clefval
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics keyval
catalogue-version 0.1

name cleveref
shortdesc Intelligent cross-referencing
longdesc The package enhances LaTeX's cross-referencing features,
longdesc allowing the format of references to be determined
longdesc automatically according to the type of reference. The formats
longdesc used may be customised in the preamble of a document; babel
longdesc support is available (though the choice of languages remains
longdesc limited: currently Danish, Dutch, English, French, German,
longdesc Italian, Norwegian, Russian, Spanish and Ukrainian). The
longdesc package also offers a means of referencing a list of
longdesc references, each formatted according to its type. In such
longdesc lists, it can collapse sequences of numerically-consecutive
longdesc labels to a reference range.
catalogue-also crefthe
catalogue-contact-home https://www.dr-qubit.org/cleveref.html
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/cleveref
catalogue-license lppl1.2
catalogue-topics label-ref tagged-pdf-partially
catalogue-version 0.21.4

name cleveref-forward
shortdesc Forward-referencing functionality for cleveref
longdesc This package aims at providing the forward-referencing
longdesc functionality for the package cleveref. It is derived from the
longdesc package cleveref-usedon, with several fixes and enhancements.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/Jinwen-XU/cleveref-forward
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/cleveref-forward
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics label-ref

name cleveref-icelandic
shortdesc Icelandic grammatical declension for cleveref cross-references
longdesc The cleveref-icelandic package extends cleveref with Icelandic
longdesc declension support, allowing cross-references to figures,
longdesc tables, equations, and sections to appear in the correct
longdesc grammatical case (nominative, accusative, dative, genitive) in
longdesc both singular and plural. Case can be specified explicitly by
longdesc name (nom/acc/dat/gen or Icelandic abbreviations
longdesc nf/thf/thgf/ef), by number (0-3), or automatically inferred
longdesc from a preposition argument. Built-in declension tables are
longdesc provided for the four most common reference types. Additional
longdesc reference types and prepositions can be declared in the
longdesc document preamble using \DeclareIcrefType and
longdesc \DeclareIscrefPreposition.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/SindriIAV/cleveref-icelandic
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/cleveref-icelandic
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics icelandic label-ref
catalogue-version 0.1

name cleveref-usedon
shortdesc Adds forward-referencing functionality to the cleveref package
longdesc Imagine you are reading a long mathematical text such as a text
longdesc book or a thesis. There are plenty of supplementary lemmas,
longdesc propositions, theorems and/or exercises throughout the whole
longdesc text. You ask yourself Gosh, while Lemma 1.12 is certainly an
longdesc interesting result, where is this result used later on in this
longdesc long text? I really would find that helpful to decide why I
longdesc should read the proof. You can, of course, use the PDF search
longdesc function of your viewer to look up the string Lemma 1.12, but
longdesc wouldn't it be more helpful if Lemma 1.12 already indicated all
longdesc or at least its most useful/crucial applications via an info
longdesc message? This is what this package tries to address: The info
longdesc message Used on p. 40, 43-45 and 101. would then be printed to
longdesc the header of Lemma 1.12. This is done by extending the \cref
longdesc and \Cref commands and giving them an optional argument UsedOn.
longdesc Every time you wish to record a reference in the used on page
longdesc list, you would simply type \cref[UsedOn]{<LabelName>}. If you
longdesc use \cref without this optional argument, this reference won't
longdesc be recorded in this page list.
catalogue-also cleveref-forward
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/SvenPistre/cleveref-usedon/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/SvenPistre/cleveref-usedon
catalogue-contact-support https://github.com/SvenPistre/cleveref-usedon/discussions
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/cleveref-usedon
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics label-ref
catalogue-version 0.4.0

