name concrete
shortdesc Knuth's Concrete Roman typeface for LaTeX
longdesc Concrete Roman fonts, designed by Donald E. Knuth, originally
longdesc for use with Euler mathematics fonts. Alternative mathematics
longdesc fonts, based on the concrete parameter set are available as the
longdesc concmath fonts bundle. LaTeX support is offered by the beton,
longdesc concmath and ccfonts packages. T1- and TS1-encoded versions of
longdesc the fonts are available in the ecc bundle, and Adobe Type 1
longdesc versions of the ecc fonts are part of the cm-super bundle.
catalogue-ctan /fonts/concrete
catalogue-license knuth
catalogue-topics font font-mf tagged-pdf-partially

name concrete-vec
shortdesc Concrete text and mathematics as outlines, with a synthetic bold weight
longdesc This package typesets a document in Donald Knuth's Concrete
longdesc fonts with two properties the existing Concrete packages do not
longdesc jointly provide: every glyph, in text and in mathematics, is a
longdesc vector outline rather than a bitmap; and a bold weight is
longdesc available, synthesised by stroking, in text and in mathematics.
longdesc It is a thin configuration layer over ccfonts, mathastext and
longdesc pdfrender, and targets pdfLaTeX.
catalogue-also concrete-macros
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/concrete-vec
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics font font-maths font-supp
catalogue-version 1.2

name conditext
shortdesc Define and manage conditional content
longdesc This package provides some commands to define and manage
longdesc conditional content in a LaTeX source document. A conditional
longdesc content, in the sense within this is understood in this
longdesc package, is a text (including mathematical or other formulas)
longdesc and/or a graphical element (diagram, figure, image...) as
longdesc substitutable forms, which, according to a condition test, may
longdesc or may not appear in the generated document. One of the most
longdesc common forms of conditional content management is multilingual
longdesc ; but it can also include versioning, confidentiality levels,
longdesc and so on. The philosophy of this package is based on the
longdesc respective notions of condition field, condition property and
longdesc condition space. With this package, any substitutable form in a
longdesc source document is identified by a condition field and a
longdesc condition property. The condition field is a functional theme
longdesc that allows you to group together substitutable forms for the
longdesc same conditional management. The condition property is a
longdesc functional characterization specific to each substitutable form
longdesc of a single condition domain. The condition space is used to
longdesc designate the substitutable form(s) that must appear in the
longdesc generated document. A condition space is defined by specifying
longdesc a condition domain and a condition property to match with one
longdesc or more substitutable forms.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/conditext
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics cond-comp
catalogue-version 1.5

name confproc
shortdesc A set of tools for generating conference proceedings
longdesc The confproc collection comprises a class, a BibTeX style, and
longdesc some scripts for generating conference proceedings. It derives
longdesc from LaTeX scripts written for the DAFx-06 conference
longdesc proceedings, largely based on the pdfpages package for
longdesc including the proceedings papers and the hyperref package for
longdesc creating a proper table of contents, bookmarks and general
longdesc bibliography back-references. Confproc also uses many other
longdesc packages for fine tuning of the table of contents, bibliography
longdesc and index of authors. The added value of the class resides in
longdesc its time-saving aspects when designing conference proceedings.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/conferences/confproc
catalogue-license lppl1.2
catalogue-topics confproc
catalogue-version 0.8

name constants
shortdesc Automatic numbering of constants
longdesc The package provides a way to number constants in a
longdesc mathematical proof automatically, with a system for
longdesc labelling/referencing. In addition, several families of
longdesc constants (with different symbols) may be defined.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/constants
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics maths
catalogue-version 1.0

name conteq
