name context-vim
shortdesc Generate ConTeXt syntax highlighting code from vim
longdesc ConTeXt has excellent pretty printing capabilities for many
longdesc languages. The code for pretty printing is written in TeX, and
longdesc due to catcode juggling, such verbatim typesetting is perhaps
longdesc the trickiest part of TeX. This makes it difficult for a normal
longdesc user to define syntax highlighting rules for a new language.
longdesc This module takes the onus of defining syntax highlighting
longdesc rules away from the user and uses ViM editor to generate the
longdesc syntax highlighting. There is a helper 2context.vim script to
longdesc do the syntax parsing in ViM.
catalogue-also context-filter
catalogue-ctan /macros/context/contrib/context-vim
catalogue-license bsd
catalogue-topics context ext-code synt-hlt

