name countwords
shortdesc Exact word counts, stored in LaTeX counters, using Lua
longdesc This is a simple package for generating exact wordcounts in
longdesc LaTeX projects. It counts words, storing the value in a
longdesc standard LaTeX counter, which can then be printed in the normal
longdesc way. Word counting can be paused and resumed, so you can skip
longdesc certain environments like mathematics, and multiple word counts
longdesc can happen in parallel (you could keep separate global and
longdesc per-chapter counts, for example). The word counting engine
longdesc itself is pulled from https://gist.github.com/phi-gamma/2622252
longdesc .
