name dashbox
shortdesc Draw dashed boxes
longdesc The package can draw boxes that perform like \framebox or
longdesc \fbox, but use dashed lines. The package can also draw (an
longdesc illusion of) vertical stacks of boxes.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/dashbox
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics boxing tagged-pdf-incompatible
catalogue-version 1.14

name dashrule
shortdesc Draw dashed rules
longdesc The dashrule package makes it easy to draw a huge variety of
longdesc dashed rules (i.e., lines) in LaTeX. dashrule provides a
longdesc command, \hdashrule, which is a cross between LaTeX's \rule and
longdesc PostScript's setdash command. \hdashrule draws horizontally
longdesc dashed rules using the same syntax as \rule, but with an
longdesc additional, setdash-like parameter that specifies the pattern
longdesc of dash segments and the space between those segments. Because
longdesc dashrule's rules are constructed internally using \rule (as
longdesc opposed to, e.g., PostScript \specials) they are fully
longdesc compatible with every LaTeX back-end processor.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/dashrule
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics line-patt tagged-pdf-partially
catalogue-version 1.3

name dashrulex
shortdesc Draw dashed rules
longdesc This package provides a flexible solution for drawing dashed
longdesc rules in the body. It currently provides two commands,
longdesc \hdashrule and \hanyrule. It is written in LaTeX3 and can be
longdesc used as an alternative to the dashrule package.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/texno3/dashrulex
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/dashrulex
catalogue-license cc-by-4
catalogue-topics line-patt rule
catalogue-version 1.02d

name dashundergaps
shortdesc Produce gaps that are underlined, dotted or dashed
longdesc The package provides commands (\underline, \dotuline and
longdesc \dashuline) each of which underlines its argument with one of
longdesc the styles the package is capable of. A phantom mode is
longdesc provided, where the underline (of whatever form) can serve for
longdesc a fill-in block for student evaluation sheets.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/FrankMittelbach/fmitex-dashundergaps
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/dashundergaps
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics line-patt tagged-pdf-incompatible underline
catalogue-version 2.0h

name data-driven-visualization
shortdesc CSV-driven concentric arc charts with configurable stages and titles
longdesc The ddv package wraps wheelchart and datatool to draw
longdesc concentric arc charts from CSV data. It supports category
longdesc filtering, numeric and multi-column sorting, per-row colors,
longdesc RGB colors, gradients, and configurable stage labels, titles,
longdesc typography, and wheelchart options. The manual contains
longdesc fourteen worked examples with source listings beside their
longdesc rendered results. The package and its documentation are tested
longdesc with LuaLaTeX; no shell escape or Python is required to use the
longdesc package or build the documentation.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://codeberg.org/lukascbossert/data-driven-visualization/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://codeberg.org/lukascbossert/data-driven-visualization
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/data-driven-visualization
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics csv-support data-disp graphics-plot
catalogue-version 1.0.0

name dataref
shortdesc Manage references to experimental data
longdesc The package provides a mechanism that maintains a fixed
longdesc symbolic reference to numerical results; such results may vary
longdesc as the project proceeds (and hence the project report
longdesc develops).
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/stettberger/dataref
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/dataref
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics data-manip label-ref
catalogue-version 0.7

name datatool
shortdesc Tools to load and manipulate data
longdesc The tools comprise the packages: datatool-base.sty: the
longdesc underlying base package used by all the other packages in this
longdesc bundle; datatool.sty: databases may be created using LaTeX
longdesc commands or by importing external files; they may be sorted
longdesc numerically or alphabetically; repetitive operations (such as
longdesc mail merging) may be performed on each row of a database,
longdesc subject to conditions to exclude particular rows; commands are
longdesc provided to examine database elements, and to convert formats
longdesc (for example, to convert a numeric element to a format
longdesc compatible with l3fp or the fp package; datapie.sty: a database
longdesc may be represented as a pie chart; flexible options allow
longdesc colouring of the chart, and annotation hooks are available;
longdesc dataplot.sty: a database may be represented as a 2-dimensional
longdesc scatter or line plot; flexible options control of the plot's
longdesc overall appearance, and of legends and other extra information;
longdesc databar.sty: a database may be represented as a bar chart;
longdesc overall appearance, colouring and annotation are controllable;
longdesc datagidx.sty: provides a way of indexing or creating
longdesc glossaries/lists of abbreviations that uses TeX to do the
longdesc sorting and collating instead of using an external indexing
longdesc application, such as xindy or makeindex (although you may
longdesc prefer \printnoidxglossary now provided by the glossaries
longdesc package); databib.sty: a bibliography may be loaded into a
longdesc datatool database, and manipulated there before being printed
longdesc (this permits a LaTeX-based route to printing bibliographies in
longdesc formats for which no BibTeX style is available, although
longdesc biblatex is now the better route); and person.sty: provides
longdesc support for displaying a person's name and pronoun in a
longdesc document, thus avoiding cumbersome use of he/she, etc. The
longdesc drawing packages make use of PGF/TikZ for their output.
longdesc Localisation support needs to be installed separately. See
longdesc datatool-regions and datatool-english. The bundle supersedes
longdesc and replaces the author's csvtools bundle.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://www.dickimaw-books.com/bugtracker.php?category=datatool
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/datatool
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics data-disp data-import data-manip
catalogue-version 3.4.5

name datatool-english
shortdesc English language support for datatool.sty v3.0+
longdesc The datatool-english bundle provides English language support
longdesc for the datatool package (v3.0+). The *.ldf files should all be
longdesc placed somewhere on TeX's path. These files don't require any
longdesc explicit loading. They will automatically be input by
longdesc datatool-base.sty (or relevant supplementary package) if they
longdesc are found and required by the tracklang localisation settings.
longdesc See the datatool v3.0+ and tracklang user manuals for further
longdesc details. The English files provide encoding support for UTF-8
longdesc and ISO-8859-1 (Latin 1). Any other encoding will be treated as
longdesc US-ASCII. This bundle also includes limited support for Old
longdesc English (Anglo-Saxon) mainly to provide an example for a
longdesc language that has multiple scripts (in this case, Latin and
longdesc Runic) or for a language that has an extended Latin or
longdesc non-Latin script. The language codes are ang-Latn for
longdesc Anglo-Saxon Latin Script and ang-Runr for Anglo-Saxon Runic
longdesc Script. There's only support for UTF-8 with the Anglo-Saxon
longdesc files.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/nlct/datatool-english/issues
catalogue-contact-home https://github.com/nlct/datatool-english
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/nlct/datatool-english
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/datatool-english
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics data-disp data-import data-manip
catalogue-version 1.1

name datatool-regions
shortdesc Region (numeric) support for datatool v3.0+
longdesc The datatool-regions bundle provides the language-independent
longdesc region ldf files for the datatool package (v3.0+). The *.ldf
longdesc files should all be placed on TeX's path. These files don't
longdesc require any explicit loading. They will automatically be input
longdesc by datatool-base.sty (or relevant supplementary package) if
longdesc they are found and required by the tracklang localisation
longdesc settings. See the datatool v3.0+ and tracklang user manuals for
longdesc further details. The region files deal with defining the
longdesc currency symbol, and may additionally (if not dependent on the
longdesc language) set the number group and decimal characters, and
longdesc provide functions for parsing numeric dates and times. If a
longdesc pre-3.0 version of datatool is installed, these ldf files will
longdesc be ignored.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/nlct/datatool-regions/issues
catalogue-contact-home https://github.com/nlct/datatool-regions
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/nlct/datatool-regions
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/datatool-regions
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics data-disp data-import data-manip
catalogue-version 1.0

name datax
shortdesc Import individual data from script files
longdesc This LaTeX package uses pgfkeys to retrieve individual data
longdesc points generated in some script. Analogous to how one might
longdesc generate graphics in a script and import those graphics into a
longdesc LaTeX document.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/Datax-package/Datax.sty
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/datax
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics data-import
catalogue-version 1.2.0

name dateiliste
shortdesc Extensions of the \listfiles concept
longdesc The package provides a file list (similar to that offered by
longdesc \listfiles), neatly laid out as a table. The main document can
longdesc be included in the list, and a command is available for
longdesc providing RCS-maintained data for printing in the file list.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/dateiliste
catalogue-license lppl1.3b
catalogue-topics doc-mgmt
catalogue-version 0.6

name datemultical
shortdesc Named dates, calendar conversion, and date formatting for LaTeX
longdesc This package provides a unified interface for defining,
longdesc converting, and formatting named dates in multiple calendar
longdesc systems in LaTeX. It provides a built-in TeX backend supporting
longdesc the Gregorian, Solar Hijri, and Lunar Hijri calendars under
longdesc supported TeX engines, and an extended LuaLaTeX backend that
longdesc additionally interfaces with lua-calendrica to support a wide
longdesc range of historical, astronomical, and traditional calendar
longdesc systems. Dates can be stored under user-defined names,
longdesc converted between supported calendars, and retrieved through a
longdesc common field-based interface. The package provides predefined
longdesc date styles and customizable formatting patterns, including
longdesc calendar-specific month and weekday names, week information,
longdesc and leap-year, leap-month, and leap-day fields. Persian
longdesc localization and high-level Persian date and weekday wrappers
longdesc are also provided.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/gambi-shah/datemultical/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/gambi-shah/datemultical
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/datemultical
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics calendar date-time persian use-luatex
catalogue-version 0.1.0

name datenumber
shortdesc Convert a date into a number and vice versa
longdesc This package provides commands to convert a date into a number
longdesc and vice versa. Additionally there are commands for
longdesc incrementing and decrementing a date. Leap years and the
longdesc Gregorian calendar reform are considered.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/datenumber
catalogue-license lppl1.2
catalogue-topics date-time tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 0.03

name datestamp
