name decimal
shortdesc LaTeX package for the English raised decimal point
longdesc This LaTeX package should be used by people who need the
longdesc traditional English raised decimal point, instead of the
longdesc American-style period.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/decimal
catalogue-license lppl1
catalogue-topics typesetting

name decimalcomma
shortdesc Comma for decimal numbers
longdesc This small package offers a new definition of the comma , as an
longdesc active character. It ensures the correct spacing in
longdesc mathematical mode when using the comma either as a decimal
longdesc separator or as a list separator. With this package, the comma
longdesc behaves similarly to ncccomma, but the code is lighter, and
longdesc several compatibility issues have been fixed.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/decimalcomma
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics maths numbers tagged-pdf typesetting
catalogue-version 1.4

name decision-table
shortdesc An easy way to create Decision Model and Notation decision tables
longdesc The decision-table package allows for an easy way to generate
longdesc decision tables in the Decision Model and Notation (DMN)
longdesc format. This package ensures consistency in the tables (i.e.
longdesc fontsize), and is thus a better alternative to inserting tables
longdesc via images. The decision-table package adds the \dmntable
longdesc command, with which tables can be created. This command expands
longdesc into a tabular, so it can be used within a table or figure
longdesc environment. Furthermore, this allows labels and captions to be
longdesc added seamlessly. It is also possible to place multiple DMN
longdesc tables in one table/figure environment. The package relies on
longdesc nicematrix and l3keys2e.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://gitlab.com/Vadevesi/dmn-tex/-/work_items
catalogue-contact-repository https://gitlab.com/Vadevesi/dmn-tex/
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/decision-table
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics diagram planning table
catalogue-version 0.0.4

name decorule
shortdesc Decorative swelled rule using font character
longdesc The package implements a decorative swelled rule using only a
longdesc symbol from a font installed with all distributions of TeX, so
longdesc it works independently, without the need to install any
longdesc additional software or fonts. This is the packaged version of
longdesc the macro which was originally published in the Typographers'
longdesc Inn column in TUGboat 31:1 (2010).
catalogue-also swrule
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/decorule
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics decoration line-weight tagged-pdf-incompatible
catalogue-version 0.7

name defoldfonts
shortdesc Define old font commands
longdesc In 1994, with LaTeX2e, the old font commands \rm, \sf, \tt,
longdesc \bf, \it, \sl, and \sc became obsolete. This package defines
longdesc them, and also the deprecated KOMA-Script command \sfb.
catalogue-contact-repository https://codeberg.org/komascript/defoldfonts
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/defoldfonts
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics font-supp
catalogue-version 1.1

name dehyph
shortdesc German hyphenation patterns for traditional orthography
longdesc The package provides older hyphenation patterns for the German
longdesc language. Please note that by default only pdfLaTeX uses these
longdesc patterns (mainly for backwards compatibility). The older
longdesc packages ghyphen and gnhyph are now bundled together with
longdesc dehyph, and are no longer be updated. Both XeLaTeX and LuaLaTeX
longdesc use the current German hyphenation patterns taken from
longdesc Hyphenation patterns in UTF-8, and using the Experimental
longdesc hyphenation patterns for the German language package it is
longdesc possible to make pdfLaTeX use the new German patterns as well.
catalogue-alias ghyphen gnhyph
catalogue-ctan /language/hyphenation/dehyph
catalogue-license lppl1
catalogue-topics german hyphenation

name dehyph-exptl
shortdesc Experimental hyphenation patterns for the German language
longdesc The package provides experimental hyphenation patterns for the
longdesc German language, covering both traditional and reformed
longdesc orthography. The patterns can be used with packages Babel and
longdesc hyphsubst from the Oberdiek bundle. Dieses Paket enthalt
longdesc experimentelle Trennmuster fur die deutsche Sprache. Die
longdesc Trennmuster decken das in Deutschland, Osterreich und der
longdesc Schweiz gebrauchliche Standarddeutsch in der traditionellen und
longdesc reformierten Rechtschreibung ab und konnen mit den Paketen
longdesc Babel und hyphsubst aus dem Oberdiek-Bundel verwendet werden.
catalogue-contact-home https://wiki.dante.de/doku.php?id=trennmuster:trennmuster
catalogue-contact-repository https://repo.or.cz/w/wortliste.git
catalogue-contact-support mailto:trennmuster@dante.de
catalogue-ctan /language/hyphenation/dehyph-exptl
catalogue-license mit lppl1.3
catalogue-topics german hyphenation
catalogue-version 1.0

name dejavu
shortdesc LaTeX support for the DejaVu fonts
longdesc The package contains LaTeX support for the DejaVu fonts, which
longdesc are derived from the Vera fonts but contain more characters and
longdesc styles. The fonts are included in the original TrueType format,
longdesc and in converted Type 1 format. The (currently) supported
longdesc encodings are: OT1, T1, IL2, TS1, T2*, X2, QX, and LGR. The
longdesc package doesn't (currently) support mathematics. More encodings
longdesc and/or features are expected.
catalogue-ctan /fonts/dejavu
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics font font-cyrillic font-greek font-mono font-sans font-serif font-t1enc font-ttf font-type1 tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 2.34

name dejavu-otf
shortdesc Support for the ttf and otf DejaVu fonts
longdesc This package supports the free ttf-fonts from the DejaVu
longdesc project which are available from GitHub or already part of your
longdesc system (Windows/Linux/...), and the OpenType version of TeXGyre
longdesc Math, which is part of any TeX distribution. The following font
longdesc files are supported: DejaVuSans-BoldOblique.ttf
longdesc DejaVuSans-Bold.ttf DejaVuSansCondensed-BoldOblique.ttf
longdesc DejaVuSansCondensed-Bold.ttf DejaVuSansCondensed-Oblique.ttf
longdesc DejaVuSansCondensed.ttf DejaVuSans-ExtraLight.ttf
longdesc DejaVuSansMono-BoldOblique.ttf DejaVuSansMono-Bold.ttf
longdesc DejaVuSansMono-Oblique.ttf DejaVuSansMono.ttf
longdesc DejaVuSans-Oblique.ttf DejaVuSans.ttf
longdesc DejaVuSerif-BoldItalic.ttf DejaVuSerif-Bold.ttf
longdesc DejaVuSerifCondensed-BoldItalic.ttf
longdesc DejaVuSerifCondensed-Bold.ttf DejaVuSerifCondensed-Italic.ttf
longdesc DejaVuSerifCondensed.ttf DejaVuSerif-Italic.ttf DejaVuSerif.ttf
longdesc texgyredejavu-math.otf
catalogue-ctan /fonts/dejavu-otf
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics font-absent font-mono font-otf font-sans font-serif font-supp font-ttf tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 0.07

name delim
shortdesc Simplify typesetting mathematical delimiters
longdesc The package permits simpler control of delimiters without
longdesc excessive use of \big... commands (and the like).
