name dental-palmer
shortdesc Typeset Zsigmondy-Palmer dental notation with TikZ
longdesc The dental-palmer distribution provides the palmer LaTeX
longdesc package for typesetting Zsigmondy-Palmer dental notation using
longdesc TikZ. It provides the \Palmer command with a key-value
longdesc interface for alignment, spacing (gap-ratio), midline-bar
longdesc suppression (no-vert), and quadrant-order control (no-reverse),
longdesc plus \palmerset for document-wide defaults. It is intended for
longdesc dental professionals, educators, and researchers preparing
longdesc clinical and academic documents.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/yosukey/palmer-latex
catalogue-ctan /graphics/pgf/contrib/dental-palmer
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics diagram medical pgf-tikz
catalogue-version 2.0.0

name derivative
shortdesc Nice and easy derivatives
longdesc Typesetting derivatives and differentials in a consistent way
longdesc are clumsy and require care to ensure the preferred formatting.
longdesc Several packages have been developed for this purpose, each
longdesc with its own features and drawbacks, with the most ambitious
longdesc one being diffcoeff. While this package is comparable to
longdesc diffcoeff in terms of features, it takes a different approach.
longdesc One difference is this package provides more options to tweak
longdesc the format of the derivatives and differentials. However, the
longdesc automatic calculation of the total order isn't as developed as
longdesc the one in diffcoeff. This package makes it easy to write
longdesc derivatives and differentials consistently with its predefined
longdesc commands. It also provides a set of commands that can define
longdesc custom derivatives and differential operators. The options
longdesc follow a consistent naming scheme making them easy to use and
longdesc understand.
catalogue-also diffcoeff
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/sjelatex/derivative
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/derivative
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics maths tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 1.4

name detex
shortdesc Strip TeX from a source file
longdesc Detex is a program to remove TeX constructs from a text file.
longdesc It recognizes the \input command. The program assumes it is
longdesc dealing with LaTeX input if it sees the string \begin{document}
longdesc in the text. In this case, it also recognizes the \include and
longdesc \includeonly commands. The author now considers this program to
longdesc be retired and Piotr Kubowicz's OpenDetex as its successor.
catalogue-contact-home https://www.cs.purdue.edu/homes/trinkle/detex/
catalogue-license other-free
catalogue-topics obsolete plain-text

