shortdesc x86_64-linuxmusl files of diadia

name diagbox
shortdesc Table heads with diagonal lines
longdesc The package's principal command, \diagbox, takes two arguments
longdesc (texts for the slash-separated parts of the box), and an
longdesc optional argument with which the direction the slash will go,
longdesc the box dimensions, etc., may be controlled. The package also
longdesc provides \slashbox and \backslashbox commands for compatibility
longdesc with the slashbox package, which it supersedes. diagbox depends
longdesc on e-TeX as well as the packages array, calc, fp, keyval, and
longdesc pict2e.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/leo-liu/tex-pkg
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/diagbox
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics table tagged-pdf-incompatible
catalogue-version 2.4

name diagmac2
shortdesc Diagram macros, using pict2e
longdesc This is a development of the long-established diagmac package,
longdesc using pict2e so that the restrictions on line direction are
longdesc removed.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/diagmac2
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics diagram-comm graphics-in-tex
catalogue-version 2.1

name diagnose
shortdesc A diagnostic tool for a TeX installation
longdesc Provides macros to assist evaluation of the capabilities of a
longdesc TeX installation (i.e., what extensions it supports). An
longdesc example document that examines the installation is available.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/diagnose
catalogue-license gpl
catalogue-topics install-mgmt
catalogue-version 0.2

name dialogl
shortdesc Macros for constructing interactive LaTeX scripts
longdesc Gathers together a bunch of code and examples about how to
longdesc write macros to carry on a dialogue with the user.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/dialogl
catalogue-license lppl1
catalogue-topics macro-supp

name dice
shortdesc A font for die faces
longdesc A Metafont font that can produce die faces in 2D or with
longdesc various 3D effects.
catalogue-also epsdice
catalogue-ctan /fonts/dice
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics font font-mf graphics-use

name dichokey
shortdesc Construct dichotomous identification keys
longdesc The package can be used to construct dichotomous identification
longdesc keys (used especially in biology for species identification),
longdesc taking care of numbering and indentation of successive key
longdesc steps automatically. An example file is provided, which
longdesc demonstrates usage.
catalogue-also identkey
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/dichokey
catalogue-license pd
catalogue-topics biology

name dichromacy
shortdesc Simulation of color vision deficiency, using LuaLaTeX
longdesc Simulate color vision deficiencies, including protanopia,
longdesc deuteranopia, and tritanopia, in LuaLaTeX documents. This
longdesc package provides a few simple commands that allow you to
longdesc control both the type of color deficiency, and the severity of
longdesc the simulation.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/jolars/dichromacy
catalogue-ctan /macros/luatex/latex/dichromacy
catalogue-license mit
catalogue-topics accessible colour luatex
catalogue-version 0.3.0

name dickimaw
shortdesc Books and tutorials from the Dickimaw LaTeX Series
longdesc The package provides some of the books and tutorials that form
longdesc part of the Dickimaw LaTeX Series. Only the A4 PDF of each book
longdesc is detailed here. Other formats, such as HTML or screen
longdesc optimized PDF, are available from the package home page. Books
longdesc included are: LaTeX for Complete Novices: an introductory guide
longdesc to LaTeX. Using LaTeX to Write a PhD Thesis: a follow-on from
longdesc LaTeX for Complete Novices geared towards students who want to
longdesc use LaTeX to write their PhD thesis. Creating a LaTeX minimal
longdesc example: describes how to create a minimal example, which can
longdesc be used as a debugging aid when you encounter errors in your
longdesc LaTeX documents.
catalogue-contact-home https://www.dickimaw-books.com/latex/
catalogue-ctan /info/dickimaw
catalogue-license fdl
catalogue-topics doc-debug tut-latex

name dictsym
shortdesc Font and macros for dictionary symbols
longdesc This directory contains the DictSym Type1 font designed by
longdesc Georg Verweyen and all files required to use it with LaTeX on
longdesc the Unix or PC platforms. The font provides a number of symbols
longdesc commonly used in dictionaries. The accompanying macro package
longdesc makes the symbols accessible as LaTeX commands.
catalogue-contact-repository https://gitlab.com/kjhtex/dictsym
catalogue-ctan /fonts/dictsym
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics font font-symbol font-type1 linguistic tagged-pdf-partially

name didactic
shortdesc Tools for writing teaching material
longdesc This package provides macros and environments useful for
longdesc writing teaching material. It provides more semantic
longdesc environments on top of the standard definition, theorem, and
longdesc friends: for instance, exercise, activity and question. These
longdesc are suitably colour-coded when used with Beamer. They occur as
longdesc normal text in handouts produced by beamerarticle (same style
longdesc as definition usually has). It also provides macros for
longdesc typesetting code listings and output side by side. Finally, it
longdesc modifies the appearance of beamer (Berlin-based theme) and
longdesc memoir (Tufte style layout), if loaded. It is designed to be
longdesc used with beamer to produce slides and beamerarticle with
longdesc memoir to produce notes and handouts from the same source.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/dbosk/didactic/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/dbosk/didactic
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/didactic
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics presentation teaching
catalogue-version 1.7

name didec
shortdesc Fixed-point arithmetic with two decimal places
longdesc This package supports fixed-point arithmetic with two decimal
longdesc places (di-decimal) which is typical for financial transactions
longdesc in many currencies. The intended use case is (personal)
longdesc bookkeeping.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/T-F-S/didec/issues
catalogue-contact-home https://github.com/T-F-S/didec
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/T-F-S/didec.git
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/didec
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics arithmetic calculation invoice tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 1.2.1

name diffcoeff
shortdesc Write differential coefficients easily and consistently
longdesc This package allows the easy and consistent writing of
longdesc ordinary, partial and other derivatives of arbitrary (algebraic
longdesc or numeric) order. For mixed partial derivatives, the total
longdesc order of differentiation is calculated by the package. Optional
longdesc arguments allow specification of points of evaluation (ordinary
longdesc derivatives), or variables held constant (partial derivatives),
longdesc and the placement of the differentiand (numerator or appended).
longdesc The package is built on xtemplate and the configurability it
longdesc enables, extending to differentials (including simple line
longdesc elements) and jacobians.
catalogue-also derivative
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/diffcoeff
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics maths tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 5.6

name digestif
shortdesc Editor plugin for LaTeX, ConTeXt etc.
longdesc Digestif is a code analyzer, and a language server, for LaTeX,
longdesc plain TeX, ConTeXt and Texinfo. It provides context-sensitive
longdesc completion, documentation, code navigation, and related
longdesc functionality to any text editor that speaks the LSP protocol.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/astoff/digestif/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/astoff/digestif
catalogue-ctan /support/digestif
catalogue-license gpl3+ lppl1.3 fdl
catalogue-topics editor-extn use-lua use-luatex
catalogue-version 0.6

