name digiconfigs
shortdesc Writing configurations
longdesc In Stochastic Geometry and Digital Image Analysis some problems
longdesc can be solved in terms of so-called configurations. A
longdesc configuration is basically a square matrix of \circ and \bullet
longdesc symbols. This package provides a convenient and compact
longdesc mechanism for displaying these configurations.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/digiconfigs
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics diagram
catalogue-version 0.5

name dijkstra
shortdesc Dijkstra's shortest-path algorithm for LaTeX
longdesc This small package uses the Dijkstra algorithm for weighted
longdesc graphs,directed or not: the search table of the shortest path
longdesc can be displayed, the minimum distance between two vertices and
longdesc the corresponding path are stored in macros. This packages
longdesc depends on simplekv.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/dijkstra
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics automata maths tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 0.13

name dimnum
shortdesc Commands for dimensionless numbers
longdesc This package simplifies the calling of Dimensionless Numbers in
longdesc math or text mode.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/CptRolinho/dimnum
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/dimnum
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics abbrev chemistry numbers physics
catalogue-version 1.0.1

name din1505
shortdesc Bibliography styles for German texts
longdesc A set of bibliography styles that conformt to DIN 1505, and
longdesc match the original BibTeX standard set (plain, unsrt, alpha and
longdesc abbrv), together with a style natdin to work with natbib.
catalogue-also dinat
catalogue-ctan /biblio/bibtex/contrib/german/din1505
catalogue-license other-free
catalogue-topics bibtex-supp

name dinat
shortdesc Bibliography style for German texts
longdesc Bibliography style files intended for texts in german. They
longdesc draw up bibliographies in accordance with the german DIN 1505,
longdesc parts 2 and 3.
catalogue-also din1505
catalogue-ctan /biblio/bibtex/contrib/german/dinat
catalogue-license pd
catalogue-topics bibtex-supp
catalogue-version 2.5

name dinbrief
shortdesc German letter DIN style
longdesc Implements a document layout for writing letters according to
longdesc the rules of DIN (Deutsches Institut fur Normung, German
longdesc standardisation institute). A style file for LaTeX 2.09 (with
longdesc limited support of the features) is part of the package. Since
longdesc the letter layout is based on a German standard, the user guide
longdesc is written in German, but most macros have English names from
longdesc which the user can recognize what they are used for. In
longdesc addition there are example files showing how letters may be
longdesc created with the package. A graphical interface for use of the
longdesc dinbrief is provided in the dinbrief-GUI bundle.
catalogue-also akletter envlab formlett g-brief
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/dinbrief
catalogue-license lppl1.1
catalogue-topics class letter std-conform

name dingbat
shortdesc Two dingbat symbol fonts
longdesc The fonts (ark10 and dingbat) are specified in Metafont;
longdesc support macros are provided for use in LaTeX. An Adobe Type 1
longdesc version of the fonts is available in the niceframe fonts
longdesc bundle.
catalogue-ctan /fonts/dingbat
catalogue-license lppl1.2
catalogue-topics font font-mf font-symbol tagged-pdf-partially
catalogue-version 1.0

name directory
shortdesc An address book using BibTeX
longdesc A package for LaTeX and BibTeX that facilitates the
longdesc construction, maintenance and exploitation of an address
longdesc book-like database.
catalogue-contact-home https://geuz.org/directory
catalogue-ctan /biblio/bibtex/contrib/directory
catalogue-license lppl1
catalogue-topics addr-list
catalogue-version 1.20

name dirtree
shortdesc Display trees in the style of windows explorer
longdesc This package is designed to emulate the way windows explorer
longdesc displays directory and file trees, with the root at top left,
longdesc and each level of subtree displaying one step in to the right.
longdesc The macros work equally well with Plain TeX and with LaTeX.
catalogue-also dirtreex
catalogue-ctan /macros/generic/dirtree
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics tagged-pdf-incompatible tree
catalogue-version 0.32

name dirtreex
shortdesc Directory tree rendering for LaTeX with TikZ
longdesc This package provides a self-contained tool for rendering
longdesc directory trees in an optionally breakable, fully styleable
longdesc frame. Built directly on TikZ and zref, it works natively
longdesc without requiring tcolorbox, dirtree, shell escape, or external
longdesc scripts. Its main features include automatically tracked depth,
longdesc so that \dir and \file commands can be nested naturally;
longdesc breakable frames whose borders, background, and vertical
longdesc connection lines continue across page boundaries; extensive
longdesc customization with per-tree and per-entry settings for line
longdesc colors, line widths, and elbow radii; and CJK-friendly
longdesc operation with ctex and LuaTeX.
catalogue-also dirtree
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/CloudCauldron/dirtreex/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/CloudCauldron/dirtreex
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/dirtreex
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics pgf-tikz tree
catalogue-version 1.2

name dirtytalk
shortdesc A package to typeset quotations easier
longdesc The package provides a macro to typeset quotations, using the
longdesc command \say{stuff}. The quotation mark glyphs are inserted by
longdesc the macro; nested quotations are detected.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/dirtytalk
catalogue-license pd
catalogue-topics quote-marks
catalogue-version 1.0

name disser
shortdesc Class and templates for typesetting dissertations in Russian
longdesc Disser comprises a document class and set of templates for
longdesc typesetting dissertations in Russian. One of its primary
longdesc advantages is a simplicity of format specification for
longdesc titlepage, headers and elements of automatically generated
longdesc lists (table of contents, list of figures, etc). Bibliography
longdesc styles, that conform to the requirements of the Russian
longdesc standard GOST R 7.0.11-2011, are provided.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/disser
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics class dissertation
catalogue-version 1.5.0

name ditaa
shortdesc Use ditaa diagrams within LaTeX documents
longdesc With this package ditaa (DIagrams Through Ascii Art) diagrams
longdesc can be embedded directly into LaTeX files.
catalogue-contact-announce https://github.com/dakusui/latex-ditaa/wiki/Announcements
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/dakusui/latex-ditaa/issues
catalogue-contact-development https://github.com/dakusui/latex-ditaa/issues/1
catalogue-contact-home https://github.com/dakusui/latex-ditaa
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/dakusui/latex-ditaa.git
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/ditaa
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics diagram
catalogue-version 0.9

name dithesis
shortdesc A class for undergraduate theses at the University of Athens
longdesc The class conforms to the requirements of the Department of
longdesc Informatics and Telecommunications at the University of Athens
longdesc regarding the preparation of undergraduate theses, as of Sep 1,
longdesc 2011. The class is designed for use with XeLaTeX; by default
longdesc (on a Windows platform), the font Arial is used, but provision
longdesc is made for use under Linux (with a different sans-serif font).
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/dithesis
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics dissertation greek
catalogue-version 0.2

name dk-bib
shortdesc Danish variants of standard BibTeX styles
longdesc Dk-bib is a translation of the four standard BibTeX style files
longdesc (abbrv, alpha, plain and unsrt) and the apalike style file into
longdesc Danish. The files have been extended with URL, ISBN, ISSN,
longdesc annote and printing fields which can be enabled through a LaTeX
longdesc style file. Dk-bib also comes with a couple of Danish sorting
longdesc order files for BibTeX8.
catalogue-ctan /biblio/bibtex/contrib/dk-bib
catalogue-license other-free
catalogue-topics bibtex-supp danish
catalogue-version 0.6

name dlfltxb
shortdesc Macros related to Introduktion til LaTeX
longdesc The bundle contains various macros either used for creating the
longdesc author's book Introduktion til LaTeX (in Danish), or presented
longdesc in the book as code tips. The bundle comprises:
longdesc dlfltxbcodetips: various macros helpful in typesetting
longdesc mathematics; dlfltxbmarkup: provides macros used throughout,
longdesc for registering macro names, packages etc. in the text, in the
longdesc margin and in the index, all by using categorised keys (note, a
longdesc configuration file may be used; a sample is included in the
longdesc distribution); dlfltxbtocconfig: macros for the two tables of
longdesc contents that the book has; dlfltxbmisc: various macros for
longdesc typesetting LaTeX arguments, and the macro used in the
longdesc bibliography that can wrap a URL up into a BibTeX entry.
longdesc Interested parties may review the book itself on the web at the
longdesc author's institution (it is written in Danish).
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/dlfltxb
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics book-ex danish

name dlrg-templates
shortdesc Templates for the German Lifesaving Association (DLRG)
longdesc This bundle provides templates for members of the German
longdesc Lifesaving Association (DLRG). This includes the letter
longdesc template, presentations, specialist publications and press
longdesc releases. These templates are based on the current cooperative
longdesc design. They can be adapted to the local structure with simple
longdesc settings.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://gitlab.com/dlrg-fs/dlrg_latex/-/work_items
catalogue-contact-repository https://gitlab.com/dlrg-fs/dlrg_latex
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/dlrg-templates
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics doc-templ essay letter presentation std-conform
catalogue-version 1.1.0

name dnaseq
shortdesc Format DNA base sequences
longdesc Defines a means of specifying sequences of bases. The bases may
longdesc be numbered (per line) and you may specify that subsequences be
longdesc coloured. For a more vanilla-flavoured way of typesetting base
longdesc sequences, the user might consider the seqsplit package.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/dnaseq
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics molbio
catalogue-version 0.01

name dnp
shortdesc subfont numbers for DNP font encoding
longdesc part of the CJK package, ctan.org/pkg/cjk

name dnsrecord
shortdesc Typeset DNS records, zone files, propagation tables, and DNSSEC chains
longdesc A comprehensive LaTeX package for typesetting DNS (Domain Name
longdesc System) data in technical documents. Provides 22 color-coded
longdesc record type commands (A, AAAA, CNAME, MX, NS, TXT, SOA, PTR,
longdesc SRV, CAA, DNSKEY, DS, RRSIG, NSEC, NSEC3, TLSA, HTTPS, SVCB,
longdesc SPF, DKIM, DMARC), seven environments for zone file tables,
longdesc propagation status displays, DNSSEC chain-of-trust diagrams,
longdesc DNS health check reports, email authentication summaries,
longdesc latency comparisons, and provider tables. Includes utility
longdesc commands for formatting domains, IPs, TTLs with human-readable
longdesc conversion, DNS response codes, and query flags. Designed for
longdesc network engineers, system administrators, security researchers,
longdesc and computer science academics writing papers, theses, and
longdesc operational documentation.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/dnsrobot/latex-dnsrecord/issues
catalogue-contact-home https://dnsrobot.net
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/dnsrobot/latex-dnsrecord
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/dnsrecord
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics engineering
catalogue-version 1.0.0

name doc-pictex
shortdesc A summary list of PiCTeX documentation
longdesc A summary of available resources providing (or merely
longdesc discussing) documentation of PiCTeX.
catalogue-contact-support https://www.webdesign-bu.de/uwe_lueck/contact.html
catalogue-ctan /info/pictex/Doc-PiCTeX.txt
catalogue-license other-free
catalogue-topics doc-mgmt

name docbytex
shortdesc Creating documentation from source code
longdesc The package creates documentation from C source code, or other
longdesc programming languages.
catalogue-contact-home https://www.olsak.net/docbytex.html
catalogue-ctan /macros/generic/docbytex
catalogue-license other-free
catalogue-topics program-doc

name docext
shortdesc Extension for documenting LaTeX source files
longdesc This package is an extension for documenting LaTeX source
longdesc files. It provides an environment codedemo for typesetting the
longdesc code within a verbatim and a demo environment at the same time.
longdesc It fixes the errors of the doc package under the engines pTeX
longdesc and upTeX, and the classes book and report (or any class that
longdesc uses the titlepage environment in \maketitle).
catalogue-contact-development https://github.com/myhsia
catalogue-contact-home https://github.com/myhsia
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/myhsia/docext
catalogue-contact-support https://github.com/myhsia/docext/issues
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/docext
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics doc-supp
catalogue-version 0.2C

name doclicense
shortdesc Support for putting documents under a license
longdesc This package allows you to put your document under a license
longdesc and include a link to read about the license or include an icon
longdesc or image of the license. Currently, only Creative Commons is
longdesc supported, but this package is designed to handle all kinds of
longdesc licenses.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/ypid/latex-packages/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/ypid/latex-packages/tree/master/doclicense
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/doclicense
catalogue-license cc0 lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics licence-mgmt tagged-pdf-partially
catalogue-version 3.3.0

name docmfp
shortdesc Document non-LaTeX code
longdesc Extends the doc package to cater for documenting non-LaTeX
longdesc code, such as Metafont or MetaPost, or other programming
longdesc languages.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/LaTeX-Package-Repositories/herries-press
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/docmfp
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics doc-supp
catalogue-version 1.2d

name docmute
shortdesc Input files ignoring LaTeX preamble, etc.
longdesc Input or include stand-alone LaTeX documents, ignoring
longdesc everything but the material between \begin{document} and
longdesc \end{document}.
catalogue-also combine includex newclude standalone
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/docmute
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics subdocs tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 1.4

name docshots
shortdesc TeX samples next to their PDF snapshots
longdesc This package helps you render TeX examples from your DTX
longdesc documentation and then embed PDF snapshots into it, next to the
longdesc source TeX code.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/yegor256/docshots
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/docshots
catalogue-license mit
catalogue-topics doc-supp
catalogue-version 0.5.2

name docsurvey
shortdesc A survey of LaTeX documentation
longdesc A survey of programming-related documentation for LaTeX.
longdesc Included are references to printed and electronic books and
longdesc manuals, symbol lists, FAQs, the LaTeX source code, CTAN and
longdesc distributions, programming-related packages, users groups and
longdesc online communities, and information on creating packages and
longdesc documentation.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/bdtc/docsurvey
catalogue-ctan /info/docsurvey
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics ref-latex review-document tut-latex tut-latex-prg

name doctools
shortdesc Tools for the documentation of LaTeX code
longdesc The package provides a collection of tools for use either in an
longdesc ordinary LaTeX document, or within a .dtx file.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/doctools
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics doc-supp
catalogue-version 0.1

name documentation
shortdesc Support for documenting C, Java, and assembler code
longdesc The package provides a simple means of typesetting computer
longdesc programs such that the result is acceptable for inclusion in
longdesc reports, etc.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/documentation
catalogue-license lppl1.2
catalogue-topics listing
catalogue-version 0.1

name docutils
shortdesc Helper commands and element definitions for Docutils LaTeX output
longdesc The package is intended for use with LaTeX documents generated
longdesc from reStructuredText sources with Docutils. When generating
longdesc LaTeX documents, specify this package with the stylesheet
longdesc configuration option, e.g. rst2latex --stylesheet=docutils
longdesc exampledocument.txt
catalogue-contact-announce https://pypi.org/rss/project/docutils/releases.xml
catalogue-contact-bugs https://sourceforge.net/p/docutils/bugs/
