name dvicopy
shortdesc Copy DVI files while expanding VF (virtual font) references
longdesc DVIcopy is a utility program that allows one to convert a DVI
longdesc file that references composite fonts (VF) into an equivalent
longdesc DVI file that does not contain such references. It also serves
longdesc as a basis for writing DVI drivers (much like DVItype). The
longdesc ODVIcopy variant does the same job for Omega/Aleph's output,
longdesc modified to support their .ofm font format.
catalogue-alias odvicopy
