name fink
shortdesc The LaTeX2e File Name Keeper
longdesc This package looks over your shoulder and keeps track of files
longdesc \input'ed (the LaTeX way) or \include'ed in your document. You
longdesc then have permanent access to the name of the file currently
longdesc being processed through the macro \finkfile. FiNK also comes
longdesc with support for AUC-TeX. As of version 2.2.1, FiNK has been
longdesc deprecated and is not maintained anymore. People interested in
longdesc FiNK's functionality are invited to use a package named
longdesc currfile instead.
catalogue-also currfile
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/fink
catalogue-license lppl1.1
catalogue-topics doc-tool
catalogue-version 2.2.1

name finstrut
shortdesc Adjust behaviour of the ends of footnotes
longdesc The LaTeX internal command \@finalstrut is used automatically
longdesc used at the end of footnote texts to insert a strut to avoid
longdesc mis-spacing of multiple footnotes. Unfortunately the command
longdesc can cause a blank line at the end of a footnote. The package
longdesc provides a solution to this problem.
