name fontaxes
shortdesc Additional font selection axes for LaTeX
longdesc The package adds several new font axes on top of LaTeX's New
longdesc Font Selection Scheme. In particular, it splits the shape axis
longdesc into a primary and a secondary shape axis, and it adds three
longdesc new axes to deal with the different figure versions offered by
longdesc many professional fonts. This package has nowadays been
longdesc deprecated in favour of the figureversions package.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/ummels/fontaxes/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/ummels/fontaxes
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/fontaxes
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics font-use obsolete tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 2.0.2

name fontbook
shortdesc Generate a font book
longdesc The package provides a means of producing a book of font
longdesc samples (for evaluation, etc.).
catalogue-ctan /macros/xetex/latex/fontbook
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics font-devel
catalogue-version 0.2

name fontch
shortdesc Changing fonts, sizes and encodings in Plain TeX
longdesc The fontch macros allow the user to change font size and family
longdesc anywhere in a plain TeX document. Sizes of 8, 10, 12, 14, 20
longdesc and 24 points are available. A sans serif family (\sf) is
longdesc defined in addition to the families already defined in plain
longdesc TeX. Optional support for Latin Modern T1 and TS1 fonts is
longdesc given. There are macros for non-latin1 letters and for most TS1
longdesc symbols. Math mode always uses CM fonts. A command for
longdesc producing doubled-spaced documents is also provided. The
longdesc present version of the package is designed to deal with the
longdesc latest release of the Latin Modern fonts version 1.106.
longdesc Unfortunately, it can no longer support earlier versions of the
longdesc fonts, so an obsolete version of the package is retained for
longdesc users who don't yet have access to the latest version of the
longdesc fonts.
catalogue-also font-selection ofs plnfss
catalogue-ctan /macros/plain/contrib/fontch
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics font-sel plain-ext
catalogue-version 2.2

name fontinst
shortdesc Help with installing fonts for TeX and LaTeX
longdesc TeX macros for converting Adobe Font Metric files to TeX metric
longdesc and virtual font format. Fontinst helps mainly with the number
longdesc crunching and shovelling parts of font installation. This means
longdesc in practice that it creates a number of files which give the
longdesc TeX metrics (and related information) for a font family that
longdesc (La)TeX needs to do any typesetting in these fonts. Fontinst
longdesc furthermore makes it easy to create fonts containing glyphs
longdesc from more than one base font, taking advantage of (e.g.) expert
longdesc font sets. Fontinst cannot examine files to see if they contain
longdesc any useful information, nor automatically search for files or
longdesc work with binary file formats; those tasks must normally be
longdesc done manually or with the help of some other tool, such as the
longdesc pltotf and vptovf programs.
catalogue-ctan /fonts/utilities/fontinst
catalogue-license lppl1.1
catalogue-topics font-cvt
catalogue-version 1.933

