name fontspec
shortdesc Advanced font selection in XeLaTeX and LuaLaTeX
longdesc Fontspec is a package for XeLaTeX and LuaLaTeX. It provides an
longdesc automatic and unified interface to feature-rich AAT and
longdesc OpenType fonts through the NFSS in LaTeX running on XeTeX or
longdesc LuaTeX engines. The package requires the l3kernel and xparse
longdesc bundles from the LaTeX3 development team.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/latex3/fontspec/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/latex3/fontspec/
catalogue-ctan /macros/unicodetex/latex/fontspec
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics font-sel luatex tagged-pdf xetex
catalogue-version 2.9h

name fonttable
shortdesc Print font tables from a LaTeX document
longdesc This is a package version of nfssfont.tex (part of the LaTeX
longdesc distribution); it enables you to print a table of the
longdesc characters of a font and/or some text (for demonstration or
longdesc testing purposes), from within a document. (Packages such as
longdesc testfont and nfssfont.tex provide these facilities, but they
longdesc run as interactive programs: the user is expected to type
longdesc details of what is needed.) Note that the package mftinc also
longdesc has a \fonttable function; the documentation explains how avoid
longdesc a clash with that package.
catalogue-also unicodefonttable
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/LaTeX-Package-Repositories/herries-press/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/LaTeX-Package-Repositories/herries-press
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/fonttable
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics font-devel font-index tagged-pdf-incompatible
catalogue-version 1.6e

name fontware
catalogue vfware
shortdesc Tools for virtual font metrics
longdesc Virtual font metrics are usually created in a textual form, the
longdesc Virtual Property List, but programs that use them need to use
longdesc binary files (the Virtual Font and the TeX Font Metric). The
longdesc present two programs translate between the two forms: vptovf
longdesc takes a VPL file and generates a VF file and a TFM file vftovp
longdesc takes a VF file and a TFM file and generates a VPL file The
longdesc programs are to be found in every distribution of TeX.
catalogue-alias vftovp vptovf
catalogue-contact-bugs https://lists.tug.org/tex-k
catalogue-contact-repository https://tug.org/svn/texlive/trunk/Build/source/texk/web2c/
catalogue-contact-support https://lists.tug.org/tex-k
catalogue-ctan /systems/knuth/dist/etc
catalogue-license knuth
catalogue-topics collection debug-supp font-util

