name fragoli
shortdesc Macros for constructing complex semantic derivations
longdesc The primary goal of this package is to provide a minimal and
longdesc user-friendly syntax for constructing large and complex
longdesc semantic derivations, following the specific notational style
longdesc used at Goethe University Frankfurt. It includes a
longdesc comprehensive set of commands for text formatting and various
longdesc types of bracketing, ensuring a consistent style - particularly
longdesc when distinguishing between meta-language and object-language
longdesc within a single derivation or formula. The formula style is
longdesc loosely based on the accompanying material to an introductory
longdesc course to linguistic semantics by Prof. Dr. Thomas Ede
longdesc Zimmermann. The package brings together and refines a
longdesc collection of LaTeX commands and concepts developed over the
longdesc years within the Department of Linguistics at the
longdesc Goethe-Universitat at Frankfurt am Main. In the process of
longdesc preparing research papers, assignments, and examinations,
longdesc numerous custom LaTeX headers and commands were shared within
longdesc the department - some mutually compatible, others not. Note:
longdesc The package name is an abbreviation of Frankfurt Goethe
longdesc Linguistic.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/fragoli/FraGoLi/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/fragoli/FraGoLi
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/fragoli
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics linguistic
catalogue-version 1.3.4

name frame
shortdesc Framed boxes for Plain TeX
longdesc A jiffy file (taken from fancybox) for placing a frame around a
longdesc box of text. The macros also provide for typesetting an empty
longdesc box of given dimensions.
catalogue-also boxit
catalogue-ctan /macros/generic/frame
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics boxing decoration
catalogue-version 1.0

name framed
shortdesc Breakable framed and shaded boxes
longdesc The package creates three environments: framed, which puts an
longdesc ordinary frame box around the region, shaded, which shades the
longdesc region, and leftbar, which places a line at the left side. The
longdesc environments allow a break at their start (the \FrameCommand
longdesc enables creation of a title that is attached to the
longdesc environment); breaks are also allowed in the course of the
longdesc framed/shaded matter. There is also a command \MakeFramed to
longdesc make your own framed-style environments.
catalogue-also mdframed
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/framed
catalogue-license other-free
catalogue-topics box-breaking boxing decoration tagged-pdf-incompatible
catalogue-version 0.96

name framedsyntax
shortdesc Typeset the syntax of commands and environments within coloured boxes
longdesc When creating new packages or user guides, it is necessary to
longdesc describe their syntax. This package helps by creating coloured
