name freemath
shortdesc LaTeX maths without backslashes
longdesc This package allows for the omission of backslashes from most
longdesc math mode commands. Specifically, any consecutive string of at
longdesc least two (Latin) letters appearing in math mode will
longdesc automatically be turned into the control sequence with the same
longdesc name, if it exists. The package provides the \freemathon and
longdesc \freemathoff commands which respectively activate and
longdesc deactivate this behaviour. It is disabled by default upon
longdesc loading. Regular commands initiated by a backslash may of
longdesc course still be used when freemath is active, and can
longdesc furthermore be freely mixed with backslash-free commands.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/plante3/freemath
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/freemath
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
