name fxpicture
shortdesc Dashed, dotted and dash-dotted line styles for the picture environment
longdesc fxpicture adds dashed, dotted and dash-dotted lines to LaTeX's
longdesc picture environment. It builds on pict2e (the more modern
longdesc version of picture), and gives it two declarations, \linestyle
longdesc and \dashpattern. Like \linethickness, they last until the end
longdesc of the group, and they apply to every line that pict2e strokes,
longdesc from \line and \vector to \oval, \circle and Bezier curves. The
longdesc same features are implement into the picture editor on
longdesc fxEditor. e.g. \setlength{\unitlength}{1mm}
longdesc \begin{picture}(40,12) \linestyle{dotted}
longdesc \put(0,10){\line(1,0){40}} \thicklines
longdesc \put(0,5){\line(1,0){40}} \linethickness{1.2pt}
longdesc \put(0,0){\line(1,0){40}} \end{picture}
catalogue-also pict2e
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/fxpicture
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
