name gfsbodoni
shortdesc A Greek and Latin font based on Bodoni
longdesc Bodoni's Greek fonts in the 18th century broke, for the first
longdesc time, with the Byzantine cursive tradition of Greek fonts. GFS
longdesc Bodoni resurrects his work for general use. The font family
longdesc supports both Greek and Latin letters. LaTeX support of the
longdesc fonts is provided, offering OT1, T1 and LGR encodings. The
longdesc fonts themselves are provided in Adobe Type 1 and OpenType
longdesc formats.
catalogue-contact-home https://myria.math.aegean.gr/labs/dt/
catalogue-ctan /fonts/greek/gfs/gfsbodoni
catalogue-license ofl
catalogue-topics font font-greek font-otf font-type1 tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 1.01

name gfscomplutum
shortdesc A Greek font with a long history
longdesc GFS Complutum derives, via a long development, from a
longdesc minuscule-only font cut in the 16th century. An unsatisfactory
longdesc set of majuscules were added in the early 20th century, but its
longdesc author died before he could complete the revival of the font.
longdesc The Greek Font Society has released this version, which has a
longdesc new set of majuscules.
catalogue-contact-home https://myria.math.aegean.gr/labs/dt/
catalogue-ctan /fonts/greek/gfs/gfscomplutum
catalogue-license ofl
catalogue-topics font font-greek font-otf font-type1 tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 1.0

name gfsdidot
shortdesc A Greek font based on Didot's work
longdesc The design of Didot's 1805 Greek typeface was influenced by the
longdesc neoclassical ideals of the late 18th century. The font was
longdesc brought to Greece at the time of the 1821 Greek Revolution, by
longdesc Didot's son, and was very widely used. The present version is
longdesc provided by the Greek Font Society. The font supports the Greek
longdesc alphabet, and is accompanied by a matching Latin alphabet based
longdesc on Zapf's Palatino. LaTeX support is provided, using the OT1,
longdesc T1, TS1, and LGR encodings.
catalogue-contact-home https://myria.math.aegean.gr/labs/dt/
catalogue-ctan /fonts/greek/gfs/gfsdidot
catalogue-license other-free
catalogue-topics font font-body font-greek font-multilingual font-otf font-serif font-t1enc font-type1 tagged-pdf

name gfsdidotclassic
shortdesc The classic version of GFSDidot
longdesc The classic version of GFSDidot provided for Unicode TeX
longdesc engines.
catalogue-ctan /fonts/greek/gfs/gfsdidotclassic
catalogue-license ofl
catalogue-topics font font-body font-greek font-otf
catalogue-version 001.001

name gfsneohellenic
shortdesc A font in the Neo-Hellenic style
longdesc The NeoHellenic style evolved in academic circles in the 19th
longdesc and 20th century; the present font follows a cut commissioned
longdesc from Monotype in 1927. The present version was provided by the
longdesc Greek Font Society. The font supports both Greek and Latin
longdesc characters, and has been adjusted to work well with the
longdesc cmbright fonts for mathematics support. LaTeX support of the
longdesc fonts is provided, offering OT1, T1 and LGR encodings.
catalogue-contact-home https://myria.math.aegean.gr/labs/dt/
catalogue-ctan /fonts/greek/gfs/gfsneohellenic
catalogue-license other-free
catalogue-topics font font-greek font-otf tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 1.02

name gfsneohellenicmath
shortdesc A math font in the Neo-Hellenic style
longdesc The GFSNeohellenic font, a historic font first designed by
longdesc Victor Scholderer, and digitized by George Matthiopoulos of the
longdesc Greek Font Society (GFS), now has native support for
longdesc Mathematics. The project was commissioned to GFS by the
longdesc Department of Mathematics of the University of the Aegean,
longdesc Samos, Greece. The Math Table was constructed by the
longdesc Mathematics Professor A. Tsolomitis. A useful application is in
longdesc beamer documents since this is a Sans Math font. The
longdesc GFSNeohellenic fontfamily supports many languages (including
longdesc Greek), and it is distributed (both text and math) under the
longdesc OFL license.
catalogue-ctan /fonts/gfsneohellenicmath
catalogue-license ofl
catalogue-topics font font-greek font-maths font-otf font-type1 maths tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 1.02

name gfsporson
shortdesc A Greek font, originally from Porson
longdesc Porson is an elegant Greek font, originally cut at the turn of
longdesc the 19th Century in England. The present version has been
longdesc provided by the Greek Font Society. The font supports the Greek
longdesc alphabet only. LaTeX support is provided, using the LGR
longdesc encoding.
catalogue-contact-home https://myria.math.aegean.gr/labs/dt/
catalogue-ctan /fonts/greek/gfs/gfsporson
catalogue-license other-free
catalogue-topics font font-greek font-otf font-type1 tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 1.01

name gfssolomos
shortdesc A Greek-alphabet font
longdesc Solomos is a font which traces its descent from a
longdesc calligraphically-inspired font of the mid-19th century. LaTeX
longdesc support, for use with the LGR encoding only, is provided.
catalogue-contact-home https://myria.math.aegean.gr/labs/dt/
catalogue-ctan /fonts/greek/gfs/gfssolomos
catalogue-license ofl
catalogue-topics font font-greek font-otf font-type1 tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 1.0

name ghab
shortdesc Typeset ghab boxes in LaTeX
longdesc The package defines a command \darghab that will typeset its
longdesc argument in a box with a decorated frame. The width of the box
longdesc may be set using an optional argument.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/bidi-tex/ghab/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/bidi-tex/ghab
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/ghab
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics boxing decoration
catalogue-version 0.5

name ghsystem
shortdesc Globally harmonised system of chemical (etc) naming
longdesc The package provides the means to typeset all the hazard and
longdesc precautionary statements and pictograms in a straightforward
longdesc way. The statements are taken from EU regulation 1272/2008.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/cgnieder/ghsystem/
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/ghsystem
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics chemistry tagged-pdf-partially
