name hexdumptikz
shortdesc Display hexdumps in LaTeX with the help of TikZ
longdesc Showing hexdumps is a common task in some fields. The most
longdesc rudimentary form doing this in LaTeX is using a simple listings
longdesc package. But often just showing the data is not enough.
longdesc Instead, it needs to be annotated and explained. This package
longdesc offers exactly this feature by drawing each byte as a TikZ
longdesc node. Note that this package explicitly aims to also support
longdesc hexdumps with larger addresses (thinking of 64-bit
longdesc addresses/offsets) here.
