name integramme
shortdesc Typeset staircase logic-grid puzzles (or zebra puzzles)
longdesc This is a LaTeX package for typesetting staircase-style
longdesc logic-grid puzzles (or zebra puzzles - integrammes or
longdesc logigrammes in French). Authors declare categories, item labels
longdesc and clues; the package generates the staircase grid
longdesc automatically. It supports blank puzzles, partially filled
longdesc grids for worked solutions, and complete solution grids derived
longdesc from keyed solution rows. A built-in Einstein-riddle preset is
longdesc included in English and French.
catalogue-ctan /graphics/pgf/contrib/integramme
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics graphics pgf-tikz puzzle
catalogue-version 0.9.0

name inter
shortdesc The inter font face with support for LaTeX, XeLaTeX, and LuaLaTeX
longdesc This package provides LaTeX, pdfLaTeX, XeLaTeX and LuaLaTeX
longdesc support for the Inter Sans family of fonts (version 3.015),
longdesc designed by Rasmus Andersson. Inter is a typeface specially
longdesc designed for user interfaces with focus on high legibility of
longdesc small-to-medium sized text on computer screens. The family
longdesc features a tall x-height to aid in readability of mixed-case
longdesc and lower-case text.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/ccebinger/CTAN_Inter
catalogue-ctan /fonts/inter
catalogue-license ofl lppl
catalogue-topics font font-body font-otf font-proportional font-sans font-supp font-t1enc font-type1 tagged-pdf

name interactiveworkbook
shortdesc LaTeX-based interactive PDF on the Web
longdesc The package interactiveworkbook gives the user the ability to
longdesc write LaTeX documents which, ultimately, create interactive
longdesc question-and-answer Portable Document Format (PDF) tutorials
longdesc meant to be used by Internet students and that, in particular,
longdesc freely use mathematical notation.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/interactiveworkbook
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics tutorial

name interchar
shortdesc Managing character class schemes in XeTeX
longdesc The package manages character class schemes of XeTeX. Using
longdesc this package, you may switch among different character class
longdesc schemes. Migration commands are provided for make packages
longdesc using this mechanism compatible with each others.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/zohooo/interchar
catalogue-ctan /macros/xetex/latex/interchar
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics tagged-pdf-unsupported xetex
catalogue-version 0.2

name interfaces
shortdesc Set parameters for other packages, conveniently
longdesc The package provides a small number of convenient macros that
longdesc access features in other frequently-used packages, or provide
longdesc interfaces to other useful facilities such as the pdfTeX
longdesc \pdfelapsedtime primitive. Most of these macros use pgfkeys to
longdesc provide a key-value syntax. The package also uses the package
longdesc scrlfile from the Koma-Script bundle (for controlled loading of
longdesc other files) and etoolbox. The package is bundled with
longdesc sub-packages containing actual interfaces: by default, the
longdesc package loads all available sub-packages, but techniques are
longdesc provided for the user to select no more than the interfaces
longdesc needed for a job.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/interfaces
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics package-supp
catalogue-version 3.1

name interlinear
shortdesc A package for creating interlinear glossed texts with customizable formatting
longdesc The interlinear package facilitates the creation of interlinear
longdesc glossed texts, commonly used in linguistic examples. It is
longdesc based on the gb4e package and builds upon its functionality to
longdesc provide enhanced features. It offers extensive customization
longdesc options, allowing users to control font styles, formatting, and
longdesc layout. With predefined styles and margin note customization,
longdesc interlinear provides a flexible solution for presenting
longdesc linguistic data.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/interlinear
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics linguistic
catalogue-version 1.0

name interpreter
shortdesc Translate input files on the fly
longdesc The package preprocesses input files to a Lua(La)TeX run, on
longdesc the fly. The user defines Lua regular expressions to search for
longdesc patterns and modify input lines (or entire paragraphs)
longdesc accordingly, before TeX reads the material. In this way,
longdesc documents may be prepared in a non-TeX language (e.g., some
longdesc lightweight markup language) and turned into proper TeX for
longdesc processing. The source of the documentation is typed in such a
longdesc lightweight language and is thus easily readable in a text
longdesc editor (the PDF file is also available, of course); the
longdesc transformation to TeX syntax via Interpreter's functions is
longdesc explained in the documentation itself. Interpreter is
longdesc implemented using the author's gates (Lua version), and works
longdesc for plain TeX and LaTeX, but not ConTeXt.
catalogue-ctan /macros/luatex/generic/interpreter
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics foreign-import luatex macro-supp
catalogue-version 1.2

name interval
shortdesc Format mathematical intervals, ensuring proper spacing
longdesc When typing an open interval as $]a,b[$, a closing bracket is
longdesc being used in place of an opening fence and vice versa. This
longdesc leads to the wrong spacing in, say, $]-a,b[$ or $A\in]a,b[=B$.
longdesc The package attempts to solve this using: \interval{a}{b} ->
longdesc [a,b] \interval[open]{a}{b} -> ]a,b[ \interval[open left]{a}{b}
longdesc -> ]a,b] The package also supports fence scaling and ensures
longdesc that the enclosing fences will end up having the proper closing
longdesc and opening types. TeX maths does not do this job properly. The
longdesc package depends on pgfkeys.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/interval
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics maths paren-mgmt tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 0.4

name intexgral
shortdesc A LaTeX package for typesetting integrals
longdesc Typesetting integrals, although common in LaTeX, is not
longdesc particularly practical. The way in which the different parts
longdesc are managed often generates unreadable source code, making
longdesc modifications laborious. The package therefore follows a simple
longdesc philosophy: focus on the essential element of an integral, the
longdesc integrand. Everything else (limits, differentials, symbols) can
longdesc be modified using keys. These keys are designed to allow you to
longdesc easily and quickly change the style of an integral.
longdesc Additionally, the package provides various auxiliary macros to
longdesc support some keys which can have lengthy inputs.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/TeXackers/intexgral/tree/master
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/intexgral
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics maths
catalogue-version 4.3.1

name intopdf
shortdesc Embed non-PDF files into PDF with hyperlink
longdesc The package allows to embed non-PDF files (e.g., BibTeX) into
longdesc PDF with a hyperlink.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/zauguin/intopdf
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/intopdf
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics hyper pdf-feat tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 0.4.1

name intro-scientific
shortdesc Introducing scientific/mathematical documents using LaTeX
longdesc Writing Scientific Documents Using LaTeX is an article
longdesc introducing the use of LaTeX in typesetting scientific
longdesc documents. It covers the basics of creating a new LaTeX
longdesc document, special typesetting considerations, mathematical
longdesc typesetting and graphics. It also touches on bibliographic data
longdesc and BibTeX.
catalogue-ctan /info/intro-scientific
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics tut-latex
catalogue-version 5th edition

name inversepath
shortdesc Calculate inverse file paths
longdesc The package calculates inverse relative paths. Such things may
longdesc be useful, for example, when writing an auxiliary file to a
longdesc different directory.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/inversepath
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics macro-supp tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 0.2

name invoice
shortdesc Generate invoices
longdesc The package may be used for generating invoices. The package
longdesc can deal with invisible expense items and deductions; output
longdesc may be presented in any of 10 different languages. A
longdesc long-standing bug has been removed. Numbers now can show the
longdesc comma as decimal separator. The package depends on the fp, calc
longdesc and siunitx for its calculations.
catalogue-also facture invoice2
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/invoice
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics invoice

name invoice-class
shortdesc Produces a standard US invoice from a CSV file
longdesc This class produces a standard US commercial invoice using data
longdesc from a CSV file. Invoices can span multiple pages. The class is
longdesc configurable for different shipping addresses.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/amunn/invoice-class
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/invoice-class
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics csv-support invoice
catalogue-version 1.0

name invoice2
shortdesc Intelligent invoices with LaTeX3
longdesc Typeset invoices with automatic VAT and calculation of totals.
longdesc Supports internationalization, invoices are typeset with
longdesc booktabs for readability. Does not support separate projects
longdesc per invoice. Can be used as a replacement for invoice in most
longdesc cases.
catalogue-contact-home https://github.com/no-preserve-root/invoice2
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/invoice2
catalogue-license gpl3+
catalogue-topics invoice

name iodhbwm
shortdesc Unofficial template of the DHBW Mannheim
longdesc This package provides an unofficial template of the DHBW
longdesc Mannheim for the creation of bachelor thesis, studies or
longdesc project work with LaTeX. The aim of the package is the quick
longdesc creation of a basic framework without much effort.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/faltfe/iodhbwm/issues
catalogue-contact-home https://faltfe.github.io/iodhbwm/
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/faltfe/iodhbwm/
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/iodhbwm
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics class dissertation misc-paper
catalogue-version 1.2.2

name ionumbers
shortdesc Restyle numbers in maths mode
longdesc ionumbers stands for input/output numbers. The package restyles
longdesc numbers in maths mode. If a number in the input file is
longdesc written, e.g., as $3,231.44$ as commonly used in English texts,
longdesc the package is able to restyle it to be output as $3\,231{,}44$
longdesc as commonly used in German texts (and vice versa). This may be
longdesc useful, for example, if you have a large table and want to
longdesc include it in texts with different output conventions without
longdesc the need to change the table. The package can also
longdesc automatically group digits left of the decimal separator
longdesc (thousands) and right of the decimal separator (thousandths) in
longdesc triplets without the need of specifying commas (English) or
longdesc points (German) as separators. E.g., the input $1234.567890$
longdesc can be output as $1\,234.\,567\,890$. Finally, an e starts the
longdesc exponent of the number. For example, $21e6$ may be output as
longdesc $26\times10\,^{6}$.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/ionumbers
catalogue-license gpl
catalogue-topics numbers
catalogue-version 0.3.3

name iopart-num
shortdesc Numeric citation style for IOP journals
longdesc A BibTeX style providing numeric citation in Harvard-like
longdesc format. Intended for use with Institute of Physics (IOP)
longdesc journals, including Journal of Physics.
catalogue-ctan /biblio/bibtex/contrib/iopart-num
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics bibtex-supp journalpub
catalogue-version 2.1

