name kpfonts
shortdesc A complete set of fonts for text and mathematics
longdesc The family contains text fonts in roman, sans-serif and
longdesc monospaced shapes, with true small caps and old-style numbers;
longdesc the package offers full support of the textcomp package. The
longdesc mathematics fonts include all the AMS fonts, in both normal and
longdesc bold weights. Each of the font types is available in two main
longdesc versions: default and light. Each version is available in four
longdesc variants: default; oldstyle numbers; oldstyle numbers with old
longdesc ligatures such as ct and st, and long-tailed capital Q; and
longdesc veryoldstyle with long s. Other variants include small caps as
longdesc default or large small caps, and for mathematics both upright
longdesc and slanted shapes for Greek letters, as well as default and
longdesc narrow versions of multiple integrals. The fonts were
longdesc originally derived from URW Palladio (with URW's agreement)
longdesc though the fonts are very clearly different in appearance from
longdesc their parent.
catalogue-also kpfonts-otf
catalogue-ctan /fonts/kpfonts
catalogue-license lppl gpl
catalogue-topics font font-maths font-mono font-sans font-serif font-type1 tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 3.36

name kpfonts-otf
shortdesc OpenType versions of the kpfonts (Type1) designed by Christophe Caignaert
longdesc This bundle provides OpenType versions of the Type1 Kp-fonts
longdesc designed by Christophe Caignaert. It is usable with LuaTeX or
longdesc XeTeX engines only. It consists of sixteen Text fonts (eight
longdesc Serif, four Sans-Serif, four Monotype) and six Math fonts.
longdesc Serif and Sans-Serif families have small caps available in two
longdesc sizes (SmallCaps and PetitesCaps), upper and lowercase digits,
longdesc real superscripts and subscripts; ancient ligatures (ct and
longdesc st), ancient long-s and a long-tailed capital Q are available
longdesc via font features. Math fonts cover all usual symbols including
longdesc AMS'; a full list of available symbols is provided, see the
longdesc List of glyphs.
catalogue-also kpfonts
catalogue-ctan /fonts/kpfonts-otf
catalogue-license ofl lppl1.3
catalogue-topics font font-body font-maths font-mono font-otf font-proportional font-sans font-serif font-supp tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 0.75

name ksfh_nat
catalogue ksfh-nat
shortdesc BibTeX style for KSFH Munich
longdesc The package supports bibliographies as standard for KSFH
longdesc (Katholische Stiftungsfachhochschule) Munich. BibTeX entries in
longdesc article, book, inbook, incollection and misc formats are
longdesc supported.
catalogue-ctan /biblio/bibtex/contrib/ksfh_nat
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics bibtex-supp
catalogue-version 1.1

name ksp-thesis
shortdesc A LaTeX class for theses published with KIT Scientific Publishing
longdesc This package provides a LaTeX class intended for authors who
longdesc want to publish their thesis or other scientific work with KIT
longdesc Scientific Publishing (KSP). The class is based on the scrbook
longdesc class of the KOMA-script bundle in combination with the
longdesc ClassicThesis and ArsClassica packages. It modifies some of the
longdesc layout and style definitions of these packages in order to
longdesc provide a document layout that should be compatible with the
longdesc requirements by KSP.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/GORywwyN/ksp-thesis/tree/master/release/
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/ksp-thesis
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics class dissertation
catalogue-version 1.0.2

name ktbox
shortdesc Framework for semantic color, structured highlighting, and scholarly communication
longdesc KTBox is a modular LaTeX framework that introduces semantic
longdesc color palettes, structured highlight boxes, and ORCID-linked
longdesc author utilities for scholarly writing. The package is composed
longdesc of three lightweight and independent style files: ktbox.sty -
longdesc defines highlight boxes (standard, numbered, wide) with
longdesc semantic theming. ktcolor.sty - provides semantic color
longdesc palettes with light and dark modes. ktorcid.sty - adds
longdesc ORCID-linked author commands and icons. The framework separates
longdesc structure from style, ensuring compatibility with major classes
longdesc such as IEEEtran, acmart, article, beamer, and ICLR. Features
longdesc include numbered key-takeaway boxes, wide-format environments
longdesc for emphasis, multi-column layouts, and dual light/dark themes.
longdesc KTBox aims to improve clarity, portability, and reproducibility
longdesc in academic publishing across articles, posters, and
longdesc presentations.
catalogue-contact-announce https://github.com/mangalbhaskar/ktbox/releases
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/mangalbhaskar/ktbox/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/mangalbhaskar/ktbox
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/ktbox
catalogue-license apache2
catalogue-topics boxing notes
catalogue-version 0.0.1

name ktv-texdata
shortdesc Extract subsets of documents
longdesc The package defines an exercice environment which numbers every
longdesc exercise, and a command \get to extract a collection whose
longdesc argument is a comma-separated set of exercise index numbers.
longdesc While the package was designed for teachers constructing tables
longdesc of exercises, it plainly has more general application.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/ktv-texdata
catalogue-license gpl
catalogue-topics data-sel
catalogue-version 05.34

name ku-template
shortdesc Copenhagen University or faculty logo for front page
longdesc A comprehensive package for adding University of Copenhagen or
longdesc faculty logo to your front page. For use by student or staff at
longdesc University of Copenhagen (Kobenhavns Universitet).
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/ku-template
catalogue-license mit
catalogue-topics logo
catalogue-version 0.02

name kurdishlipsum
shortdesc A lipsum package for the Kurdish language
longdesc This package provides lipsum-like facilities for the Kurdish
longdesc language. The package gives you easy access to the Kurdish
longdesc poetry and balladry texts of the Diwany Vafaiy, Ahmedy Xani,
longdesc Naly, Mahwy,.... The package needs to be run under XeLaTeX.
catalogue-ctan /macros/xetex/latex/kurdishlipsum
catalogue-license lppl1.2
catalogue-topics dummy-gen kurdish macro-supp tagged-pdf-unsupported xetex
catalogue-version 1.1

name kurier
shortdesc A two-element sans-serif typeface
longdesc Kurier is a two-element sans-serif typeface. It was designed
longdesc for a diploma in typeface design at the Warsaw Academy of Fine
longdesc Arts under the supervision of Roman Tomaszewski. This
longdesc distribution contains a significantly extended set of
longdesc characters covering the following modern alphabets: latin
longdesc (including Vietnamese), Cyrillic and Greek as well as a number
longdesc of additional symbols (including mathematical symbols). The
longdesc fonts are prepared in Type 1 and OpenType formats. For use with
longdesc TeX the following encoding files have been prepared: T1 (ec),
longdesc T2 (abc), and OT2-Cyrillic, T5 (Vietnamese), OT4, QX, texansi
longdesc and-nonstandard (IL2 for the Czech fonts), as well as
longdesc supporting macros and files defining fonts for LaTeX.
catalogue-ctan /fonts/kurier
catalogue-license gfl
catalogue-topics font font-otf font-type1 tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 0.995b

name kvdefinekeys
shortdesc Define keys for use in the kvsetkeys package
longdesc The package provides a macro \kv@define@key (analogous to
longdesc keyval's \define@key, to define keys for use by kvsetkeys.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/LaTeX-Package-Repositories/kvdefinekeys/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/LaTeX-Package-Repositories/kvdefinekeys
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/kvdefinekeys
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics keyval tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 1.6

name kvmap
shortdesc Create Karnaugh maps with LaTeX
longdesc This LaTeX package allows the creation of (even large) Karnaugh
longdesc maps. It provides a tabular-like input syntax and support for
longdesc drawing bundles (implicants) around adjacent values. It is
longdesc based on an answer at StackExchange.
