name l3experimental
shortdesc Experimental LaTeX3 concepts
longdesc The l3experimental packages are a collection of experimental
longdesc implementations for aspects of the LaTeX3 kernel, dealing with
longdesc higher-level ideas such as the Designer Interface. Some of them
longdesc work as stand alone packages, providing new functionality, and
longdesc can be used on top of LaTeX2e with no changes to the existing
longdesc kernel. The present release includes: l3draw, a code-level
longdesc interface for constructing drawings; xcoffins, which allows the
longdesc alignment of boxes using a series of handle positions,
longdesc supplementing the simple TeX reference point;
catalogue-also l3kernel l3packages
catalogue-contact-home https://www.latex-project.org
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/l3experimental
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics latex3 layout macro-supp tagged-pdf

name l3kernel
shortdesc LaTeX3 programming conventions
longdesc The l3kernel bundle provides an implementation of the LaTeX3
longdesc programmers' interface, as a set of packages that run under
longdesc LaTeX2e. The interface provides the foundation on which the
longdesc LaTeX3 kernel and other future code are built: it is an API for
longdesc TeX programmers. The packages are set up so that the LaTeX3
longdesc conventions can be used with regular LaTeX2e packages.
longdesc Important: l3backend is now integrated in l3kernel!
catalogue-alias l3backend
catalogue-also l3packages l3experimental
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/latex3/latex3/issues
catalogue-contact-home https://www.latex-project.org
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/latex3/latex3
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/required/l3kernel
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics format latex3

name l3kernel-dev
shortdesc Development pre-release of l3kernel
longdesc This is a pre-release version of the l3kernel package. It
longdesc accompanies the pre-testing kernel code (latex-base-dev), and
longdesc is intended for testing by knowledgeable users. Important:
longdesc l3backend-dev is now integrated in l3kernel-dev!
catalogue-alias l3backend-dev
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex-dev/required/l3kernel
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics format latex3 pre-release

name l3packages
shortdesc High-level LaTeX3 concepts
longdesc This collection deals with higher-level ideas such as the
longdesc Designer Interface, as part of LaTeX3 developments. The
longdesc packages here have over time migrated into the LaTeX kernel:
longdesc the material here is retained to support older files. The
longdesc appropriate LaTeX kernel releases incorporating the ideas from
longdesc the packages here are l3keys2e 2022-06-01 xfp 2022-06-01 xparse
longdesc 2020-10-01 xtemplate 2024-06-01
catalogue-also l3kernel l3experimental
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/latex3/latex3/issues
catalogue-contact-home https://www.latex-project.org
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/l3packages
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics latex3 macro-supp

name l3sys-query
shortdesc System queries for LaTeX using Lua
longdesc The l3sys-query script provides a method for TeX runs to obtain
longdesc system information via shell escape to Lua. The facilities are
longdesc more limited than the similar Java script texosquery, but since
longdesc it uses Lua, l3sys-query can be used out of the box; with any
longdesc installed TeX system. The script is written taking account of
longdesc TeX Live security requirements; it is therefore suitable for
longdesc use with restricted shell escape, the standard setting when
longdesc installing a TeX system. The supported queries are lsDirectory
longdesc listing supporting a range of options pwdObtaining details of
longdesc the current working directory
catalogue-also texosquery
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/latex3/l3sys-query/issues
catalogue-contact-home https://github.com/latex3/l3sys-query
catalogue-ctan /support/l3sys-query
catalogue-license mit
catalogue-topics sys-supp tagged-pdf use-lua

