longdesc manipulations take place in what Knuth is pleased to call TeX's
longdesc mouth.
catalogue-ctan /macros/generic/lambda-lists
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics macro-supp

name lambdax
shortdesc Use Lambda expression within LaTeX
longdesc This package provides Lambda expressions. It is an interface to
longdesc specify the parameters and replacement code of a
longdesc document-command, and then to evaluate it with compatible
longdesc arguments. Optionally, it can be used recursively.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/rogard/lambdax
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/lambdax
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics macro-def macro-supp
catalogue-version 1.1

name langcode
shortdesc Simple language-dependent settings based on language codes
longdesc The package provides a command \uselangcode{<code>} to adjust
longdesc language-dependent settings such as key words, typographical
longdesc conventions and language codes (ISO 639-1). The package
longdesc provides a means of selecting macros according to the specified
longdesc code, for preparing a document that is to be separately typeset
longdesc in different languages. The package is dependent on the
longdesc plainpkg package, and is already in use in the morehype and
longdesc catcodes packages.
catalogue-contact-support https://www.webdesign-bu.de/uwe_lueck/contact.html
catalogue-ctan /macros/generic/langcode
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics macro-gen multilingual
catalogue-version 0.2

name langnames
shortdesc Name languages and their genetic affiliations consistently
longdesc This package attempts to make the typing of language names,
longdesc codes, and families slightly easier by providing macros to
longdesc access pre-defined language-code-family combinations from two
longdesc important databases, as well as the possibility to create new
longdesc combinations. It may be particularly useful for large,
longdesc collaborative projects as well as typologically minded ones
longdesc with a variety of language examples.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/cicervlvs/langnames/issues
catalogue-contact-home https://github.com/cicervlvs/langnames
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/cicervlvs/langnames
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/langnames
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics abbrev linguistic
catalogue-version 3.0.0

name langsci
shortdesc Typeset books for publication with Language Science Press
longdesc This package allows you to typeset monographs and edited
longdesc volumes for publication with Language Science Press
longdesc (https://www.langsci-press.org). It includes all necessary
longdesc files for title pages, frontmatter, main content, list of
longdesc references and indexes. Dust jackets for BoD and Createspace
longdesc (print-on-demand service providers) can also be produced.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/langsci/langscibook/issues
catalogue-contact-development https://github.com/glottotopia
catalogue-contact-home https://www.langsci-press.org
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/langsci/langscibook
catalogue-contact-support mailto:support@langsci-press.org
catalogue-ctan /macros/xetex/latex/langsci
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics book-pub class journalpub

name langsci-avm
shortdesc Feature structures and attribute-value matrices (AVM)
longdesc A package for typesetting feature structures, also known as
longdesc attribute-value matrices (AVMs), for use in linguistics. The
longdesc package provides a minimal and easy to read syntax. It depends
longdesc only on the array package and can be placed almost everywhere,
longdesc in particular in footnotes or graphs and tree structures. The
longdesc package serves the same purpose as, Christopher Manning's avm
longdesc package, but shares no code base with that package.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/langsci/langsci-avm/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/langsci/langsci-avm
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/langsci-avm
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics linguistic matrix
catalogue-version 0.4.0

name lapdf
shortdesc PDF drawing directly in TeX documents
longdesc The package provides the means to use PDF drawing primitives to
longdesc produce high quality, colored graphics. It uses Bezier curves
longdesc (integral and rational) from degree one to seven, allows TeX
longdesc typesetting in the graphic, offers most of the standard math
longdesc functions, allows plotting normal, parametric and polar
longdesc functions. The package has linear, logx, logy, logxy and polar
longdesc grids with many specs; it can rotate, clip and do many nice
longdesc things easily it has two looping commands for programming and
longdesc many instructive example files. The package requires pdfTeX but
longdesc otherwise only depends on the calc package.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/lapdf
catalogue-license gpl
catalogue-topics graphics-in-tex
catalogue-version 1.1

name lastbib
shortdesc Record the number of citations in a document
longdesc The package records the number of citations in a document, and
longdesc provides a command (\LastBib) to print the number.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/lastbib
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics cite-supp
catalogue-version 2.1

name lastpackage
shortdesc Indicates the last loaded package
longdesc This package may be used to define the last point where some
longdesc code shall be executed. Its provides a package name for use in
longdesc package-placing commands from the author's templatetools. Usage
longdesc examples are provided in the documentation.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/lastpackage
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics preamble-admin
catalogue-version 0.1

name lastpage
shortdesc Reference last page for Page N of M type footers
longdesc Reference the number of pages in your LaTeX document through
longdesc the introduction of a new label which can be referenced like
longdesc \pageref{LastPage} to give a reference to the last page of a
longdesc document. It is particularly useful in the page footer that
longdesc says: Page N of M.
catalogue-also totpages
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/lastpage
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics label-ref tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 2.1h

name latex
shortdesc A TeX macro package that defines LaTeX
longdesc LaTeX is a widely-used macro package (format) for TeX,
longdesc providing many basic document formatting commands extended by a
longdesc wide range of packages. It was originally created by Leslie
longdesc Lamport, whose last release was LaTeX 2.09. The current LaTeX
longdesc superseded that release in June 1994. The basic distribution is
longdesc catalogued separately, at latex-base. Apart from a large set of
longdesc contributed packages and third-party documentation (elsewhere
longdesc on the archive), the distribution includes: a number of
longdesc required packages, which LaTeX authors may assume will be
longdesc present on any system running LaTeX; and a minimal set of
longdesc documentation detailing differences from the old version of
longdesc LaTeX in the areas of user commands, font selection and
longdesc control, class and package writing, font encodings,
longdesc configuration options and modification of LaTeX. For
longdesc downloading details, documentation links, etc., see the linked
longdesc catalogue entries above.
catalogue-contact-home https://www.latex-project.org/
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics format

name latex-amsmath-dev
shortdesc Development pre-release of the LaTeX amsmath bundle
longdesc This is a pre-release version of the standard LaTeX amsmath
longdesc bundle. It accompanies the pre-testing kernel code
longdesc (latex-base-dev), and is intended for testing by knowledgeable
longdesc users.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex-dev/required/amsmath
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics latex-devel maths pre-release
catalogue-version pre-release 2

name latex-base-dev
shortdesc Development pre-release of the LaTeX kernel
longdesc This package provides a test release for upcoming LaTeX2e
longdesc kernel changes. Testing by the LaTeX team itself suggests that
longdesc the code is stable and usable, but wider use by knowledgeable
longdesc users is desired. The code here is used by TeX systems to
longdesc create dedicated formats, for example pdflatex-dev and
longdesc lualatex-dev, which can then be used explicitly for testing,
longdesc simply by changing your program invocation.
catalogue-alias latex-dev
catalogue-also latex-base
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex-dev/base
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics class format latex-devel pre-release
catalogue-version pre-release 2

