name lineara
shortdesc Linear A script fonts
longdesc The linearA package provides a simple interface to two fonts
longdesc which include all known symbols, simple and complex, of the
longdesc Linear A script. This way one can easily replicate Linear A
longdesc texts using modern typographic technology. Note that the Linear
longdesc A script has not been deciphered yet and probably never will be
longdesc deciphered.
catalogue-ctan /fonts/archaic/linearA
catalogue-license lppl1
catalogue-topics font font-archaic font-type1

name linearregression
shortdesc Calculate and display linear regressions
longdesc This package provides the definition of some document-level
longdesc commands (and some auxiliary functions) that perform the linear
longdesc regression on a set of data and present the data and the
longdesc results in tabular and in graphic form.
catalogue-also xint-regression
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/linearregression
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics calculation maths

name linebreaker
shortdesc Prevent overflow boxes with LuaLaTeX
longdesc This package tries to prevent overflow lines in paragraphs or
longdesc boxes. It changes LuaTeX's \linebreak callback and re-typesets
longdesc the paragraph with increased values of \tolerance and
longdesc \emergencystretch until the overflow no longer happens. If that
longdesc doesn't help, it chooses the solution with the lowest badness.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/michal-h21/linebreaker/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/michal-h21/linebreaker
catalogue-ctan /macros/luatex/latex/linebreaker
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics luatex micro-layout tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 0.1c

name linegoal
shortdesc A dimen that returns the space left on the line
longdesc The linegoal package provides a macro \linegoal to be used with
longdesc \setlength: \setlength<some dimen>\linegoal will set <some
longdesc dimen> to the horizontal length of the remainder of the line.
longdesc This is achieved using the \pdfsavepos primitive of pdfTeX,
longdesc through the zref-savepos package. Example: Some text:
longdesc \begin{tabularx}\linegoal{|l|X|} \hline one & two \\ three &
longdesc four \\\hline \end{tabularx} will position the table after the
longdesc initial text, and make the table fill the rest of the line.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/linegoal
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics layout tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 2.9

name lineno
shortdesc Line numbers on paragraphs
longdesc Adds line numbers to selected paragraphs with reference
longdesc possible through the LaTeX \ref and \pageref cross reference
longdesc mechanism. Line numbering may be extended to footnote lines,
longdesc using the fnlineno package.
catalogue-also numline edmac ledmac ednotes manyfoot poemscol
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/latex-lineno/lineno/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/latex-lineno/lineno
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/lineno
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics line-nos tagged-pdf-incompatible typesetting
catalogue-version 5.9

name linesys
shortdesc Typeset linear systems and expressions from matrix-like input
longdesc linesys is a LaTeX package for converting
longdesc augmented-matrix-style input into typeset systems of linear
longdesc equations or inequalities. It also provides linear-expression
longdesc rendering through the linexp environment and the \linexpr
longdesc command, together with configurable variable generation,
longdesc relation symbols, pivot selection and highlighting, selective
longdesc styling wrappers, persistent defaults, and extensible lexical
longdesc coefficient classification.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/linesys
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics maths maths-syseqn matrix
catalogue-version 1.0

name ling-macros
shortdesc Macros for typesetting formal linguistics
longdesc This package contains macros for typesetting glosses and formal
longdesc expressions. It covers a range of subfields in formal
longdesc linguistics.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/ling-macros
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics linguistic

name linguex
shortdesc Format linguists' examples
longdesc This bundle comprises two packages: The linguex package
longdesc facilitates the formatting of linguist examples, automatically
longdesc taking care of example numbering, indentations, indexed
longdesc brackets, and the * in grammaticality judgments. The ps-trees
longdesc package provides linguistic trees, building on the macros of
longdesc tree-dvips, but overcoming some of the older package's
longdesc shortcomings.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/linguex
catalogue-license lppl1
catalogue-topics linguistic tagged-pdf tree
catalogue-version 4.3

name linguexx
shortdesc A tagging-aware package for typesetting linguistic examples and glosses
longdesc This is a standalone LaTeX package for linguistic examples,
longdesc with a linguex-compatible input syntax and first-class support
longdesc for accessible (tagged) PDF output. linguexx reimplements the
longdesc familiar dot-syntax of linguex on the expl3 kernel, with no
longdesc dependency on linguex, cgloss4e, or xspace. It runs on
longdesc pdfLaTeX, XeLaTeX and LuaLaTeX. When the document enables the
longdesc LaTeX tagging code, linguexx writes its examples into the PDF
longdesc structure tree as accessible objects.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/ghschaden/linguexx
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/linguexx
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics linguistic
catalogue-version 1.4

name linguisticspro
shortdesc LaTeX support for the LinguisticsPro font family
longdesc The package provides LaTeX, pdfLaTeX, XeLaTeX and LuaLaTeX
longdesc support for the LinguisticsPro family of fonts. This family is
longdesc derived from the Utopia Nova font family, by Andreas Nolda.
catalogue-contact-home https://www.fontsquirrel.com/fonts/linguistics-pro
catalogue-ctan /fonts/linguisticspro
catalogue-license lppl ofl
