name linguistix
shortdesc Enhanced support for linguistics
longdesc This is an experimental bundle of packages that provide
longdesc enhanced support for typesetting in linguistics. It can be used
longdesc as a single package, or the packages can be loaded
longdesc independently for separate features. Currently, it provides the
longdesc following packages: LinguisTiX-base: A base package used by
longdesc other LinguisTiX siblings LinguisTiX-fixpex: Solves the
longdesc compatibility bug between expex and unicode-math
longdesc LinguisTiX-fonts: General text in the New Computer Modern font
longdesc family LinguisTiX-ipa: IPA text in the New Computer Modern font
longdesc family LinguisTiX-glossing: Accessible interlinear glossing
longdesc LinguisTiX-leipzig: Leipzig-style glossing with tagging
longdesc LinguisTiX-languages: Support for modern multilingual
longdesc typesetting LinguisTiX-logos: For printing the logos of the
longdesc LinguisTiX bundle LinguisTiX-nfss: Extra control over NFSS
catalogue-alias linguistix-base linguistix-fonts linguistix-ipa linguistix-logos linguistix-nfss linguistix-fixpex linguistix-languages linguistix-british linguistix-american linguistix-greek linguistix-malayalam linguistix-marathi
catalogue-contact-bugs https://puszcza.gnu.org.ua/bugs/?group=linguistix
catalogue-contact-home https://puszcza.gnu.org.ua/projects/linguistix
catalogue-contact-repository https://git.gnu.org.ua/linguistix.git/
catalogue-ctan /macros/unicodetex/latex/linguistix
catalogue-license gpl3+
catalogue-topics linguistic
catalogue-version 1.0

name linkedthm
shortdesc Hyperlinked theorem-proof environments for LaTeX
longdesc This package provides lightweight infrastructure for
longdesc bidirectional linking between theorem-like environments and
longdesc their corresponding proofs. It automatically adds a [Proof]
longdesc hyperlink at the end of a theorem and a restated version with a
longdesc [Return] link inside the proof. You can declare any number of
longdesc custom linked environments (e.g., linkeddefinition,
longdesc linkedexample) using \DeclareLinkedTheorem, and base them on
longdesc any amsthm-compatible environment. This is useful for
longdesc mathematical writing and documentation, where proof navigation
longdesc is essential. The package uses amsthm, xparse, and hyperref,
longdesc and is compatible with all standard LaTeX engines.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/Ludvins/linkedthm/tree/main
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/linkedthm
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics hyper maths-theorem
catalogue-version 1.0

name linop
shortdesc Typeset linear operators as they appear in quantum theory or linear algebra
longdesc This small package aims to provide two simple commands and many
longdesc options to easily write linear operators as they appear in
longdesc many-body physics, quantum theory, and linear algebra, in any
longdesc of the ways commonly in use.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/linop
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics maths physics
catalogue-version 0.1

name lion-msc
shortdesc LaTeX class for B.Sc. and M.Sc. reports at Leiden Institute of Physics (LION)
longdesc LaTeX class for B.Sc. and M.Sc. reports at Leiden Institute of
longdesc Physics (LION). The purpose of this class is twofold: It
longdesc creates a uniform layout of the student theses from our
longdesc department. More importantly it contains several fields on the
longdesc front-page that the user needs to fill that are used in the
longdesc university administration (name, student number and name of
longdesc supervisor). Students are free to change the layout of the text
longdesc but should leave the title page as it is.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/lion-msc
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics class dissertation
catalogue-version 0.31

