name lua-alt-getopt
shortdesc Process application arguments the same way as getopt_long
longdesc lua_altgetopt is a MIT-licensed module for Lua, for processing
longdesc application arguments in the same way as BSD/GNU getopt_long(3)
longdesc functions do. This module is made available for Lua script
longdesc writers to have consistent command line parsing routines.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/cheusov/lua-alt-getopt
catalogue-ctan /support/lualibs/lua-alt-getopt
catalogue-license mit
catalogue-topics lua-supp
catalogue-version 0.7.0

name lua-calendrica
shortdesc Lua implementation of Calendrical Calculations by Dershowitz & Reingold
longdesc This is a Lua port of the calendrical algorithms from
longdesc Calendrical Calculations (4th edition) by Nachum Dershowitz and
longdesc Edward M. Reingold. It covers a wide range of calendars
longdesc including Gregorian, Hebrew, Islamic, Persian, Chinese, Hindu
longdesc (modern and old), Tibetan, Balinese, Mayan, Julian, Coptic,
longdesc Ethiopic, French Revolutionary, Icelandic, Akan, Baha'i, and
longdesc more, along with astronomical calculations for sunrise, sunset,
longdesc lunar phases, and solar terms.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://codeberg.org/polyglossia/lua-calendrica/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://codeberg.org/polyglossia/lua-calendrica
catalogue-ctan /macros/luatex/generic/lua-calendrica
catalogue-license apache2
catalogue-topics calendar luatex macro-gen
catalogue-version 0.2

name lua-check-hyphen
shortdesc Mark hyphenations in a document, for checking
longdesc The package looks at all hyphenation breaks in the document,
longdesc comparing them against a white-list prepared by the author. If
longdesc a hyphenation break is found, for which there is no entry in
longdesc the white-list, the package flags the line where the break
longdesc starts. The author may then either add the hyphenation to the
longdesc white-list, or adjust the document to avoid the break.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/pgundlach/lua-check-hyphen/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/pgundlach/lua-check-hyphen
catalogue-ctan /macros/luatex/latex/lua-check-hyphen
catalogue-license mit
catalogue-topics hyphenation luatex tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 0.7a

name lua-font-config
shortdesc Lua-based OpenType font configuration for LuaLaTeX
longdesc Fast and simple OpenType font configuration for LuaLaTeX.
longdesc Efficient auto-generation of font families providing easy
longdesc access to the multiple shapes, weights, widths and features
longdesc provided by many of today's fonts. Engine callbacks, LaTeX
longdesc hooks and caching are used to eliminate pre-loading, reduce
longdesc lookups and minimise pre-defining. This allows very rich font
longdesc families to be quicky generated, with minimal user input and
longdesc zero configuration files. The core code consists of two Lua
longdesc modules: one taken as-is from ConTeXt (MKIV) and one providing
longdesc the LaTeX interface and data processing. The package is
longdesc experimental and, while already usable in many cases,
longdesc currently(?) provides only a small part of fontspec's
longdesc functionality. Implemented features include configuration of
longdesc the main document font families (roman, sans, typewriter), use
longdesc of these families in maths mode, creation of additional
longdesc families (text mode) and support for Unicode maths (via
longdesc lua-unicode-math). Missing features include support for
longdesc multi-lingual typesetting, variable fonts, spot colours etc.
longdesc and a user interface beyond the rudimentary.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/cfr42/nfssext
catalogue-ctan /macros/luatex/latex/lua-font-config
catalogue-license lppl1.3c gpl2
catalogue-topics font-mgmt font-sel font-use luatex
catalogue-version 0.1

name lua-list-hyphen
shortdesc Per-language checking and listing of hyphenated words for LuaLaTeX
longdesc This LuaLaTeX package can check each word that has been
longdesc hyphenated across lines against language-specific dictionaries
longdesc of valid divisions, optionally adding visual flags to the
longdesc generated document, and write files listing hyphenations (and
longdesc their contexts), for external checking.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://codeberg.org/ajcain/lua-list-hyphen/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://codeberg.org/ajcain/lua-list-hyphen
catalogue-ctan /macros/luatex/latex/lua-list-hyphen
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics hyphenation luatex
catalogue-version 0.43.2

name lua-physical
shortdesc Functions and objects for the computation of physical quantities
longdesc This is a pure Lua library, which provides functions and
longdesc objects for the computation of physical quantities. The package
longdesc provides units of the SI and the imperial system. In order to
longdesc display the numbers with measurement uncertainties, the package
longdesc is able to perform Gaussian error propagation.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/tjenni/lua-physical/issues
catalogue-contact-home https://github.com/tjenni/lua-physical
catalogue-ctan /macros/luatex/latex/lua-physical
catalogue-license mit
catalogue-topics luatex physics
catalogue-version 1.0.5

name lua-placeholders
shortdesc Specifying placeholders for demonstration purposes
longdesc This package is meant for setting parameters in a LuaLaTeX
longdesc document in a more programmatic way with YAML. Parameters can
longdesc be specified by adding a recipe file. These recipe files
longdesc describe the parameter's type, placeholders and/or default
longdesc values. From thereon, the placeholders can be displayed in the
longdesc document and an example document can be created. An actual copy
longdesc document can be created by loading additional payload files,
longdesc which all must correspond to a recipe file.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/Xerdi/lua-placeholders
catalogue-ctan /macros/luatex/generic/lua-placeholders
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics luatex macro-gen
catalogue-version 2.0.2

name lua-regression
shortdesc Add polynomial regressions to graphs
longdesc This LuaLaTeX package provides a simple interface for
longdesc performing polynomial regression on data sets. It allows users
longdesc to specify the order of the polynomial regression, the columns
longdesc of the data set to use, and whether to plot the results. The
longdesc package also includes options for confidence intervals and
longdesc error bands.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/HaivuUK/lua-regression/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/HaivuUK/lua-regression
catalogue-ctan /macros/luatex/latex/lua-regression
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics csv-support data-manip data-prep graphics-plot luatex
catalogue-version 1.0.2

name lua-tikz3dtools
shortdesc Not-so-experimental LuaLaTeX package for 3D illustrations in TikZ
longdesc This package improves on existing 3D capabilities in TikZ. In
longdesc particular, the package enables z-sorting of multiple
longdesc triangulated parametric objects and uses elaborate clipping and
longdesc occlusion logic. The parametric objects are defined using
longdesc pgfkeys, and endeavor to enable user customization. All of the
longdesc 3D math is handled in Lua, and the results are projected onto
longdesc the 2D TikZ canvas. The user is enabled to use linear, affine
longdesc and projective transformations on their parametric objects.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/Pseudonym321/lua-tikz3dtools
catalogue-ctan /graphics/pgf/contrib/lua-tikz3dtools
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics graphics graphics-3d luatex pgf-tikz
catalogue-version 3.4.0

name lua-tinyyaml
shortdesc A tiny YAML (subset) parser in pure Lua
longdesc This package provides a YAML (subset) parser written in pure
longdesc Lua. It supports a subset of the YAML 1.2 specifications. It is
longdesc required by several other LuaTeX packages including markdown
longdesc and citeproc-lua.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/zepinglee/lua-tinyyaml
catalogue-ctan /macros/luatex/generic/lua-tinyyaml
catalogue-license mit
catalogue-topics luatex parser
catalogue-version 0.4.4

name lua-typo
shortdesc Highlighting typographical flaws with LuaLaTeX
longdesc Prints the list of pages on which typographical flaws were
longdesc found (i.e. widows, orphans, hyphenated words split across two
longdesc pages, consecutive lines ending with hyphens, paragraphs ending
longdesc on too short or nearly full lines, homeoarchy, etc).
longdesc Customisable colours are used to highlight these flaws.
catalogue-ctan /macros/luatex/latex/lua-typo
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics luatex tagged-pdf text-layout
catalogue-version 0.88

name lua-uca
shortdesc Unicode Collation Algorithm library for Lua
longdesc The Lua-UCA library provides basic support for Unicode
longdesc Collation Algorithm in Lua. It can be used to sort arrays of
longdesc strings according to rules of particular languages. It can be
longdesc used in other Lua projects that need to sort text in a language
longdesc dependent way, like indexing processors, bibliographic
longdesc generators, etc.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/michal-h21/lua-uca/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/michal-h21/lua-uca
catalogue-ctan /support/lualibs/lua-uca
catalogue-license mit
catalogue-topics luatex typesetting
catalogue-version 0.1e

name lua-ul
shortdesc Underlining for LuaLaTeX
longdesc This package provides underlining, strikethough, and
longdesc highlighting using features in LuaLaTeX which avoid the
longdesc restrictions imposed by other methods. In particular, kerning
longdesc is not affected, the underlined text can use arbitrary
longdesc commands, hyphenation works etc. The package requires LuaTeX
longdesc version [?] 1.12.0.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/zauguin/luaul/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/zauguin/luaul
catalogue-ctan /macros/luatex/latex/lua-ul
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics luatex tagged-pdf-partially underline
catalogue-version 0.2.1

name lua-uni-algos
shortdesc Unicode algorithms for LuaTeX
longdesc Lua code working with Unicode data has to deal with quite some
longdesc challenges. For example there are many canonically equivalent
longdesc sequences which should be treated in the same way, and even
longdesc identifying a single character becomes quite different once you
longdesc have to deal with all kinds of combining characters, emoji
longdesc sequences and syllables in different scripts. Therefore
longdesc lua-uni-algos wants to build a collection of small libraries
longdesc implementing algorithms to deal with lots of the details in
longdesc Unicode, such that authors of LuaTeX packages can focus on
longdesc their actual functionality instead of having to fight against
longdesc the peculiarities of Unicode. Given that this package provides
longdesc Lua modules, it is only useful in Lua(HB)TeX. Additionally, it
longdesc expects an up-to-date version of the unicode-data package to be
longdesc present. This package is intended for package authors only; no
longdesc user-level functionality provided.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/latex3/lua-uni-algos
catalogue-ctan /macros/luatex/generic/lua-uni-algos
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics luatex unicode
catalogue-version 0.5

name lua-unicode-math
shortdesc OpenType Math font support for LuaLaTeX
longdesc A faster and more compatible package to support using OpenType
longdesc math fonts in LuaLaTeX as an alternative for unicode-math.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/zauguin/lua-unicode-math/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/zauguin/lua-unicode-math
catalogue-ctan /macros/luatex/latex/lua-unicode-math
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics font-use luatex maths tagged-pdf unicode
catalogue-version 0.11

name lua-visual-debug
shortdesc Visual debugging with LuaLaTeX
longdesc The package uses lua code to provide visible indications of
longdesc boxes, glues, kerns and penalties in the PDF output. The
longdesc package is known to work in LaTeX and Plain TeX documents.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/Udi-Fogiel/lvdebug
catalogue-ctan /macros/luatex/generic/lua-visual-debug
catalogue-license mit
catalogue-topics debug-supp luatex macro-gen
catalogue-version 1.1

name lua-widow-control
shortdesc Automatically remove widows and orphans from any document
longdesc Unmodified TeX has very few ways of preventing widows and
longdesc orphans. In documents with figures, section headings, and
longdesc equations, TeX can stretch the vertical glue between items in
longdesc order to prevent widows and orphans, but many documents have no
longdesc figures or headings. TeX can also shorten the page by 1 line,
longdesc but this will give each page a different length which can make
longdesc a document look uneven. The typical solution is to
longdesc strategically insert \looseness=1, but this requires manual
longdesc editing every time that the document is edited.
longdesc Lua-widow-control is essentially an automation of the
longdesc \looseness method: it uses Lua callbacks to find stretchy
longdesc paragraphs, then it lengthens them to remove widows and
longdesc orphans. Lua-widow-control is compatible with all LuaTeX and
longdesc LuaMetaTeX-based formats. All that is required is to load the
longdesc package at the start of your document. To load: Plain LuaTeX:
longdesc \input lua-widow-control LuaLaTeX:
longdesc \usepackage{lua-widow-control} ConTeXt:
longdesc \usemodule[lua-widow-control] OpTeX: \load[lua-widow-control]
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/gucci-on-fleek/lua-widow-control/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/gucci-on-fleek/lua-widow-control
catalogue-contact-support https://github.com/gucci-on-fleek/lua-widow-control/discussions
catalogue-ctan /macros/luatex/generic/lua-widow-control
catalogue-license other-free cc-by-sa-4
catalogue-topics layout luatex tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 3.0.1

name luaaddplot
shortdesc An extension to pgfplots' \addplot macro
longdesc This package is an extension to pgfplots. It extends the
longdesc \addplot macro by a facility which allows modification of data
longdesc files while they are read. With luaaddplot it is no longer
longdesc necessary to pre-process data files generated by measuring
longdesc devices with external scripts. This package can be used with
longdesc plain LuaTeX or LuaLaTeX.
catalogue-ctan /macros/luatex/generic/luaaddplot
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics graphics graphics-plot luatex
catalogue-version 1.0a

name luabibentry
