name makeglos
shortdesc Include a glossary into a document
longdesc The package provides the means to include a glossary into a
longdesc document. The glossary is prepared by an external program, such
longdesc as xindy or makeindex, in the same way that an index is made.
catalogue-also nomencl glosstex gloss
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/makeglos
catalogue-license gpl
catalogue-topics glossary

name makegobbler
shortdesc Keep or drop some part of LaTeX source code
longdesc The makegobbler package provides a mechanism to selectively
longdesc drop (gobble) or keep (ungobble) portions of LaTeX source code,
longdesc either conditionally or unconditionally. The affected code is
longdesc delimited by user-defined control sequences that act as
longdesc explicit markers. For example, you can define a conditional as
longdesc follows: \newif\ifkeep You can then make a portion of the
longdesc source conditional like this: \keepfalse
longdesc \MGBkeep*\ifkeep\SomeArbitraryDelimitingControlSequence Here,
longdesc everything - including \fi#!{}_^$ - is dropped.
longdesc \SomeArbitraryDelimitingControlSequence
catalogue-also etoolbox
catalogue-contact-bugs https://puszcza.gnu.org.ua/bugs/?group=latex-makegobbler
catalogue-contact-home https://puszcza.gnu.org.ua/projects/latex-makegobbler
catalogue-contact-repository https://svn.gnu.org.ua/sources/latex-makegobbler/trunk
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/makegobbler
catalogue-license lppl1.3c other-free
catalogue-topics cond-comp macro-supp
catalogue-version 0.3.2

