name math-into-latex-4
shortdesc Samples from Math into LaTeX, 4th Edition
longdesc Samples for the book (More) Math into LaTeX, 4th edition. In
longdesc addition, there are two excerpts from the book: A Short Course
longdesc to help you get started quickly with LaTeX, including detailed
longdesc instructions on how to install LaTeX on a PC or a Mac; Math and
longdesc Text Symbol Tables.
catalogue-ctan /info/examples/Math_into_LaTeX-4
catalogue-license other-free
catalogue-topics book-ex

name math-operator
shortdesc Predefined and new math operators
longdesc This package defines control sequences for roughly one hundred
longdesc and fifty math operators, including special functions,
longdesc probability distributions, pure mathematical constructions, and
longdesc a variant of \overline. The package also provides an interface
longdesc for users to define new math operators similar to the amsopn
longdesc package. New operators can be medium or bold weight, and they
longdesc may be declared as \mathord or \mathop subformulas.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/math-operator
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics maths maths-symbol
catalogue-version 1.3a

name math-shorthandz
shortdesc Smart shorthands for typesetting math in LaTeX
longdesc The package provides shorthand macros for typesetting the most
longdesc common mathematical expressions in LaTeX. It provides compact
longdesc commands to construct symbols with highly customizable
longdesc positioning and (auto-)scaling, such as: zline -
longdesc multi-underlines, zscript - pre/succeeding scripts, zfrac -
longdesc fractions, zdiff - differentials/derivatives, zint - integrals
longdesc with different placement of limits, and more! All commands are
longdesc safe in text and distinguish their customization between
longdesc display, inline, script and/or scriptscript contexts.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/tplobo/math-shorthandz/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/tplobo/math-shorthandz
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/math-shorthandz
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics maths
catalogue-version 1.0.0

name mathabx
shortdesc Three series of mathematical symbols
longdesc Mathabx is a set of 3 mathematical symbols font series: matha,
longdesc mathb and mathx. They are defined by Metafont code and should
longdesc be of reasonable quality (bitmap output). Things change from
longdesc time to time, so there is no claim of stability (encoding,
longdesc metrics, design). The package includes Plain TeX and LaTeX
longdesc support macros. A version of the fonts, in Adobe Type 1 format,
longdesc is also available.
catalogue-contact-home http://www-math.univ-poitiers.fr/~phan/
catalogue-ctan /fonts/mathabx
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics font font-mf font-symbol-maths tagged-pdf-partially

name mathabx-type1
shortdesc Outline version of the mathabx fonts
longdesc This is an Adobe Type 1 outline version of the mathabx fonts.
catalogue-also mathabx
catalogue-ctan /fonts/ps-type1/mathabx
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics font font-symbol-maths font-type1

name mathador
shortdesc LaTeX commands for the French game Mathador
longdesc This is a LaTeX package with graphic commands for the French
longdesc game MATHADOR (by author Eric Trouillot and Reseau CANOPE). The
longdesc principle of the game is like this: Roll the dice! They give
longdesc you one target number (between 0 and 99) and five numbers to
longdesc use to reach it. You can use the four arithmetic operations to
longdesc get there.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/cpierquet/latex-packages/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/cpierquet/latex-packages/tree/main/mathador
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/mathador
catalogue-license lppl1.3c other-free
catalogue-topics games graphics pgf-tikz
catalogue-version 0.1.2

name mathaidisclose
shortdesc AI disclosure for mathematics
longdesc This package is designed to help mathematics researchers
longdesc disclose AI use transparently and in a standardised way. It
longdesc builds on the cleveref package to reference indexed lemmas,
longdesc theorems or definitions when generating the AI disclosure.
longdesc There are two different styles of AI disclosure available, one
longdesc using footnotes, and one generating a disclosure at the end of
longdesc the document.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/mathaidisclose
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics editorial maths
catalogue-version 1.1

name mathalpha
shortdesc General package for loading maths alphabets in LaTeX
longdesc Package mathalfa was renamed to mathalpha. For backward
longdesc compatibility the old name will continue to be recognized in
longdesc LaTeX documents. The package provides means of loading maths
longdesc alphabets (such as are normally addressed via macros \mathcal,
longdesc \mathbb, \mathfrak and \mathscr), offering various features
longdesc normally missing in existing packages for this job.
catalogue-alias mathalfa
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/mathalpha
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics maths tagged-pdf-partially
catalogue-version 1.145

name mathastext
shortdesc Use the text font in maths mode
longdesc The package uses a text font (usually the document's text font)
longdesc for the letters of the Latin alphabet needed when typesetting
longdesc mathematics. (Optionally, other characters in the font may also
longdesc be used). This facility makes possible (for a document with
longdesc simple mathematics) a far wider choice of text font, with
longdesc little worry that no specially designed accompanying maths
longdesc fonts are available. The package also offers a simple mechanism
longdesc for using many different choices of (text hence, now, maths)
longdesc font in the same document. Of course, using one font for two
longdesc purposes helps produce smaller PDF files.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/jfbu/mathastext/issues
catalogue-contact-home https://jfbu.github.io/mathastext/
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/mathastext
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics font-sel font-supp-maths maths tagged-pdf-partially
catalogue-version 1.4e

name mathcommand
shortdesc \newcommand-like commands for defining math macros
longdesc This package provides functionalities for defining macros that
longdesc have different behaviors depending on whether in math or text
longdesc mode, that absorb Primes, Indices and Exponents (PIE) as extra
longdesc parameters usable in the code; and it offers some iteration
longdesc facilities for defining macros with similar code. The primary
longdesc objective of this package is to be used together with the
longdesc knowledge package for a proper handling of mathematical
longdesc notations.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/mathcommand
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics macro-def macro-iterate maths
catalogue-version 1.04

name mathcomp
shortdesc Text symbols in maths mode
longdesc A package which provides access to some interesting characters
longdesc of the Text Companion fonts (TS1 encoding) in maths mode.
catalogue-also textcomp
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/mathcomp
catalogue-license lppl1
catalogue-topics font-supp-maths tagged-pdf-partially
catalogue-version 0.1f

name mathdesign
shortdesc Mathematical fonts to fit with particular text fonts
longdesc The Math Design project offers free mathematical fonts that
longdesc match with existing text fonts. To date, three free font
longdesc families are available: Adobe Utopia, URW Garamond and
longdesc Bitstream Charter. Three commercial fonts are also supported:
longdesc Adobe Garamond Pro, Adobe UtopiaStd and ITC Charter. Mathdesign
longdesc covers the whole LaTeX glyph set, including AMS symbols and
longdesc some extra. Both roman and bold versions of these symbols can
longdesc be used. Moreover you can choose between three greek fonts (two
longdesc of them created by the Greek Font Society).
catalogue-also fourier
catalogue-ctan /fonts/mathdesign
catalogue-license gpl
catalogue-topics font font-maths font-supp-maths font-type1
catalogue-version 2.31

name mathdots
shortdesc Commands to produce dots in math that respect font size
longdesc Redefines \ddots and \vdots, and defines \iddots. The dots
longdesc produced by \iddots slant in the opposite direction to \ddots.
longdesc All the commands are designed to change size appropriately in
longdesc scripts, as well as in response to LaTeX size changing
longdesc commands. The commands may also be used in plain TeX.
catalogue-ctan /macros/generic/mathdots
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics maths tagged-pdf-partially
catalogue-version 0.9

name mathexam
shortdesc Package for typesetting exams
longdesc The package can help you typeset exams (mostly in mathematics
longdesc and related disciplines where students are required to show
longdesc their calculations followed by one or more short answers). It
longdesc provides commands for inclusion of space for calculations, as
longdesc well as commands for automatic creation of answer spaces. In
longdesc addition, the package will automatically create page headers
longdesc and footers, and will let you include instructions and space
longdesc for students to put their name.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/mathexam
catalogue-license lppl1.2
catalogue-topics exam maths
catalogue-version 1.00

name mathfam256
shortdesc Extend math family up to 256 for pLaTeX/upLaTeX/Lamed
longdesc This package increases the upper limit of math symbols up to
longdesc 256, using \omath... primitives. These primitives were
longdesc originally introduced in Omega and are currently available in
longdesc the following formats: pLaTeX (runs on e-pTeX), upLaTeX (runs
longdesc on e-upTeX), Lamed (runs on Aleph, successor of Omega).
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/aminophen/mathfam256
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/mathfam256
catalogue-license bsd3
catalogue-topics etex japanese maths omega
catalogue-version 0.5

name mathfixs
shortdesc Fix various layout issues in math mode
longdesc This is a LaTeX2e package to fix some odd behaviour in math
longdesc mode such as spacing around fractions and roots, math symbols
longdesc within bold text as well as capital Greek letters. It also adds
longdesc some related macros.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/mathfixs
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics bugfix maths
catalogue-version 1.2.1

name mathfont
shortdesc Use TrueType and OpenType fonts in math mode
longdesc The mathfont package adapts unicode text fonts for math mode.
longdesc The package allows the user to specify a default unicode font
longdesc for different classes of math symbols, and it enables Unicode
longdesc input in math mode. The package provides tools to change the
longdesc font locally for math alphabet characters. When typesetting
longdesc with LuaTeX, mathfont adds resizable delimiters, big operators,
longdesc and a MathConstants table to text fonts.
catalogue-ctan /macros/unicodetex/latex/mathfont
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics font-mgmt font-use maths tagged-pdf-partially
catalogue-version 3.0a

name mathformule
shortdesc A lightweight environment for single- and multiline numbered math displays
longdesc This package provides the LaTeX2e formule environment for both
longdesc single-line and ampersand-aligned multiline display
longdesc mathematics. A multiline display may use one overall equation
longdesc number or configurable per-row subnumbers. Extensible left and
longdesc right braces, optional mathematics outside a brace, and signed
longdesc row- and brace-spacing corrections are supported. The package
longdesc shares LaTeX's standard equation counter and integrates with
longdesc the usual numbering and cross-reference mechanisms.
catalogue-also eqnlines
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/mathformule
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics maths
catalogue-version 0.6

name mathgreeks
shortdesc Use different Greek letter fonts in math mode
longdesc The purpose of this package is to provide access to numerous
longdesc Greek letter fonts for math mode, without altering other
longdesc mathematical characters and symbols and without loading whole
longdesc extensions that provide these fonts. Moreover, the chosen font
longdesc or shape can be changed dynamically throughout the document.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/mathgreeks
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics font-supp-maths
catalogue-version 1.3

name mathlig
shortdesc Define maths ligatures
longdesc The package defines character sequences that behave like
longdesc ligatures, in maths mode. Example definitions (chosen to show
longdesc the package's flexibility, are: \mathlig{->}{\rightarrow}
longdesc \mathlig{<-}{\leftarrow} \mathlig{<->}{\leftrightarrow}
catalogue-ctan /macros/generic/misc/mathlig.tex
catalogue-license other-free
catalogue-topics shortcut
catalogue-version 1.0

name mathpartir
shortdesc Typesetting sequences of math formulas, e.g. type inference rules
longdesc The package provides macros for typesetting math formulas in
longdesc mixed horizontal and vertical mode, automatically as best fit.
longdesc It provides an environment mathpar that behaves much as a loose
longdesc centered paragraph where words are math formulas, and spaces
longdesc between them are larger and adjustable. It also provides a
longdesc macro \inferrule for typesetting fractions where both the
longdesc numerator and denominator may be sequences of formulas that
longdesc will be also typeset in a similar way. It can typically be used
longdesc for typesetting sets of type inference rules or typing
longdesc derivations. A macro inferrule for typesetting type inference
longdesc rules.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/mathpartir
catalogue-license gpl2
catalogue-topics maths tagged-pdf-partially
catalogue-version 1.3.2

name mathpazo
shortdesc Fonts to typeset mathematics to match Palatino
longdesc The Pazo Math fonts are a family of PostScript fonts suitable
longdesc for typesetting mathematics in combination with the Palatino
longdesc family of text fonts. The Pazo Math family is made up of five
longdesc fonts provided in Adobe Type 1 format (PazoMath,
longdesc PazoMath-Italic, PazoMath-Bold, PazoMath-BoldItalic, and
longdesc PazoMathBlackboardBold). These contain, in designs that match
longdesc Palatino, glyphs that are usually not available in Palatino and
longdesc for which Computer Modern looks odd when combined with
longdesc Palatino. These glyphs include the uppercase Greek alphabet in
longdesc upright and slanted shapes in regular and bold weights, the
longdesc lowercase Greek alphabet in slanted shape in regular and bold
longdesc weights, several mathematical glyphs (partialdiff, summation,
longdesc product, coproduct, emptyset, infinity, and proportional) in
longdesc regular and bold weights, other glyphs (Euro and dotlessj) in
longdesc upright and slanted shapes in regular and bold weights, and the
longdesc uppercase letters commonly used to represent various number
longdesc sets (C, I, N, Q, R, and Z) in blackboard bold. LaTeX macro
longdesc support (using package mathpazo.sty) is provided in psnfss (a
longdesc required part of any LaTeX distribution).
catalogue-also pxfonts newpx tex-gyre-math-pagella
catalogue-ctan /fonts/mathpazo
catalogue-license gpl
catalogue-topics font font-bbd font-maths font-type1 tagged-pdf-partially
catalogue-version 1.003

name mathpunctspace
shortdesc Control the space after punctuation in math expressions
longdesc This package provides a mechanism to control the space after
longdesc commas and semicolons in mathematical expressions.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/yuw/texmf-mathpunctspace
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/mathpunctspace
catalogue-license bsd2
catalogue-topics maths typesetting
catalogue-version 1.1

name maths-symbols
shortdesc Summary of mathematical symbols available in LaTeX
longdesc A predecessor of the comprehensive symbols list, covering
longdesc mathematical symbols available in standard LaTeX (including the
longdesc AMS symbols, if available at compile time).
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/davidcarlisle/dpctex/tree/master/maths-symbols
catalogue-ctan /info/symbols/math
catalogue-license lppl1.2
catalogue-topics font-index maths-symbol
catalogue-version 3.4

name mathsemantics
shortdesc Semantic math commands in LaTeX
longdesc This LaTeX package provides both syntactic and semantic helpers
longdesc to typeset mathematics in LaTeX. The syntactic layer eases
longdesc typesetting of formulae in general, while the semantic layer
longdesc provides commands like \inner{x}{y} to unify typesetting of
longdesc inner products. These not only unify typesetting of math
longdesc formulae but also allow to easily adapt notation if a user
longdesc prefers to. The semantic layer is split into topics.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/kellertuer/MathSemantics.sty/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/kellertuer/MathSemantics.sty
catalogue-contact-support https://github.com/kellertuer/MathSemantics.sty/discussions
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/mathsemantics
catalogue-license mit
catalogue-topics maths
catalogue-version 1.0.0

name mathspec
shortdesc Specify arbitrary fonts for mathematics in XeTeX
longdesc The mathspec package provides an interface to typeset
longdesc mathematics in XeLaTeX with arbitrary text fonts using fontspec
longdesc as a backend. The package is under development and later
longdesc versions might to be incompatible with this version, as this
longdesc version is incompatible with earlier versions. The package
longdesc requires at least version 0.9995 of XeTeX.
catalogue-ctan /macros/xetex/latex/mathspec
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics font-maths font-sel tagged-pdf-unsupported
catalogue-version 0.2b

name mathspic
shortdesc A Perl filter program for use with PiCTeX
longdesc MathsPIC(Perl) is a development of the earlier MathsPIC(DOS)
longdesc program, now implemented as a Perl script, being much more
longdesc portable than the earlier program. MathsPIC parses a plain text
longdesc input file and generates a plain text output-file containing
longdesc commands for drawing a diagram. Version 1.0 produces output
longdesc containing PiCTeX and (La)TeX commands, which may then be
longdesc processed by plain TeX or LaTeX in the usual way. MathsPIC also
longdesc outputs a comprehensive log-file. MathsPIC facilitates creating
longdesc figures using PiCTeX by providing an environment for
longdesc manipulating named points and also allows the use of variables
longdesc and maths (advance, multiply, and divide). In short, it takes
longdesc the pain out of PiCTeX. Both the original DOS version and the
longdesc new Perl version are available.
catalogue-ctan /graphics/mathspic
catalogue-license lppl1
catalogue-topics graphics-prep
catalogue-version 1.13

name mathspic.aarch64-linux
shortdesc aarch64-linux files of mathspic

name mathspic.amd64-freebsd
shortdesc amd64-freebsd files of mathspic

name mathspic.amd64-netbsd
shortdesc amd64-netbsd files of mathspic

name mathspic.armhf-linux
shortdesc armhf-linux files of mathspic

name mathspic.i386-freebsd
shortdesc i386-freebsd files of mathspic

name mathspic.i386-linux
shortdesc i386-linux files of mathspic

name mathspic.i386-netbsd
shortdesc i386-netbsd files of mathspic

name mathspic.universal-darwin
shortdesc universal-darwin files of mathspic

name mathspic.windows
shortdesc windows files of mathspic

name mathspic.x86_64-cygwin
shortdesc x86_64-cygwin files of mathspic

name mathspic.x86_64-darwinlegacy
shortdesc x86_64-darwinlegacy files of mathspic

name mathspic.x86_64-linux
shortdesc x86_64-linux files of mathspic

name mathspic.x86_64-linuxmusl
shortdesc x86_64-linuxmusl files of mathspic

name mathtools
shortdesc Mathematical tools to use with amsmath
longdesc Mathtools provides a series of packages designed to enhance the
longdesc appearance of documents containing a lot of mathematics. The
longdesc main backbone is amsmath, so those unfamiliar with this
longdesc required part of the LaTeX system will probably not find the
longdesc packages very useful. Mathtools provides many useful tools for
longdesc mathematical typesetting. It is based on amsmath and fixes
longdesc various deficiencies of amsmath and standard LaTeX. It
longdesc provides: Extensible symbols, such as brackets, arrows,
longdesc harpoons, etc.; Various symbols such as \coloneqq (:=); Easy
longdesc creation of new tag forms; Showing equation numbers only for
longdesc referenced equations; Extensible arrows, harpoons and
longdesc hookarrows; Starred versions of the amsmath matrix environments
longdesc for specifying the column alignment; More building blocks:
longdesc multlined, cases-like environments, new gathered environments;
longdesc Maths versions of \makebox, \llap, \rlap etc.; Cramped math
longdesc styles; and more... Mathtools requires mhsetup.
catalogue-also mhsetup empheq
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/latex3/mathtools
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/mathtools
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics maths tagged-pdf-partially
catalogue-version 1.31

name matlab-prettifier
shortdesc Pretty-print Matlab source code
longdesc The package extends the facilities of the listings package, to
longdesc pretty-print Matlab and Octave source code. (Note that support
longdesc of Octave syntax is not complete.)
catalogue-also matlabweb
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/matlab-prettifier
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics listing tagged-pdf-incompatible
catalogue-version 0.3

name matrix-skeleton
shortdesc A PGF/TikZ library that simplifies working with multiple matrix nodes
longdesc The package provides a PGF/TikZ library that simplifies working
longdesc with multiple matrix nodes. To do so, it correctly aligns
longdesc groups of nodes with the content of the whole matrix.
longdesc Furthermore, matrix.skeleton provides rows and columns for easy
longdesc styling.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/dudebout/matrix.skeleton/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/dudebout/matrix.skeleton
catalogue-ctan /graphics/pgf/contrib/matrix-skeleton
catalogue-license isc
catalogue-topics maths pgf-tikz tagged-pdf-incompatible
catalogue-version 1.1

name matrixdiagrams
shortdesc Create structured matrix diagrams using TikZ
longdesc This package generates schematic matrix diagrams in TikZ to
longdesc visualize specific structures within matrices, such as
longdesc bidiagonal, tridiagonal, and Hessenberg forms. Users can also
longdesc fill in matrix portions with color, add text and mathematical
longdesc labels, and draw vertical and horizontal lines to indicate
longdesc partitions. Diagrams can be independently scaled in size and
longdesc aspect, enabling more realistic and relative drawings, such as
longdesc those used in matrix factorizations.
catalogue-also drawmatrix
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/kylemonette/matrix-diagrams/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/kylemonette/matrix-diagrams
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/matrixdiagrams
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics diagram maths matrix pgf-tikz
catalogue-version 1.3

name mattens
shortdesc Matrices/tensor typesetting
longdesc The mattens package contains the definitions to typeset
longdesc matrices, vectors and tensors as used in the engineering
longdesc community for the representation of common vectors and tensors
longdesc such as forces, velocities, moments of inertia, etc.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/mattens
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics engineering maths tagged-pdf-partially
catalogue-version 1.3b

name mayanumber
shortdesc Mayan numerals and vigesimal notation with positional floor colors
longdesc This package typesets decimal integers of any magnitude as
longdesc Mayan numerals (dots and bars, Unicode block U+1D2E0-U+1D2F3)
longdesc or as vigesimal alphabetic notation (0-9, A-J), for XeLaTeX and
longdesc LuaLaTeX. Each positional floor can be colored with a
longdesc seven-color cycle (earth, water, vegetation, life, sky, sun,
longdesc universe). Options: vertical/horizontal layout, colors/nocolor,
longdesc scale and alignment; the starred form prints the alphabetic
longdesc notation. The base-20 conversion uses long division over the
longdesc decimal string, so magnitudes are unbounded. Requires the free
longdesc font BabelStone Mayan Numerals. Extends the original macro by
longdesc @egreg (TeX StackExchange, answer 452806).
catalogue-contact-announce https://github.com/mlmateos/puntoybarra/releases
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/mlmateos/puntoybarra/issues
catalogue-contact-home https://mlmateos.github.io/puntoybarra/
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/mlmateos/puntoybarra
catalogue-ctan /macros/unicodetex/latex/mayanumber
catalogue-license mit
catalogue-topics numbers
catalogue-version 1.0.2

name maybemath
shortdesc Make math bold or italic according to context
longdesc The \maybebm and \maybeit macros can be used in maths
longdesc expressions to make the arguments typeset as bold or italic
longdesc respectively if the surrounding context is appropriate. They
longdesc are useful for writing user macros for use in general contexts.
longdesc \maybebm is especially appropriate when section titles contain
longdesc math expressions, since the title will appear bold but the
longdesc header and table of contents usually replicate the title in
longdesc normal width. It uses the bm package to make things bold
longdesc \maybeit performs a similar role to \mathrm{} but the maths
longdesc expression will be italicised if the surrounding text is.
longdesc \maybeitsubscript is provided to shift subscripts to the left
longdesc if the expression is italicised.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/maybemath
catalogue-license lppl1
catalogue-topics font-sel maths

name maze
shortdesc Generate random mazes
longdesc This package can generate random square mazes of a specified
longdesc size. The mazes generated by this package are natural and their
longdesc solution is not too obvious. The output is based on the picture
longdesc environment.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/Quantum-Phantom/expl3maze/issues
catalogue-contact-development https://github.com/Quantum-Phantom
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/Quantum-Phantom/expl3maze
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/maze
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics games
catalogue-version 1.3

name mcaption
shortdesc Put captions in the margin
longdesc The mcaption package provides an mcaption environment which
longdesc puts figure or table captions in the margin. The package works
longdesc with the standard classes and with the KOMA-Script document
longdesc classes scrartcl, scrreprt and scrbook. The package requires
longdesc the changepage package.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/mcaption
catalogue-license lppl1.2
catalogue-topics caption tagged-pdf-incompatible
catalogue-version 3.0

name mceinleger
shortdesc Creating covers for music cassettes
longdesc A package for creating MC-covers on your own. It allows the
longdesc creation of simple covers as well as covers with an additional
longdesc page for more information about the cassette (table of contents
longdesc e.g.). The rotating package is required.
catalogue-also cdcover
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/mceinleger
catalogue-license gpl
catalogue-topics covers

name mcexam
shortdesc Create randomized Multiple Choice questions
longdesc This LaTeX package automatically randomly permutes the order of
longdesc questions as well as the answer options in different versions
longdesc of a multiple choice exam/test. Next to the exam versions
longdesc themselves, the package also allows printing a concept version
longdesc of the exam, a key table with the correct answers or points,
longdesc and a document with solutions and explanations per exam
longdesc version. The package also allows writing an R code which
longdesc processes the results of the exam and calculates the grades.
longdesc The following other LaTeX packages are required: enumitem,
longdesc environ, etoolbox, longtable, newfile, pgffor (from the
longdesc PGF/TikZ bundle), xkeyval, and xstring.
catalogue-also esami
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/mcexam
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics exam random
catalogue-version 0.5

name mcf2graph
shortdesc Draw chemical structure diagrams with MetaPost
longdesc The Molecular Coding Format (MCF) is a linear notation for
longdesc describing chemical structure diagrams. This package converts
longdesc MCF to graphic files using MetaPost.
catalogue-ctan /graphics/mcf2graph
catalogue-license mit
catalogue-topics chemistry graphics graphics-mpost
catalogue-version 5.33

name mcite
shortdesc Multiple items in a single citation
longdesc The mcite package allows the user to collapse multiple
longdesc citations into one, as is customary in physics journals. The
longdesc package requires a customised BibTeX style for its work; the
longdesc documentation explains how to do that customisation.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/mcite
catalogue-license gpl
catalogue-topics cite-supp tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 1.6

name mciteplus
shortdesc Enhanced multiple citations
longdesc The mciteplus LaTeX package is an enhanced reimplementation of
longdesc Thorsten Ohl's mcite package which provides support for the
longdesc grouping of multiple citations together as is often done in
longdesc physics journals. An extensive set of features provide for
longdesc other applications such as reference sublisting.
catalogue-contact-home https://www.michaelshell.org/tex/mciteplus/
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/mciteplus
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics cite-supp tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 1.2

name mcmthesis
shortdesc Template designed for MCM/ICM
longdesc The package offers a template for MCM (The Mathematical Contest
longdesc in Modeling) and ICM (The Interdisciplinary Contest in
longdesc Modeling) for typesetting the submitted paper.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/latexstudio-org/mcmthesis
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/mcmthesis
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics class dissertation
catalogue-version 6.3.3

name mdframed
shortdesc Framed environments that can split at page boundaries
longdesc The package develops the facilities of framed in providing
longdesc breakable framed and coloured boxes. The user may instruct the
longdesc package to perform its operations using default LaTeX commands,
longdesc PStricks or TikZ.
catalogue-also framed
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/marcodaniel/mdframed
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/mdframed
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics box-breaking boxing decoration tagged-pdf-unsupported
catalogue-version 1.9b

name mdputu
shortdesc Upright digits in Adobe Utopia Italic
longdesc The Annals of Mathematics uses italics for theorems. However,
longdesc slanted digits and parentheses look disturbing when surrounded
longdesc by (upright) mathematics. This package provides virtual fonts
longdesc with italics and upright digits and punctuation, as an
longdesc extension to Mathdesign's Utopia bundle.
catalogue-ctan /fonts/mdputu
catalogue-license other-free
catalogue-topics font-maths font-virtual
catalogue-version 1.2

name mdsymbol
shortdesc Symbol fonts to match Adobe Myriad Pro
longdesc The package provides a font of mathematical symbols, MyriadPro
longdesc The font is designed as a companion to Adobe Myriad Pro, but it
longdesc might also fit well with other contemporary typefaces.
catalogue-ctan /fonts/mdsymbol
catalogue-license ofl
catalogue-topics font-mf font-otf font-symbol font-symbol-maths font-type1 tagged-pdf-partially
catalogue-version 0.5

name mdwtools
shortdesc Miscellaneous tools by Mark Wooding
longdesc This collection of tools includes: support for short commands
longdesc starting with @, macros to sanitise the OT1 encoding of the
longdesc cmtt fonts; a do after command; improved footnote support;
longdesc mathenv for various alignment in maths; list handling; mdwmath
longdesc which adds some minor changes to LaTeX maths; a rewrite of
longdesc LaTeX's tabular and array environments; verbatim handling; and
longdesc syntax diagrams.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/mdwtools
catalogue-license gpl
catalogue-topics footnote list-supp macro-supp maths notes syntax table verbatim
catalogue-version 1.05.4

name measurebox
shortdesc Precise measurements of glyphs
longdesc MeasureBox is a (plain TeX) package for measuring material. It
longdesc is intended for precise measurements of glyphs so that they can
longdesc be manipulated by other macros and packages (e.g. the Stretchy
longdesc package). Its only dependency is the pdfToolbox package, which
longdesc is currently only supported by plain-pdfTeX.
catalogue-ctan /macros/generic/measurebox
catalogue-license mit
catalogue-topics font-devel measure
catalogue-version 1.0

name mecaso
shortdesc Formulas frequently used in rigid body mechanics
longdesc This package provides a number of formulas frequently used in
longdesc rigid body mechanics. Since most of these formulas are long and
longdesc tedious to write, this package wraps them up in short commands.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/YDFTW/mecaso
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/mecaso
catalogue-license gpl3+
catalogue-topics physics
catalogue-version 1.0

name media4svg
shortdesc Multimedia inclusion for the dvisvgm backend
longdesc This package implements an interface for embedding video and
longdesc audio files in SVG (Scalable Vector Graphics) output. SVG with
longdesc embedded media is very portable, as it is supported by all
longdesc modern Web browsers across a variety of operating systems and
longdesc platforms, including portable devices. All DVI producing TeX
longdesc engines can be used. The dvisvgm utility, which is part of all
longdesc major TeX distributions, converts the intermediate DVI to SVG.
longdesc By default, media files are embedded into the SVG output to
longdesc make self-sufficient SVG files.
catalogue-contact-repository https://gitlab.com/agrahn/media4svg
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/media4svg
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics multimedia tagged-pdf-unsupported
catalogue-version 0.13

name media9
shortdesc Multimedia inclusion package with Adobe Reader-9/X compatibility
longdesc The package provides an interface to embed interactive Flash
longdesc (SWF) and 3D objects (Adobe U3D & PRC), as well as video and
longdesc sound files or streams in the popular MP4, FLV and MP3 formats
longdesc into PDF documents with Acrobat-9/X compatibility. Playback of
longdesc multimedia files uses the built-in Flash Player of Adobe Reader
longdesc and does, therefore, not depend on external plug-ins. Flash
longdesc Player supports the efficient H.264 codec for video
longdesc compression. The package is based on the RichMedia Annotation,
longdesc an Adobe addition to the PDF specification. It replaces the now
longdesc obsolete movie15 package.
catalogue-contact-repository https://gitlab.com/agrahn/media9
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/media9
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics multimedia
catalogue-version 1.30

name medmath
shortdesc Better medium-size math commands
longdesc This package started as a fork of the mediummath code of the
longdesc nccmath package, aiming to provide more stable and flexible
longdesc medium-size math commands. This concerns sizes of operators and
longdesc infinite loops caused by definite integrals.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/medmath
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics bugfix maths
catalogue-version 2025A

name medstarbeamer
shortdesc Beamer document class for MedStar Health Research Institute
longdesc This is a beamer template for MedStar Health presentations. It
longdesc includes sample presentations using both .tex files and .rnw
longdesc files. The document class is obviously compatible with both.
longdesc The advantage of the .rnw file is that it can be used with
longdesc knitr such that you can weave your R code with your
longdesc presentation.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/medstarbeamer
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics presentation statistics

name meetingmins
shortdesc Format written minutes of meetings
longdesc The class allows formatting of meeting minutes using \section
longdesc commands (which provide hierarchical structure). An agenda can
longdesc also be produced for distribution prior to the meeting, with
longdesc user-selected portions suppressed from printing.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/meetingmins
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics meeting-admin
catalogue-version 1.6

name membranecomputing
shortdesc Membrane Computing notation
longdesc This is a LaTeX package for the Membrane Computing community.
longdesc It comprises the definition of P systems, rules and some
longdesc concepts related to languages and computational complexity
longdesc usually needed for Membrane Computing research. The package
longdesc depends on ifthen and xstring.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/membranecomputing
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics comp-sci comp-theory
catalogue-version 0.2.1

name memdesign
shortdesc Notes on book design
longdesc A Few Notes on Book Design provides an introduction to the
longdesc business of book design. It is an extended version of what used
longdesc to be the first part of the memoir users' manual. Please note
longdesc that the compiled copy, supplied in the package, uses
longdesc commercial fonts; the README file contains instructions on how
longdesc to compile the document without these fonts.
catalogue-ctan /info/memdesign
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics review-document

name memexsupp
shortdesc Experimental memoir support
longdesc A package of code proposed as supporting material for memoir.
longdesc The package is intended as a test bed for such code, which may
longdesc in the fullness of time be adopted into the main memoir
longdesc release.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/memexsupp
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics test-dist
catalogue-version 0.1

name memoir
shortdesc Typeset fiction, non-fiction and mathematical books
longdesc The memoir class is for typesetting poetry, fiction,
longdesc non-fiction, and mathematical works. Permissible document base
longdesc font sizes range from 9 to 60pt. There is a range of
longdesc page-styles and well over a dozen chapter-styles to choose
longdesc from, as well as methods for specifying your own layouts and
longdesc designs. The class also provides the functionality of over
longdesc thirty of the more popular packages, thus simplifying document
longdesc sources. Users who wish to use the hyperref package, in a
longdesc document written with the memoir class, should also use the
longdesc memhfixc package (part of this bundle). Note, however, that any
longdesc current version of hyperref actually loads the package
longdesc automatically if it detects that it is running under memoir.
catalogue-also memdesign
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/memoir
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics book-pub class tagged-pdf-incompatible
catalogue-version 3.8.4b

name memoirchapterstyles
shortdesc Chapter styles in memoir class
longdesc A showcase of chapter styles available to users of memoir: the
longdesc six provided in the class itself, plus many from elsewhere (by
longdesc the present author and others). The package's resources apply
longdesc only to memoir, but the package draws from a number of sources
longdesc relating to standard classes, including the fncychap package,
longdesc and Vincent Zoonekynd's tutorial on headings.
catalogue-ctan /info/latex-samples/MemoirChapStyles
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics use-sample
catalogue-version 1.7e

name memoize
shortdesc Externalization of graphics and memoization of compilation results in general
longdesc Memoize is a package for externalization of graphics and
longdesc memoization of compilation results in general, allowing the
longdesc author to reuse the results of compilation-intensive code.
longdesc Memoize (i) induces very little overhead, as all externalized
longdesc graphics is produced in a single compilation. It features (ii)
longdesc automatic recompilation upon the change of code or
longdesc user-adjustable context, and (iii) automatic externalization of
longdesc TikZ pictures and Forest trees, easily extensible to other
longdesc commands and environments. Furthermore, Memoize (iv) supports
longdesc cross-referencing, TikZ overlays and Beamer, (v) works with all
longdesc major engines and formats, and (vi) is adaptable to any
longdesc workflow.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/sasozivanovic/memoize
catalogue-ctan /macros/generic/memoize
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics compilation cond-comp ext-code graphics macro-gen tagged-pdf-partially
catalogue-version 1.4.1

name memoize-ext
shortdesc Extended support for memoization with Memoize
longdesc Automatic handling of additional kinds of material by or during
longdesc memoization with Memoize. Provides support for memoizing
longdesc content in tagged PDFs and compatibility with ltx-talk. TikZ
longdesc pictures tagged with alt, actualtext or artifact are handled
longdesc automatically. The package supports automatic detection of
longdesc expl3 syntax zones, auto-replication of expl3 functions without
longdesc weird arguments and auto-memoization of l3draw pictures. The
longdesc code is arranged into interdependent modules so activation may
longdesc be customised at load time.
catalogue-contact-home https://codeberg.org/cfr/prooftrees
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/cfr42/prooftrees
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/memoize-ext
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics compilation cond-comp ext-code graphics pgf-tikz tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 0.4.3

