name mfb-oldstyle
shortdesc MFB Oldstyle serif fonts
longdesc MFB Oldstyle is a serif font family designed for body text.
longdesc This typeface was originally designed by Morris Fuller Benton
longdesc and released by American Type Founders in 1909 as Century
longdesc Oldstyle. The family contains four fonts: regular, italic, bold
longdesc and bold italic. All the fonts in the family have small
longdesc capitals, a choice of lining or old-style figures, as well as
longdesc superior and inferior figures. A variety of Latin scripts are
longdesc supported, as well as Greek (with full polytonic coverage).
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/dbenjaminmiller/mfb-oldstyle/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/dbenjaminmiller/mfb-oldstyle
catalogue-ctan /fonts/mfb-oldstyle
catalogue-license cc0
catalogue-topics font font-body font-greek font-otf font-proportional font-serif font-supp font-type1 tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 2.1

name mfirstuc
shortdesc Uppercase the first letter of a word
longdesc The package provides commands \makefirstuc that uppercases the
longdesc first letter in its argument (with a check for a semantic
longdesc markup command at the start of the argument), and
longdesc \xmakefirstuc, which expands the argument before uppercasing.
longdesc It also provides \capitalisewords{phrase} which applies
longdesc \makefirstuc to each word in the phrase, where the words are
longdesc separated by regular spaces. (Exceptions can be made for words
longdesc that shouldn't be converted.)
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/mfirstuc
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics macro-supp tagged-pdf text-manip
catalogue-version 2.09

name mflogo
shortdesc LaTeX support for Metafont logo fonts
longdesc LaTeX package and font definition file to access the Knuthian
longdesc mflogo fonts described in The Metafontbook and to typeset
longdesc Metafont logos in LaTeX documents.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/mflogo
catalogue-license lppl1
catalogue-topics font-supp tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 2.0

name mflogo-font
shortdesc Metafont logo font
longdesc These fonts were created in Metafont by Knuth, for his own
longdesc publications. At some stage, the letters P and S were added, so
longdesc that the MetaPost logo could also be expressed. The fonts were
longdesc originally issued (of course) as Metafont source; they have
longdesc since been autotraced and reissued in Adobe Type 1 format by
longdesc Taco Hoekwater.
catalogue-ctan /fonts/mflogo
catalogue-license knuth
catalogue-topics font font-mf font-type1
catalogue-version 1.002

name mflua
shortdesc configuration and base files for MFLua
longdesc For information on this Lua-enabled Metafont, see, for example:
longdesc tug.org/TUGboat/tb32-2/tb101scarso.pdf.

