name mintspirit
shortdesc LaTeX support for MintSpirit font families
longdesc The package provides LaTeX, pdfLaTeX, XeLaTeX and LuaLaTeX
longdesc support for the MintSpirit and MintSpiritNo2 families of fonts,
longdesc designed by Hirwen Harendal. MintSpirit was originally designed
longdesc for use as a system font on a Linux Mint system. The No. 2
longdesc variant provides more conventional shapes for some glyphs.
catalogue-contact-home https://arkandis.tuxfamily.org/adffonts.html
catalogue-ctan /fonts/mintspirit
catalogue-license ofl lppl
catalogue-topics font font-body font-otf font-proportional font-sans font-supp font-t1enc font-type1 tagged-pdf

name minutes
shortdesc Typeset the minutes of meetings
longdesc Supports the creation of a collection of minutes. Features
longdesc include: Support of tasks (who, schedule, what, time of
longdesc finishing; possibility of creating a list of open tasks;
longdesc inclusion of open tasks from other minutes; Support for
longdesc attachments; Support of schedule dates (in planning: support
longdesc for the calendar package); Different versions (secret parts);
longdesc and Macros for votes and decisions (list of decisions). Support
longdesc for minutes in German, Dutch and English is provided.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/minutes
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics meeting-admin
catalogue-version 1.8f

name mismath
shortdesc Miscellaneous mathematical macros
longdesc The package provides some mathematical macros to typeset:
longdesc mathematical constants e, i, p in upright shape (automatically)
longdesc as recommended by ISO 80000-2, vectors with nice arrows and
longdesc adjusted norm, several standard operator names, small commands
longdesc with useful aliases, tensors in sans serif bold italic shape
longdesc (ISO recommendation), improved spacings in mathematical
longdesc formulas, systems of equations and small matrices, displaymath
longdesc in double columns for lengthy calculations with short
longdesc expressions.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/mismath
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics maths
catalogue-version 3.3

name missaali
shortdesc A late medieval OpenType textura font
longdesc This package contains the free OpenType Textura font Missaali
longdesc and a style file for using it with XeLaTeX. Textura is a
longdesc typeface based on the textus quadratus form of the textualis
longdesc formata that late medieval scribes used for the most valuable
longdesc manuscripts. The font Missaali is based on Textura that German
longdesc printer Bartholomew Ghotan used for printing missals and
longdesc psalters in the 1480s. This font has two intended use cases: as
longdesc a Gothic display font; and for emulating late-medieval
longdesc manuscripts. In addition to the basic textura letters, the font
longdesc contains a large number of abbreviation sigla as well as a set
longdesc of Lombardic initials. As modern typesetting algorithms are not
longdesc intended for creating 15th century style layout, the package
longdesc contains a XeLaTeX style file that makes it easier to achieve
longdesc the classic incunabula look.
catalogue-ctan /fonts/missaali
catalogue-license ofl lppl1.3
catalogue-topics font-gothic font-medieval font-otf
catalogue-version 2.0

name mitthesis
shortdesc A LaTeX template for an MIT thesis
longdesc This class provides a LaTeX template for an MIT thesis or
longdesc dissertation formatted according to the requirements of the
longdesc Massachusetts Institute of Technology Libraries (as posted in
longdesc 2026):
longdesc https://libraries.mit.edu/distinctive-collections/thesis-specs/
longdesc This template is appropriate for an MIT thesis or MIT
longdesc dissertation of any type. This template works with either
longdesc pdfLaTeX or LuaLaTeX. The bibliography may be prepared with
longdesc biblatex/biber. The class requires TeX Live 2022 or later
longdesc distributions. This template replaces the older version of
longdesc mitthesis.cls, which was first composed in the 1980s.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/mitthesis
catalogue-license mit
catalogue-topics class dissertation doc-templ engineering humanities scientific-docs tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 1.24

name mkgrkindex
catalogue greek-makeindex
shortdesc Makeindex working with Greek
longdesc Makeindex is resolutely stuck with Latin-based alphabets, so
longdesc will not deal with Greek indexes, unaided. This package
longdesc provides a Perl script that will transmute the index of a Greek
longdesc document in such a way that makeindex will sort the entries
longdesc according to the rules of the Greek alphabet.
catalogue-ctan /language/greek/mkgrkindex
catalogue-license other-free
catalogue-topics greek index-proc
catalogue-version 2.0

