name modiagram
shortdesc Drawing molecular orbital diagrams
longdesc The package provides an environment MOdiagram and some
longdesc commands, to create molecular orbital diagrams using TikZ. For
longdesc example, the MO diagram of dihydrogen would be written as:
longdesc \begin{MOdiagram} \atom{left}{ 1s = {0;up} } \atom{right}{ 1s =
longdesc {0;up} } \molecule{ 1sMO = {1;pair, } } \end{MOdiagram} The
longdesc package also needs the l3kernel and l3packages bundles from the
longdesc LaTeX 3 experimental distribution.
catalogue-contact-repository https://bitbucket.org/cgnieder/modiagram/
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/modiagram
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics chemistry diagram
catalogue-version 0.3a

name modref
shortdesc Customisation of cross-references in LaTeX
longdesc The package contains macros which allow authors to easily
longdesc customise how cross-references appear in their document, both
longdesc in general (across all cross-references) and for particular
longdesc types of references (identified by a prefix in the reference
longdesc label), in a very generic manner.
catalogue-also refstyle
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/modref
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics label-ref
catalogue-version 1.0

name modroman
shortdesc Write numbers in lower case roman numerals
longdesc This package provides only two macros viz. \modromannumeral
longdesc which writes the number given as argument in lower case roman
longdesc numeral with a j instead of a i as the final letter of numbers
longdesc greater than 1 and \modroman{MyCounter} which writes the value
longdesc of a counter in the same way. You use the first in the same way
longdesc as the TeX primitive \romannumeral and the second as LaTeX
longdesc command \roman. The default option is vpourv with which 5 is
longdesc translated as v and option upourv with which the same 5 is
longdesc given as u.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/modroman
catalogue-license lppl1.2
catalogue-topics numbers
catalogue-version 1

name modular
shortdesc Relative section headings for modular documents
longdesc LaTeX sections have absolute depth, e.g. \section, \subsection,
longdesc etc. When composing modular documents, we want relative depths.
longdesc The coseoul package provides relative headings, but does not
longdesc get things right when composing a document modularly from
longdesc multiple parts. This package provides the missing piece.
longdesc modular relies on coseoul, import, and ifthen.
catalogue-also coseoul
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/danielsank/tex-modular/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/danielsank/tex-modular
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/modular
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics file-control headings

name modulus
shortdesc A non-destructive modulus and integer quotient operator for TeX
longdesc The package provides an easy way to take the remainder of a
longdesc division operation without destroying the values of the
longdesc counters containing the dividend and divisor. Also provides a
longdesc way to take the integer quotient of a division operation
longdesc without destroying the values of the counters containing the
longdesc dividend and divisor. A tiny but occasionally useful package,
longdesc when doing heavy TeX programming.
catalogue-ctan /macros/generic/modulus
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics calculation tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 1.0

name mohe-book
shortdesc Typeset authored, translated, and research books according to mohe rules
longdesc The mohe-book LaTeX class is a specialized template designed to
longdesc streamline the typesetting of academic and educational
longdesc materials, including authored textbooks, translated works,
longdesc research publications, and course materials. Tailored for
longdesc faculty members and academic staff in Afghanistan, it adheres
longdesc to rigorous scholarly standards while offering customizable
longdesc layouts for bilingual (e.g., Dari-English) or multilingual
longdesc content. Key features include preconfigured chapter/section
longdesc styles, support for complex scripts, and templates for front
longdesc matter (prefaces, dedications) and back matter (bibliographies,
longdesc indices). The package aims to simplify the creation of
longdesc professional-grade academic documents, ensuring consistency and
longdesc compliance with institutional or regional publishing
longdesc guidelines.
catalogue-ctan /macros/xetex/latex/mohe-book
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics book-pub class doc-templ persian
catalogue-version 1.0.0

name mohelper
shortdesc Draw fully customizeable MO diagrams
longdesc This is a package to draw fully customizable MO (molecular
longdesc orbital) diagrams. The package comes with the mohelper
longdesc environment and many other commands to create an MO diagram.
longdesc The diagram is created using TikZ. See the manual for further
longdesc information and use the interactive webhelper
longdesc (https://thevicraft.github.io/modiagram-latex-integration/).
