catalogue-contact-home https://puszcza.gnu.org.ua/projects/muling
catalogue-contact-repository https://git.gnu.org.ua/muling.git
catalogue-contact-support mailto:muling-help@gnu.org.ua
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/muling
catalogue-license gpl3+ fdl
catalogue-topics class linguistic
catalogue-version 0.5

name multenum
shortdesc Multi-column enumerated lists
longdesc Defines an environment multienumerate, that produces an
longdesc enumerated array in which columns are vertically aligned on the
longdesc counter. The motivation was lists of answers for a text book,
longdesc where there are many rather small items; the multienumerate
longdesc environment goes some way to making such lists look neater.
catalogue-also shortlst paralist
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/multenum
catalogue-license lppl1
catalogue-topics list list-enum tagged-pdf-incompatible

name multi-sudoku
shortdesc Create and customise Sudoku grids of various sizes
longdesc This package provides tools for typesetting Sudoku grids of
longdesc various sizes in LaTeX. Unlike other Sudoku packages which are
longdesc typically limited to the standard 9x9 layout, this package
longdesc supports a broad range of grid sizes - from trivial 1x1 puzzles
longdesc to extended 49x49 Sudokus - that's the limit for now! Grids are
longdesc drawn with our sudoku environment, which is based on using
longdesc LaTeX's native tabular environment. We include intuitive
longdesc options to control dimensions, font size, and grid thickness.
longdesc Entries in the grid are inserted as in a regular table, thus
longdesc making it simple to create, customise, and fill Sudoku puzzles
longdesc manually.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/multi-sudoku
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics games sudoku
catalogue-version 1.00

name multiaudience
shortdesc Several versions of output from the same source
longdesc This package allows to generate several versions of the same
longdesc document for different audiences.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/multiaudience
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics cond-comp tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 1.04

name multibbl
shortdesc Multiple bibliographies
longdesc The package multibbl redefines the standard bibliographic
longdesc commands so that one can generate multiple reference sections.
longdesc Each section has it own auxiliary file (for use with BibTeX)
longdesc and title.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/multibbl
catalogue-license lppl1
catalogue-topics bibtex-multi bibtex-supp
catalogue-version 1.1

name multibib
shortdesc Multiple bibliographies within one document
longdesc The package the creation of references to multiple
longdesc bibliographies within one document. It thus provides
longdesc complementary functionality to packages like bibunits and
longdesc chapterbib, which allow the creation of one bibliography for
longdesc multiple, but different parts of the document. Multibib is
longdesc compatible with inlinebib, natbib, and koma-script.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/multibib
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics bibtex-multi bibtex-supp tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 1.4

name multibibliography
shortdesc Multiple versions of a bibliography, with different sort orders
longdesc Conventional standards for bibliography styles impose a forced
longdesc choice between index and name/year citations, and corresponding
longdesc references. The package avoids this choice, by providing
longdesc alphabetic, sequenced, and even chronological orderings of
longdesc references. Inline citations, that integrate these
longdesc heterogeneous styles, are also supported (and work with other
longdesc bibliography packages).
catalogue-also nmbib
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/multibibliography
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics bibtex-supp tagged-pdf-incompatible
catalogue-version 1.03

