longdesc Nanum is a unicode font designed especially for Korean-language
longdesc script. The font was designed by Sandoll Communication and
longdesc Fontrix; it includes the sans serif (gothic), serif (myeongjo),
longdesc pen script and brush script typefaces. The package provides
longdesc Type1 subfonts converted from Nanum Myeongjo (Regular and
longdesc ExtraBold) and Nanum Gothic (Regular and Bold) OTFs. C70, LUC,
longdesc T1, and TS1 font definition files are also provided. (The
longdesc package does not include OpenType/TrueType files, which are
longdesc available from Naver)
