name optidef
shortdesc Environments for writing optimization problems
longdesc This small library provides a standard set of environments for
longdesc writing optimization problems. It automatically aligns the
longdesc problems in three points with an optional fourth: Beginning of
longdesc the words minimize/argmin and subject to The objective function
longdesc and the longest left hand side of the constraints. The $= | > |
longdesc <$ signs of the constraints. Optionally, the user can add
longdesc manually a double align character && to align some common
longdesc constraints feature. A clear example could be the constraints
longdesc names, e.g. (boundary constraint) alignment with (dynamic
longdesc constraint). Furthermore, it provides an easy interface to
longdesc define optimization problem for three different reference
longdesc situations: Where no equation is referenced/numbered. Where the
longdesc problem is referenced with a single number. Where each equation
longdesc has an individual reference. Finally, it also allows a
longdesc definition of any optimization problem without a limitless
longdesc number of constraints.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/jeslago/optidef/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/jeslago/optidef
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/optidef
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics maths tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 3.1

name optikz
shortdesc Customizable optical components for drawing laser setups and optical systems using TikZ
longdesc This package provides a collection of TikZ-based commands for
longdesc drawing laser setups and optical systems. It includes
longdesc components such as lenses, mirrors, beamsplitters, cameras,
longdesc spectrometers, detectors and more. Each element is highly
longdesc customizable through optional key-value arguments (e.g. angle,
longdesc width, thickness, color). Furthermore, rainbow and single color
longdesc beams can be drawn to visualize beam size and dispersion in
longdesc e.g. stretcher-compressor setups.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/Tatze99/optikz
catalogue-ctan /graphics/pgf/contrib/optikz
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics graphics-in-tex optics pgf-tikz physics
catalogue-version 1.1.0

name optional
shortdesc Facilitate optional printing of parts of a document
longdesc Optional provides simple, flexible, optional compilation of
longdesc LaTeX documents. Option switches may be given via package
longdesc options, by the \UseOption command, or interactively via the
longdesc \AskOption command (help text may be provided, by defining the
longdesc \ExplainOptions command). The package is not robust, in the way
longdesc that comment package is, against ill-behaved text. In
longdesc particular, verbatim text may not be directly included in
longdesc optional sections (whether they're included or not).
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/optional
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics cond-comp editorial tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 2.2b

name options
shortdesc Provides convenient key-value options for LaTeX package writers
longdesc The options package provides easy to use key-value options for
longdesc LaTeX package writers. It has a similar interface as pgfkeys
longdesc with path options but comes with more built-in data types and
longdesc more convenient support for families and searching.
catalogue-also keyval pgfkeys xkeyval
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/options
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics keyval
catalogue-version 1.0

name orbitals
shortdesc Atomic subshell / orbital-box diagrams for LaTeX, with automatic electron filling following Hund's rule and the Pauli principle
longdesc orbitals draws the familiar box-and-arrow notation for atomic
longdesc subshells (s, p, d, f). You give only the principal quantum
longdesc number, the subshell letter and the number of electrons; the
longdesc package fills the boxes automatically (one spin-up arrow per
longdesc box first, then pairing), reproducing the high-spin free-atom
longdesc ground state. It can draw: a single subshell (suborbital) a row
longdesc of subshells (electronconfig) a valence configuration with a
longdesc noble-gas core (atomconfig) an empty transition-series template
longdesc (transitionseries) Every diagram can be scaled and placed
longdesc inline in running text. Colours, box size, spacing and arrow
longdesc shape are configurable.
catalogue-ctan /graphics/pgf/contrib/orbitals
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics chemistry diagram pgf-tikz physics
catalogue-version 1.0

