name printcolormanager
shortdesc Automated color model management (CMYK, RGB, Gray) for print and digital
longdesc The printColorManager package provides a robust and automated
longdesc workflow for handling color models in LaTeX documents. It is
longdesc designed for users who need to output the same document for
longdesc different media, such as CMYK for professional printing, RGB
longdesc for screen/web viewing, and grayscale for black-and-white
longdesc printing. Built on top of the xcolor package, it introduces a
longdesc unified macro (\definePrintColor) that allows users to
longdesc explicitly set exact values for CMYK, RGB, and Gray for their
longdesc custom brand colors, overriding automated and often inaccurate
longdesc mathematical conversions. It also features built-in definitions
longdesc for typographic Pure Black and background Rich Black to ensure
longdesc professional prepress quality.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/printcolormanager
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics colour prepress print-app
catalogue-version 1.0

name printfilelist
shortdesc Print a list of the files used by the current document
longdesc This package provides two commands for inspecting the files
longdesc used by the current document. \printfilelist lists the files
longdesc together with their version information, with an optional name
longdesc filter and a starred form that produces a compact,
longdesc comma-separated inline list. \ispackageloaded reports whether a
longdesc given package is loaded, and its version if so. The package
longdesc requires nothing beyond the LaTeX kernel.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/gaksaray/printfilelist/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/gaksaray/printfilelist
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/printfilelist
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics doc-debug doc-mgmt
catalogue-version 1.1.0

name printlen
shortdesc Print lengths using specified units
longdesc \printlength{length} prints the value of a LaTeX length in the
longdesc units specified by \uselengthunit{unit} (unit may be any TeX
longdesc length unit except for scaled point, viz., any of: pt, pc, in,
longdesc mm, cm, bp, dd or cc). When the unit is pt, the printed length
longdesc value will include any stretch or shrink; otherwise these are
longdesc not printed. The unit argument may also be PT, in which case
longdesc length values will be printed in point units but without any
longdesc stretch or shrink values.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/LaTeX-Package-Repositories/herries-press
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/printlen
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics debug-supp doc-debug tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 1.1a

