name pronunciation
shortdesc American English Pronunciation
longdesc This style file is designed for automatically typing phonetic
longdesc symbols in American English. The system supports as many as
longdesc 21,082 English words all told. The main packages used in
longdesc pronunciation.sty are ifthen, xparse and tipa.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/pronunciation
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics linguistic phonetic
catalogue-version 1.0.2

name proof-at-the-end
shortdesc A package to move proofs to appendix
longdesc This package aims to provide a way to easily move proofs to the
longdesc appendix. You can (among other things) move proofs to different
longdesc places/sections, create links from theorems to proofs, restate
longdesc theorems, add comments in appendix...
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/leo-colisson/proof-at-the-end/issues
catalogue-contact-home https://github.com/leo-colisson/proof-at-the-end
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/proof-at-the-end
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics appendix maths proof

name proofgraph
shortdesc Dependency graphs of the results of mathematical articles
longdesc The proofgraph package automatically produces a graph of the
longdesc dependencies between the results (theorems, lemmas,
longdesc propositions, and so on) of a mathematical article. It requires
longdesc no manual annotation: an edge from one result to another is
longdesc inferred whenever the proof of the former refers to the latter
longdesc through an ordinary cross-reference (\ref, \cref, \autoref,
longdesc \eqref, and similar), with a manual \uses command also
longdesc available for dependencies not expressed through a visible
longdesc reference. Citations of external work can optionally be
longdesc captured as well. The package writes a Graphviz .dot file
longdesc describing the graph; with shell-escape enabled it can
longdesc additionally run Graphviz and embed the rendered graph into the
longdesc document. Nodes can be styled according to the type of result,
longdesc self-loops removed, specific citations suppressed, and chosen
longdesc nodes excluded.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/PierreSenellart/proofgraph
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/proofgraph
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics diagram-maths label-ref maths-theorem proof
catalogue-version 1.2.0

name proofread
shortdesc Commands for inserting annotations
longdesc This package defines a few LaTeX commands that may be useful
longdesc when you proofread a LaTeX document. They allow you to easily
longdesc highlight text and add comments in the margin. Vim escape
longdesc sequences are provided for inserting or removing these LaTeX
longdesc commands in the source. Options are provided for displaying the
longdesc document with extra line spacing, and for displaying it in
longdesc either corrected or uncorrected state, both without margin
longdesc notes. The package is based on code for a text highlighting
longdesc command that was published by Antal Spector-Zabusky on
longdesc https://tex.stackexchange.com/questions/5959. The main file,
longdesc proofread.dtx, is self-extracting, so you can generate the
longdesc style file by compiling proofread.dtx with pdfLaTeX. This
longdesc package is based on the soul package; so if you plan to
longdesc highlight non-ASCII characters, you must compile your source
longdesc with either XeTeX- or LuaTeX-based compilers.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/proofread
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics decoration editorial
catalogue-version 1.04

name prooftrees
shortdesc Forest-based proof trees (symbolic logic)
longdesc The package supports drawing proof trees of the kind often used
longdesc in introductory logic classes, especially those aimed at
longdesc students without strong mathematical backgrounds. Hodges (1991)
longdesc is one example of a text which uses this system. When teaching
longdesc such a system it is especially useful to annotate the tree with
longdesc line numbers, justifications and explanations of branch
longdesc closures. prooftrees provides a single environment, prooftree,
longdesc and a variety of tools for annotating, customising and
longdesc highlighting such trees. A cross-referencing system is provided
longdesc for trees which cite line numbers in justifications for proof
longdesc lines or branch closures. prooftrees is based on forest and,
longdesc hence, TikZ. The package requires version 2.1+ of forest for
longdesc expected results. It will not work with versions prior to 2.1.
catalogue-also forest
catalogue-contact-repository https://codeberg.org/cfr/prooftrees
catalogue-ctan /graphics/pgf/contrib/prooftrees
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics logic pgf-tikz tagged-pdf tree
catalogue-version 0.9.3

name properties
shortdesc Load properties from a file
longdesc The package loads properties (key, value) from a properties
longdesc file, e.g. \jobname.properties.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/properties
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics macro-supp
catalogue-version 0.2

name proposal
shortdesc A set of LaTeX classes for preparing proposals for collaborative projects
longdesc The process of preparing a collaborative proposal, to a major
longdesc funding body, involves integration of contributions of a many
longdesc people at many sites. It is therefore an ideal application for
longdesc a text-based document preparation system such as LaTeX, in
longdesc concert with a distributed version control system such as SVN.
longdesc The proposal class itself provides a basis for such an
longdesc enterprise. The dfgproposal and dfgproposal classes provide two
longdesc specialisations of the base class for (respectively) German and
longdesc European research proposals. The packages depend on the
longdesc author's stex bundle.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/KWARC/LaTeX-proposal
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/proposal
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics proposal

name propositions
shortdesc Typeset and cross-reference named and numbered propositions
longdesc A LaTeX package for typesetting and cross-referencing named and
longdesc numbered displayed propositions (examples, theses,
longdesc premises...). Cross-references can include customizable
longdesc formatting; the appearance of proposition labels and
longdesc cross-references is controlled by a flexible key-value
longdesc interface.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/ciandorr/propositions/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/ciandorr/propositions
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/propositions
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics humanities label-ref maths-theorem
catalogue-version 0.91

name prosper
shortdesc LaTeX class for high quality slides
longdesc Prosper is a LaTeX class for writing transparencies. It is
longdesc written as an extension of the seminar class by Timothy Van
longdesc Zandt. Prosper offers a friendly environment for creating
longdesc slides for both presentations with an overhead projector and a
longdesc video projector. Slides prepared for a presentation with a
longdesc computer and a video projector may integrate animation effects,
longdesc incremental display, and so on. Various visual styles are
longdesc supported (including some that mimic PowerPoint) and others are
longdesc being contributed.
catalogue-also ifmslide ha-prosper
catalogue-contact-repository https://prosper.sourceforge.net/
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/prosper
catalogue-license lppl1.2
catalogue-topics presentation tagged-pdf-unsupported
catalogue-version 1.0h

name protex
shortdesc Literate programming package
longdesc ProTeX is a simple but powerful literate programming tool,
longdesc which is designed to generate useful hypertext output (either
longdesc PDF, or HTML using TeX4ht).
catalogue-ctan /web/protex
catalogue-license lppl1
catalogue-topics litprog

name protocol
shortdesc A class for minutes of meetings
longdesc The present version of the class supports German meeting
longdesc minutes including vote results and action items. The author has
longdesc ambitions to internationalise the code, and would welcome
longdesc support in the work.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/protocol
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics meeting-admin
catalogue-version 1.13

name prtec
shortdesc A template for PRTEC conference papers
longdesc This package provides a LaTeX class, a BibTeX style, and a
longdesc LaTeX template to format conference papers for the Pacific Rim
longdesc Thermal Engineering Conference (PRTEC). The .tex and .cls files
longdesc are commented and should be self-explanatory. The package
longdesc depends on newtx.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/prtec
catalogue-license mit
catalogue-topics bibtex-supp class confproc doc-templ engineering scientific-docs
catalogue-version 1.07

name przechlewski-book
shortdesc Examples from Przechlewski's LaTeX book
longdesc The bundle provides machine-readable copies of the examples
longdesc from the book Praca magisterska i dyplomowa z programem LaTeX.
catalogue-ctan /info/examples/przechlewski-book-examples
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics book-ex

name ps2eps
shortdesc Produce Encapsulated PostScript from PostScript
longdesc Produce Encapsulated PostScript Files (EPS/EPSF) from a
longdesc one-page PostScript document, or any PostScript document. A
longdesc correct Bounding Box is calculated for the EPS files and some
longdesc PostScript command sequences that can produce erroneous results
longdesc on printers are filtered. The input is cropped to include just
longdesc the image contained in the PostScript file. The EPS files can
longdesc then be included into TeX documents. Other programs like
longdesc ps2epsi (a script distributed with ghostscript) don't always
longdesc calculate the correct bounding box (because the values are put
longdesc on the PostScript stack which may get corrupted by bad
longdesc PostScript code) or they round it off, resulting in clipping
longdesc the image. Therefore ps2eps uses a resolution of 144 dpi to get
longdesc the correct bounding box. The bundle includes binaries for
longdesc Linux, Solaris, Digital Unix or Windows 2000/9x/NT; for other
longdesc platforms, the user needs perl, ghostscript and an ANSI-C
longdesc compiler. Included in the distribution is the bbox program, an
longdesc application to produce Bounding Box values for rawppm or rawpbm
longdesc format files.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/roland-bless/ps2eps
catalogue-ctan /support/ps2eps
catalogue-license gpl
catalogue-topics ps-manip
catalogue-version 1.72

