catalogue-ctan /graphics/pgf/contrib/quantikz
catalogue-license cc-by-4
catalogue-topics diagram-circ graphics pgf-tikz tagged-pdf-incompatible
catalogue-version 1.0.1

name quantum-chemistry-bonn
shortdesc Use consistent typesetting for quantum chemistry related software
longdesc This package gives access to several commands related to
longdesc quantum chemistry. This includes consistent formatting of names
longdesc of QC programs, as well as methods such as density functionals.
longdesc Furthermore, units of energy are set, and easy-to-use commands
longdesc are provided. Lastly, the corporate design colors of the
longdesc University of Bonn are defined.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/chselz/quantum-chemistry-bonn/issues
catalogue-contact-development https://github.com/chselz/quantum-chemistry-bonn/pulls
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/chselz/quantum-chemistry-bonn/
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/quantum-chemistry-bonn
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics chemistry scientific-docs
catalogue-version 0.2.0

name quantumarticle
shortdesc Document class for submissions to the Quantum journal
longdesc This package provides the preferred document class for papers
longdesc to be submitted to Quantum - the open journal of quantum
longdesc science. It is based on the widely used article document class
longdesc and designed to allow a seamless transition from documents
longdesc typeset with the article, revtex4-1, and elsarticle document
longdesc classes. As a service to authors, the document class comes with
longdesc a predefined bibilography style quantum.bst that is optimized
longdesc to be used with the quantumarticle document class.
longdesc Additionally, the quantumview documentclass is provided, which
longdesc can be used as a proxy to typeset the HTML-only editorial
longdesc pieces in Quantum Views in a LaTeX editor. The quantumarticle
longdesc document class also offers an option to remove the
longdesc Quantum-related branding. In that way, users appreciating the
longdesc esthetics of this document class can use it for their notes as
longdesc well.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/quantum-journal/quantum-journal/issues
catalogue-contact-home https://quantum-journal.org
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/quantum-journal/quantum-journal
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/quantumarticle
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics class journalpub physics
catalogue-version 6.1

name quantumcubemodel
shortdesc Representation of quantum states in the quantum cube model
longdesc This package provides simple LaTeX commands to draw intuitive
longdesc cube-based diagrams for quantum states of one, two, or three
longdesc qubits. Inspired by Prof. B. Just's educational framework, it
longdesc supports amplitude-phase notation, gate transition
longdesc visualizations (Hadamard, Pauli, CNOT, Toffoli). The package is
longdesc ideal for teaching and documenting small quantum circuits.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/CedricSchacht/quantumcubemodel/issues
catalogue-contact-development https://github.com/cedricschacht/quantumcubemodel
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/cedricschacht/quantumcubemodel
catalogue-ctan /graphics/pgf/contrib/quantumcubemodel
catalogue-license mit
catalogue-topics comp-sci graphics pgf-tikz
catalogue-version 0.2.1

name quattrocento
shortdesc LaTeX support for Quattrocento and Quattrocento Sans
longdesc The package provides LaTeX, pdfLaTeX, XeLaTeX and LuaLaTeX
longdesc support for the Quattrocento and Quattrocento Sans families of
longdesc fonts, designed by Pablo Impallari; the fonts themselves are
longdesc also provided, in both TrueType and Type1 format. Quattrocento
longdesc is a classic typeface with wide and open letterforms, and great
longdesc x-height, which makes it very legible for body text at small
longdesc sizes. Tiny details that only show up at bigger sizes make it
longdesc also great for display use. Quattrocento Sans is the perfect
longdesc sans-serif companion for Quattrocento.
catalogue-ctan /fonts/quattrocento
catalogue-license ofl lppl
catalogue-topics font font-body font-proportional font-sans font-serif font-supp font-t1enc font-ttf font-type1 tagged-pdf

name query-astro
shortdesc Querying astronomical databases in LaTeX
longdesc The query-astro package is an experimental package developed to
longdesc allow users to query astronomical databases directly from
longdesc LaTeX. The query is performed by sending ADQL (Astronomical
longdesc Data Query Language) instructions to a Table Access Protocol
longdesc (TAP) service, so enabled \write18 is required. The result is
longdesc then stored in a macro, which can be used in the document.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/TeXackers/query-astro/tree/main
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/query-astro
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics astronomy data-import
catalogue-version 0.1.0

name quickderivs
shortdesc Typeset derivatives and differentials with minimal input
longdesc This is a small LaTeX package containing macros allowing one to
longdesc typeset mathematical derivatives quickly, similar to esdiff.
catalogue-also diffcoeff
catalogue-contact-announce https://github.com/ljtpetersen/quickderivs/releases
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/ljtpetersen/quickderivs/issues
catalogue-contact-development https://github.com/ljtpetersen/quickderivs
