catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics graphics-in-tex tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 1

name runcode
shortdesc Execute foreign source code and embed the result in the pdf file
longdesc This LaTeX package executes programming source codes (including
longdesc all command line tools) from within LaTeX and embeds the output
longdesc in the resulting .pdf file. Many programming languages can be
longdesc easily used and any command-line executable can be invoked when
longdesc preparing the .pdf file from a .tex file. It is however
longdesc recommended to use this package in server-mode together with
longdesc the Python talk2stat package. Currently, this server-mode
longdesc supports Julia, MatLab, Python, and R. More languages will be
longdesc added. For more details and usage examples, refer to the
longdesc package's github repository.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/Ossifragus/runcode
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/runcode
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics callback exec-foreign
catalogue-version 2.6.2

name runtexfile
shortdesc Automate the process of compiling (La)TeX documents with index, bibliography, ...
longdesc This package provides a small script like latexmk to run a TeX
longdesc or LaTeX document controlled from within the document itself.
longdesc The commands have to be defined at the beginning of the
longdesc document, e.g.: %! HV lualatex --shell-escape %! HV biber %! HV
longdesc lualatex --shell-escape %! HV xindex %! HV xindex --config DIN2
longdesc -l DE -o test2.vwd %! HV xindex --config DIN2 -l DE -o
longdesc test2.dbd %! HV lualatex --shell-escape %! HV lualatex
longdesc --shell-escape \documentclass[...]{...} ... The script itself
longdesc does not parse the log file.
catalogue-ctan /support/runtexfile
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics compilation
catalogue-version 0.06

