name runtexshebang
shortdesc A Lua script running LaTeX document files with TeX-style shebang
longdesc In short, a TeX-style shebang (%#!) is a special kind of TeX
longdesc comment that you include in your TeX/LaTeX document file to
longdesc tell the operating system's shell how to run the file for the
longdesc rest of the file: %#!lualatex foo.tex \documentclass{article}
longdesc \begin{document} Hello, {\LaTeX} World! Happy {\TeX}ing.
longdesc \end{document} If you are using a TeX-style shebang, it must
longdesc appear on the line that matched 20 lines or less in your LaTeX
longdesc document, and it has to start with a TeX comment symbol (%)
longdesc followed by a hash sign (#) and an exclamation mark (!),
longdesc colloquially known as the bang, hence the name shebang for
longdesc TeX/LaTeX.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/munepi/runtexshebang/issues
catalogue-contact-home https://github.com/munepi/runtexshebang
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/munepi/runtexshebang.git
catalogue-ctan /support/runtexshebang
catalogue-license mit
catalogue-topics compilation
catalogue-version 0.5

