name skull
shortdesc A font to draw a skull
longdesc The font (defined in Metafont) defines a single character, a
longdesc black solid skull. A package is supplied to make this character
longdesc available as a symbol in maths mode.
catalogue-ctan /fonts/skull
catalogue-license gpl
catalogue-topics font font-mf font-novelty tagged-pdf-partially
catalogue-version 0.1

name slantsc
shortdesc Access different-shaped small-caps fonts
longdesc This package enables the use of small capitals in different
longdesc font shapes, e.g., slanted or bold slanted for all fonts that
longdesc provide appropriate font shapes. (Note that a separate .fd file
longdesc is needed to define font shapes such as scsl or scit.)
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/slantsc
catalogue-license lppl1
catalogue-topics font-supp tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 2.11

name slideshow
shortdesc Generate slideshow with MetaPost
longdesc The package provides a means of creating presentations in
longdesc MetaPost, without intervention from other utilities (except a
longdesc distiller). Such an arrangement has its advantages (though
longdesc there are disadvantages too).
catalogue-ctan /graphics/metapost/contrib/macros/slideshow
catalogue-license other-free
catalogue-topics presentation
catalogue-version 1.0

name slixte
shortdesc A customizable class for creating slides
longdesc This class creates customizable slides and is mostly powered by
longdesc the beamer class and the tikz package.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/slixte
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics class presentation

name smalltableof
shortdesc Create listoffigures etc. in a single chapter
longdesc The package allows you to create a list of figures and list of
longdesc tables in a chapter named List that contains separate sections
longdesc for each list of figures, tables, etc.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/smalltableof
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics toc-etc

name smart-eqn
shortdesc Automatic math symbol styling for LaTeX documents
longdesc In LaTeX typesetting, one usually needs to use different
longdesc variants of a math symbol to clarify the meanings. For example,
longdesc in linear algebra literature, it is common to use boldfaced
longdesc symbols to represent vectors, and normal symbols to represent
longdesc scalars. However, applying these variants by typing \mathbf,
longdesc \mathrm commands manually can be daunting. This package aims to
longdesc provide an automatic and customizable approach for math symbol
longdesc styling which eliminates the need to enter style commands
longdesc repeatedly.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/xziyue/smart-eqn
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/smart-eqn
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics maths maths-symbol
catalogue-version 1.0

name smartdiagram
shortdesc Generate diagrams from lists
longdesc The package will create smart diagrams from lists of items, for
longdesc simple documents and for presentations.
catalogue-ctan /graphics/pgf/contrib/smartdiagram
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics diagram pgf-tikz
catalogue-version 0.3b

name smartnotes
shortdesc Visually anchored margin notes with connector lines and dynamic placement
longdesc This package provides margin notes that automatically choose
longdesc the left or right margin based on the note position, so
longdesc connector lines remain as short and direct as possible. Its
longdesc main focus is clear visual anchoring: notes can point precisely
longdesc to the relevant place in a sentence while avoiding
longdesc unnecessarily long cross-page margin lines. The package also
longdesc supports forced side placement, basic overlap avoidance,
longdesc selectable box shapes, and an easy global disable option for
longdesc drafting.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/smartnotes
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics marginal notes pgf-tikz
catalogue-version 0.1

name smartref
shortdesc Extend LaTeX's \ref capability
longdesc The package extends the LaTeX labelling system: whenever a
longdesc label is set, the values of counters (selected by the user) are
longdesc recorded, along with the label. The value of these counters can
longdesc be recalled with a command similar to \pageref. The package
longdesc also adds commands \s[name]ref (for each counter [name] that
longdesc the user has selected); these commands display something only
longdesc if the value of the [name] counter is changed from when the
longdesc label was set. Many commands are provided to serve as a macro
longdesc programming environment for using the extended labels.
catalogue-also zref
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/smartref
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics counter-mgmt label-ref tagged-pdf-partially
catalogue-version 1.9

name smartunits
shortdesc Converting between common metric and Imperial units
longdesc This LaTeX package implements a \SmartUnit macro for converting
longdesc between (some) metric and Imperial units. The package requires
longdesc pgfkeys and siunitx.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/smartunits
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics misc-conv units
catalogue-version 1.2

name smflatex
shortdesc Classes for Societe mathematique de France publications
longdesc The Societe mathematique de France provides a set of classes,
longdesc packages and BibTeX styles that are used in its publications.
longdesc They are based on AMS classes (whose code is sometimes
longdesc recopied) and mainly upward-compatible. Their main features
longdesc are: quite different design; new environments for typesetting
longdesc some information in two languages (altabstract, alttitle,
longdesc altkeywords); if necessary, use of babel (option frenchb) and
longdesc deactivation of some features of frenchb. Includes smfart.cls,
longdesc smfbook.cls, smfplain.bst, smfalpha.bst, amongst others.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/smflatex
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics french journalpub
catalogue-version 1.6

name smileghost
shortdesc A smiling ghost symbol
longdesc This package provides a smiling ghost symbol for LaTeX. The
longdesc artwork is encoded as vector paths using the standard pict2e
longdesc package.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/diracdeltafunk/smileghost/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/diracdeltafunk/smileghost/
catalogue-contact-support https://github.com/diracdeltafunk/smileghost/issues
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/smileghost
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics graphics-symb novelty
catalogue-version 1.0.0

name snapshot
shortdesc List the external dependencies of a LaTeX document
longdesc The snapshot package helps the owner of a LaTeX document obtain
longdesc a list of the external dependencies of the document, in a form
longdesc that can be embedded at the top of the document. It provides a
longdesc snapshot of the current processing context of the document,
longdesc insofar as it can be determined from inside LaTeX. If a
longdesc document contains such a dependency list, then it becomes
longdesc possible to arrange that the document be processed always with
longdesc the same versions of everything, in order to ensure the same
longdesc output. This could be useful for someone wanting to keep a
longdesc LaTeX document on hand and consistently reproduce an identical
longdesc DVI file from it, on the fly; or for someone wanting to shield
longdesc a document during the final stages of its production cycle from
longdesc unexpected side effects of routine upgrades to the TeX system.
catalogue-also bundledoc
catalogue-contact-home https://www.ams.org/arc/resources/snapshot-about.html
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/snapshot
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics archival file-mgmt tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 2.14

name snaptodo
shortdesc A todo that snaps to the closer side
longdesc This package is an alternative to todonotes, from which it
longdesc differs in the following ways: Depending on where you call
longdesc \snaptodo, the note is put in the left or the right margin,
longdesc whichever is closer. The notes bump each other so they never
longdesc overlap; the lines never overlap either. Aesthetic and
longdesc customizable style.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/Symbol1/snaptodo/issues
catalogue-contact-development https://www.symbol.codes
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/Symbol1/snaptodo
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/snaptodo
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics editorial notes

name sneaker
shortdesc Configurable Sneakers with TikZ
longdesc The sneaker package provides a TikZ pic for drawing stylized
longdesc sneakers in an isometric-like perspective. The illustration is
longdesc highly configurable via a simple key-value interface, allowing
longdesc users to customize colors, shoelaces, velcro straps, decorative
longdesc patterns (like bolts or stars), stitching details, and even
longdesc inline-skate wheels. It is ideal for presentations, feature
longdesc model illustrations, or as a visual gimmick in LaTeX documents.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/Aargon06/sneaker/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/Aargon06/sneaker
catalogue-ctan /graphics/pgf/contrib/sneaker
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics decoration pgf-tikz
catalogue-version 1.1

name snotez
shortdesc Typeset notes, in the margin
longdesc The package provides a macro \sidenote, that places a note in
longdesc the margin of the document, with its baseline aligned with the
longdesc baseline in the body of the document. These sidenotes are
longdesc numbered (both in the text, and on the notes themselves). The
longdesc package loads the package etoolbox, pgfopts and marginnote.
catalogue-also sidenotes
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/cgnieder/snotez/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/cgnieder/snotez/
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/snotez
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics marginal tagged-pdf-partially
catalogue-version 0.7

name songbook
shortdesc Package for typesetting song lyrics and chord books
longdesc The package provides an all purpose songbook style. Three types
longdesc of output may be created from a single input file: words and
longdesc chords books for the musicians to play from, words only
longdesc songbooks for the congregation to sing from, and overhead
longdesc transparency masters for congregational use. The package will
longdesc also print a table of contents, an index sorted by title and
longdesc first line, and an index sorted by key, or by artist/composer.
longdesc The package attempts to handle songs in multiple keys, as well
longdesc as songs in multiple languages.
catalogue-contact-home https://rath.ca/Misc/Songbook/
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/songbook
catalogue-license lgpl2.1
catalogue-topics chords music
catalogue-version 4.5

name songproj
shortdesc Generate Beamer slideshows with song lyrics
longdesc This package, together with the Beamer class, is used to
longdesc generate slideshows with song lyrics. This is typically used in
longdesc religious services in churches equipped with a projector, for
longdesc which this package has been written, but it can be useful for
longdesc any type of singing assembly. It provides environments to
longdesc describe a song in a natural way, and formatting it into slides
longdesc with overlays. The package comes with an additional Python
longdesc script that can be used to convert plain-text song lyrics to
longdesc the expected LaTeX markup.
catalogue-contact-repository https://git.ortolo.eu/songproj.git/
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/songproj
catalogue-license bsd3
catalogue-topics music presentation verse
catalogue-version 1.2.0

name songs
shortdesc Produce song books for church or fellowship
longdesc The package provides a means of producing beautiful song books
longdesc for church or fellowship. It offers: a very easy chord-entry
longdesc syntax; multiple modes (words-only; words+chords; slides;
longdesc handouts); measure bars; guitar tablatures; automatic
longdesc transposition; scripture quotations; multiple indexes (sorted
longdesc by title, author, important lyrics, or scripture references);
longdesc and projector-style output generation, for interactive use. A
longdesc set of example documents is provided.
catalogue-also songbook
catalogue-contact-home https://songs.sourceforge.net
catalogue-contact-repository https://sourceforge.net/projects/songs
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/songs
catalogue-license gpl2
catalogue-topics chords music
catalogue-version 3.1

name sort-by-letters
shortdesc Bibliography styles for alphabetic sorting
longdesc This bundle contains several bibliography styles for separating
longdesc a document's references by the first letter of the first
longdesc author/editor in the bibliography entry. The styles are adapted
longdesc from standard ones or from natbib ones.
catalogue-also alphabib
catalogue-ctan /biblio/bibtex/contrib/sort-by-letters
catalogue-license other-free
catalogue-topics bibtex-supp

name soton
shortdesc University of Southampton-compliant slides
longdesc The bundle contains two packages: soton-palette which defines
longdesc colour-ways, and soton-beamer, which uses the colours to
longdesc produce compliant presentations.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/soton
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics presentation
catalogue-version 0.1

name soul
shortdesc Hyphenation for letterspacing, underlining, and more
longdesc The package provides hyphenable spacing out (letterspacing),
longdesc underlining, striking out, etc., using the TeX hyphenation
longdesc algorithm to find the proper hyphens automatically. It also
longdesc provides a mechanism that can be used to implement similar
longdesc tasks, that have to treat text syllable by syllable. This is
longdesc shown in two examples. This version is a merge of the original
longdesc soul package from Melchior Franz and the soulutf8 package from
longdesc Heiko Oberdiek and supports also UTF8.
catalogue-alias soulutf8
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/LaTeX-Package-Repositories/soul/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/LaTeX-Package-Repositories/soul
catalogue-ctan /macros/generic/soul
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics letterspace tagged-pdf-incompatible underline
catalogue-version 3.2

name soulpos
shortdesc A fancy means of underlining
longdesc The package combines the use of soul with the savepos mechanism
longdesc of current pdfTeX so that the user can create (almost)
longdesc arbitrary underlining and similar decorations, including rules,
longdesc leaders and even pictures (pgf, pstricks, etc.). Unlike soul
longdesc underlines, which are built by repeating small elements, here
longdesc each chunk of text to be underlined is a single element.
catalogue-contact-home https://www.texnia.com/
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/jbezos
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/soulpos
catalogue-license mit
catalogue-topics letterspace tagged-pdf-incompatible underline
catalogue-version 1.2

name soup
shortdesc Generate alphabet soup puzzles
longdesc Generate alphabet soup puzzles (aka word search puzzles), and
longdesc variations using numbers or other symbols. Provides macros to
longdesc generate an alphabet soup style puzzle (also known as word
longdesc search puzzles or find-the-word puzzles). Allow creating
longdesc numbersoup and soups with custom symbol sets.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/soup
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics cwpuzzle games puzzle
catalogue-version 1.0.2

name sourcecodepro
shortdesc Use SourceCodePro with TeX(-alike) systems
longdesc The font is an open-source Monospaced development from Adobe.
longdesc The package provides fonts (in both Adobe Type 1 and OpenType
longdesc formats) and macros supporting their use in LaTeX (Type 1) and
longdesc XeLaTeX/LuaLaTeX (OTF).
catalogue-ctan /fonts/sourcecodepro
catalogue-license ofl lppl1.3
catalogue-topics font font-mono font-otf font-sans font-t1enc font-type1 tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 2.8

name sourcesans
shortdesc Use Source Sans with TeX(-alike) systems
longdesc This package provides Source Sans for LaTeX. It includes both
longdesc Type1 and OpenType fonts and selects the latter when using
longdesc XeLaTeX or LuaLaTeX. This package used to be called
longdesc sourcesanspro and contains an alias package for backwards
