name spim-phdthesisthemes
shortdesc Classes, styles and configuration files for writing PhD dissertations
longdesc LaTeX classes, packages and configuration files for typesetting
longdesc a PhD dissertation following the SPIM doctoral school template
longdesc and recommandations. Built on top of the powerful UPmethodology
longdesc suite, it provides a professional, ready-to-use structure with
longdesc advanced formatting macros. These classes packages and
longdesc configuration files could be easily extended and adapted to the
longdesc style for your own institution. spim-phdthesisthemes is part of
longdesc the larger project TeX-templates. Note on Licensing The package
longdesc contains two distinct types of material: LaTeX source code (all
longdesc files that are under the src/ directory and any documentation
longdesc source files). University and institutions logo images (all
longdesc files under the logos/ directory). The LaTeX source code is
longdesc free software: You can redistribute it and/or modify it under
longdesc the terms of the GNU Lesser General Public License as published
longdesc by the Free Software Foundation, either version 3 of the
longdesc License, or (at your option) any later version. A copy of the
longdesc GNU Lesser General Public License (LGPLv3) is provided in the
longdesc file `LICENSE.LGPLv3`. The logo files are not licensed under
longdesc the LGPLv3. They are the property of their respective
longdesc university or institution and are included with permission for
longdesc redistribution only as part of this complete package. They may
longdesc NOT be modified, altered, or extracted and used separately
longdesc without explicit written permission from the owning university
longdesc or institution. The exact terms governing the logos are set
longdesc forth in the file logos/LICENSE.logos. By redistributing this
longdesc package, you agree to abide by those terms.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/gallandarakhneorg/tex-templates/issues
catalogue-contact-home https://www.arakhne.org/latex/tex-templates
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/gallandarakhneorg/tex-templates
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/spim-phdthesisthemes
catalogue-license lgpl3
catalogue-topics class doc-templ report-like std-conform
catalogue-version 20260508

name spix
shortdesc Yet another TeX compilation tool: simple, human readable, no option, no magic
longdesc SpiX offers a way to store information about the compilation
longdesc process for a tex file inside the tex file itself. Just write
longdesc the commands as comments in the tex files, and SpiX will
longdesc extract and run those commands. Everything is stored in the tex
longdesc file (so that you are not missing some piece of information
longdesc that is located somewhere else), in a human-readable format (no
longdesc need to know SpiX to understand it).
catalogue-contact-bugs https://framagit.org/spalax/spix/issues
catalogue-contact-home https://framagit.org/spalax/spix
