name splentinex
shortdesc Plantin-based serif font family for LaTeX
longdesc This is a serif font family designed for body text. This
longdesc typeface design was originally crated by Frank Pierpont and
longdesc Fritz Stelzer in 1913 and released by Monotype as Plantin. In
longdesc 2025, Ben Byram-Wigfield created Splentino, a new digitization
longdesc of the Plantin design, for inclusion with the music software
longdesc Dorico. Splentinex is a modified repackaging of Splentino.
