name starray
shortdesc A structured array (of properties) based on expl3
longdesc This package implements vector-like 'structures', like in 'C'
longdesc and other programming languages. So it is possible to store
longdesc information in a systematic and regular way. The provided
longdesc 'functions' are similar to the ones provided for property (or
longdesc sequence, or token) lists. The package is based on expl3 and
longdesc aimed at package authors, not end users. The name starray is an
longdesc abbreviation for structured arrays.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/alceu-frigeri/starray/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/alceu-frigeri/starray
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/starray
catalogue-license lppl1.3c agpl3
catalogue-topics package-devel
catalogue-version 2.1a

name startex
shortdesc An XML-inspired format for student use
longdesc A TeX format designed to help students write short reports and
longdesc essays. It provides the user with a suitable set of commands
longdesc for such a task. It is also more robust than plain TeX and
longdesc LaTeX.
catalogue-ctan /macros/plain/formats/startex
catalogue-license pd
catalogue-topics format
catalogue-version 1.04

name statementsp
shortdesc Theorem and proposition boxes with preview and recall functions
longdesc This package provides a convenient way to create customizable
longdesc theorem and proposition boxes using tcolorbox. Its most
longdesc distinctive feature is the automatic Preview and Recall
longdesc mechanism. By using a single command (\refcallsp), you can
longdesc display a statement box anywhere in your document. The package
longdesc automatically determines its position relative to the main
longdesc definition: if placed before, it generates a Preview box; if
longdesc placed after, it generates a Recall box. Both automatically
longdesc include hyperlinks jumping directly to the main definition.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/statementsp
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics maths-theorem
catalogue-version 1.0

name statex
shortdesc Statistics style
longdesc A package defining many macros for items of significance in
longdesc statistical presentations. An updated, but incompatible,
longdesc version of the package is available: statex2.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/statex
catalogue-license lppl1.2
catalogue-topics statistics
catalogue-version 1.6

name statex2
shortdesc Statistics style
longdesc The package defines many macros for items of significance in
longdesc statistical presentations. It represents a syntax-incompatible
longdesc upgrade of statex.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/statex2
catalogue-license lppl1.2
catalogue-topics statistics
catalogue-version 2.1

name statistics
shortdesc Compute and typeset statistics tables and graphics
longdesc The statistics package can compute and typeset statistics like
longdesc frequency tables, cumulative distribution functions (increasing
longdesc or decreasing, in frequency or absolute count domain), from the
longdesc counts of individual values, or ranges, or even the raw value
longdesc list with repetitions. It can also compute and draw a bar
longdesc diagram in case of individual values, or, when the data
longdesc repartition is known from ranges, an histogram or the
longdesc continuous cumulative distribution function. You can ask
longdesc statistics to display no result, selective results or all of
longdesc them. Similarly statistics can draw only some parts of the
longdesc graphs. Every part of the generated tables or graphics is
longdesc customizable.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://gitlab.com/frnchfrgg-latex/statistics/-/work_items
catalogue-contact-development https://gitlab.com/frnchfrgg-latex/statistics
catalogue-contact-home https://gitlab.com/frnchfrgg-latex/statistics
catalogue-contact-repository https://gitlab.com/frnchfrgg-latex/statistics
catalogue-contact-support https://gitlab.com/frnchfrgg-latex/statistics/-/work_items
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/statistics
catalogue-license gpl3+
catalogue-topics maths statistics
catalogue-version 2.2

name statistik
shortdesc Store statistics of a document
longdesc The package counts the numbers of pages per chapter, and stores
longdesc the results in a separate file; the format of the file is
longdesc selectable.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/statistik
catalogue-license gpl
catalogue-topics doc-mgmt
catalogue-version 0.03

name statmath
shortdesc A LaTeX package for simple use of statistical notation
longdesc The package offers anumber of notational conventions to be used
longdesc in applied and theoretical papers in statistics which are
longdesc currently lacking in the popular amsmath package. The seasoned
longdesc LaTeX user will see that the provided commands are simple,
longdesc almost trivial, but will hopefully offer less cluttered
longdesc preambles as well as a welcome help for novice users.
