name stdpage
shortdesc Standard pages with n lines of at most m characters each
longdesc For translations, proofreading, journal contributions etc.
longdesc standard pages are used. Those standard pages consist of a
longdesc fixed number of lines and characters per line. This package
longdesc produces pages with n lines of at most m characters each. For
longdesc instance the German Normseite: 60 lines of 30 characters each.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/stdpage
catalogue-license lppl1.2
catalogue-topics geometry
catalogue-version 0.6

name stealcaps
shortdesc Steal small capitals
longdesc This little package is mainly meant to be used when there is a
longdesc (TrueType or OpenType) font that does not provide real small
longdesc capitals. As a workaround, this package helps to borrow, or
longdesc steal, the small capitals from another font. This might also be
longdesc useful in the rare case that someone does not like the present
longdesc small capitals, and wants to change them, or likes those from
longdesc another font better. To achieve the borrowing, one only needs
longdesc to load the package and specify the name of the target font via
longdesc the from option. Package dependencies: pgfopts, iftex,
longdesc fontspec.
catalogue-contact-announce https://github.com/giannotr/stealcaps/discussions/2
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/giannotr/stealcaps/issues
catalogue-contact-development https://github.com/giannotr/stealcaps/pulls
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/giannotr/stealcaps.git
catalogue-contact-support https://github.com/giannotr/stealcaps/discussions/1
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/stealcaps
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics font-supp font-use
catalogue-version 1.1

name steinmetz
shortdesc Print Steinmetz notation
longdesc The steinmetz package provides a command for typesetting
longdesc complex numbers in the Steinmetz notation used in
longdesc electrotechnics as: <modulus>;<argument or phase inside an
longdesc angle symbol> The package makes use of pict2e.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/steinmetz
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics engineering maths tagged-pdf-partially
catalogue-version 1.0

name stellenbosch
shortdesc Thesis bundle for Stellenbosch University (legacy)
longdesc Note: This bundle should only be used for typesetting legacy
longdesc documents. For new documents, its successor stellenbosch-2 is
longdesc available. The usthesis class/style files are provided to
longdesc typeset reports, theses and dissertations that conform to the
longdesc requirements of the Engineering Faculty of the University of
longdesc Stellenbosch. The class file usthesis.cls is based on the
longdesc standard LaTeX book class, while usthesis.sty is a style file
longdesc to be loaded on top of the very powerful memoir class. Both
longdesc options give identical output, but the benefit of the using
longdesc memoir is that it has many additional command and environments
longdesc for formatting and processing of a document. Usthesis is
longdesc primarily concerned with the formatting of the front matter
longdesc such as the title page, abstract, etc. and a decent page layout
longdesc on A4 paper. It also works together with the babel package to
longdesc provide language options to typeset documents in Afrikaans or
longdesc in English. Additional packages are provided for bibliographic
longdesc matter, note title pages, lists of symbols, as well as various
longdesc graphic files for logos.
catalogue-also stellenbosch-2
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/stellenbosch
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics dissertation
catalogue-version 11a

name stellenbosch-2
shortdesc Stellenbosch University thesis bundle
longdesc Typesetting dissertations, theses and reports as well as
longdesc presentations of Stellenbosch University, South Africa. Note:
longdesc The previous version, stellenbosch, is still available for
longdesc legacy documents.
catalogue-also stellenbosch
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/stellenbosch-2
catalogue-license cc-by-4
catalogue-topics dissertation
catalogue-version 2.0

name step
shortdesc A free Times-like font
longdesc The STEP fonts are a free Times-like (i.e., Times replacement)
longdesc font family, implementing a design first created for The Times
longdesc of London in 1932. These fonts are meant to be compatible in
longdesc design with Adobe's digitization of Linotype Times, commonly
longdesc used in publishing. The fonts were forked from XITS/STIX and
longdesc Type 1 support is provided for legacy TeX engines.
catalogue-also xits
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/dbenjaminmiller/step/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/dbenjaminmiller/step
catalogue-ctan /fonts/step
