shortdesc Macros for SuperSymmetry-related work
longdesc The package provides abbreviations of longer expressions.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/susy
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics physics shortcut

name svg
shortdesc Include and extract SVG pictures in LaTeX documents
longdesc This bundle contains the two packages svg and svg-extract. The
longdesc svg package is intended for the automated integration of SVG
longdesc graphics into LaTeX documents. Therefore the capabilities
longdesc provided by Inkscape - or more precisely its command line tool
longdesc - are used to export the text within an SVG graphic to a
longdesc separate file, which is then rendered by LaTeX. For this
longdesc purpose the two commands \includesvg and \includeinkscape are
longdesc provided which are very similar to the \includegraphics command
longdesc of the graphicx package. In addition, the package svg-extract
longdesc allows the extraction of these graphics into independent files
longdesc in different graphic formats, exactly as it is rendered within
longdesc the LaTeX document, using either ImageMagick or Ghostscript.
catalogue-also svg-inkscape
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/mrpiggi/svg/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/mrpiggi/svg
catalogue-ctan /graphics/svg
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics graphics graphics-import graphics-incl tagged-pdf-partially
catalogue-version 2.02k

name svg-animate
shortdesc Generate animated SVG diagrams with TikZ
longdesc This package provides step-by-step animations for TikZ diagrams
longdesc in SVG format. The resulting animations run natively in web
longdesc browsers and do not require JavaScript or plugins. From a
longdesc single source file, both an animated SVG and a static PDF can
longdesc be generated. In the PDF output, steps may be stacked or
longdesc collapsed into a single frame. The animation model is based on
longdesc discrete steps. A TikZ picture is enclosed in \begin{animate},
longdesc material to be shown at a given step is marked with
longdesc \reveal{...}, and \animstep is used to advance to the next
longdesc step. Additional features include per-step durations,
longdesc visibility over multiple steps or step ranges, blinking
longdesc elements, one-shot or looping playback, and a \noanimate
longdesc fallback for PDF output. In SVG output, visibility changes are
longdesc implemented by means of SMIL animations with instantaneous
longdesc opacity transitions.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/renard/svg-animate/issues
catalogue-contact-development https://github.com/renard/svg-animate/pulls
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/renard/svg-animate
catalogue-ctan /graphics/pgf/contrib/svg-animate
catalogue-license agpl3
catalogue-topics graphics-motion pgf-tikz
catalogue-version 1.1

name svg-inkscape
shortdesc How to include an SVG image in LaTeX using Inkscape
longdesc The document demonstrates the use of SVG images in LaTeX
longdesc documents. Using the PDF+LaTeX output option of Inkscape, it is
longdesc possible to include SVG in documents, in which LaTeX typesets
longdesc the text. This results in uniform text style throughout the
longdesc document, including text in images; moreover, LaTeX commands
longdesc may be used in the image's text, providing such things as
longdesc mathematics and references. The document also describes how to
longdesc automate the conversion from SVG to PDF+LaTeX using Inkscape.
catalogue-also svg
catalogue-ctan /info/svg-inkscape
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics graphics-prep

