name ted
shortdesc A (primitive) token list editor
longdesc Just like sed is a stream editor, ted is a token list editor.
longdesc Actually, it is not as powerful as sed, but its main feature is
longdesc that it really works with tokens, not only characters. The ted
longdesc package provides two user macros: \Substitute and \ShowTokens.
longdesc The first is maybe the most useful: it performs substitutions
longdesc in token lists (even inside braces). The second displays each
longdesc token of the list (one per line) with its catcode (in the list,
longdesc not just the current one), and can be useful for debugging or
longdesc for TeX learners. Ted is designed to work well even if strange
longdesc tokens (that is, unusual {charcode, catcode} pairs or tokens
longdesc with a confusing meaning) occur in the list.
catalogue-also patch
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/ted
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics debug-supp
catalogue-version 1.06

