name texbytopic
shortdesc Freed version of the book TeX by Topic
longdesc An invaluable book, originally published by Addison-Wesley (who
longdesc have released their copyright - their version of the book went
longdesc out of print in the 1990s). The book describes itself as a
longdesc TeXnician's reference, and covers the way TeX (the engine)
longdesc works in as much detail as most ordinary TeX programmers will
longdesc ever need to know. A printed copy of the book, slightly
longdesc updated, may be had (for a modest price) from DANTE. The
longdesc original edition is available from Lulu. See the package home
longdesc page for details.
catalogue-contact-home https://www.eijkhout.net/tex/tex-by-topic.html
catalogue-ctan /info/texbytopic
catalogue-license fdl
catalogue-topics book-src ref-latex tut-plaintex

name texchanges
shortdesc LaTeX-native track changes for human and AI-assisted review
longdesc This package provides explicit tracked-change markup for LaTeX
longdesc and Overleaf. It supports additions, removals, replacements,
longdesc highlights, comments, authors, stable change IDs, decision
longdesc statuses, filtered review reports, localization, visual
longdesc presets, and an opt-in compatibility layer for the changes
longdesc package. Native replacement commands use the readable
longdesc old-to-new argument order. The distribution also includes, the
longdesc standard-library Python tool texchanges-merge for accepting,
longdesc rejecting, filtering, and permanently resolving marked changes.
catalogue-contact-announce https://github.com/phucnht/texchanges/releases
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/phucnht/texchanges/issues
catalogue-contact-development https://github.com/phucnht/texchanges/pulls
