name tikz-chemlab
shortdesc A TikZ-based reimplementation for drawing chemical laboratory glassware
longdesc This package provides macros for drawing a variety of devices
longdesc used mainly for chemical applications. Since most of these
longdesc devices have a standardised design, tikz-chemlab spares you the
longdesc trouble of having to create them manually. All basic objects
longdesc are included in the file tikz-chemlabObj.tex and are loaded
longdesc during the start of the package. tikz-chemlab works with any
longdesc LaTeX engine that supports TikZ. No PostScript dependency. No
longdesc latex - dvips - ps2pdf pipeline needed. This is a TikZ port of
longdesc pst-labo (v2.07, 2025/07/15) by Denis Girou, Christophe
longdesc Jorssen, Manuel Luque, and Herbert Voss. The port uses English
longdesc command names with the tkz prefix instead of the original
longdesc French pst names, and all option keys have been translated to
longdesc English.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/aihua/tikz-chemlab/issues
catalogue-contact-development https://github.com/aihua/
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/aihua/tikz-chemlab
catalogue-ctan /graphics/pgf/contrib/tikz-chemlab
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics chemistry pgf-tikz
catalogue-version 1.0.0

name tikz-cookingsymbols
shortdesc Draw cooking symbols
longdesc The package uses TikZ for drawing cooking symbols like top
longdesc heat, airfryer and so on. The commands are provided in English
longdesc and German. The size of the symbol is based on the font size
longdesc and grabbed with \settoheight and \settodepth.
catalogue-also cookingsymbols
catalogue-ctan /graphics/pgf/contrib/tikz-cookingsymbols
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics cooking pgf-tikz
