name tpslifonts
shortdesc A LaTeX package for configuring presentation fonts
longdesc This package aims to improve of font readability in
longdesc presentations, especially with maths. The standard cm maths
longdesc fonts at large design sizes are difficult to read from far
longdesc away, especially at low resolutions and low contrast color
longdesc choice. Using this package leads to much better overall
longdesc readability of some font combinations. The package offers a
longdesc couple of harmonising combinations of text and maths fonts from
longdesc the (distant) relatives of computer modern fonts, with a couple
longdesc of extras for optimising readability. Text fonts from computer
longdesc modern roman, computer modern sans serif, SliTeX computer
longdesc modern sans serif, computer modern bright, or concrete roman
longdesc are available, in addition to maths fonts from computer modern
longdesc maths, computer modern bright maths, or Euler fonts. The
longdesc package is part of the TeXPower bundle.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/texpower/tpslifonts
catalogue-license gpl
catalogue-topics font-use presentation
catalogue-version 0.6

name tqft
shortdesc Drawing TQFT diagrams with TikZ/PGF
longdesc The package defines some node shapes useful for drawing TQFT
longdesc diagrams with TikZ/PGF. That is, it defines highly customisable
longdesc shapes that look like cobordisms between circles, such as those
longdesc used in TQFT and other mathematical diagrams.
catalogue-contact-home https://github.com/loopspace/TQFT
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/loopspace/TQFT
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/tqft
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics diagram graphics-use tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 2.3

name tracklang
shortdesc Language and dialect tracker
longdesc The tracklang package is provided for package developers who
longdesc want a simple interface to find out which languages the user
longdesc has requested through packages such as babel or polyglossia.
longdesc This package does not provide any translations! Its purpose is
longdesc simply to track which languages have been requested by the
longdesc user. Generic TeX code is in tracklang.tex for non-LaTeX users.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://www.dickimaw-books.com/bugtracker.php?search_category=tracklang
catalogue-contact-support https://www.dickimaw-books.com/faq.php?action=view&category=tracklang
catalogue-ctan /macros/generic/tracklang
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics class-supp multilingual package-devel tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 1.6.8

name traffic-light-protocol
shortdesc Show TLP (Traffic Light Protocol) tags
longdesc This LaTeX package provides a command \tlp to display TLP
longdesc (Traffic Light Protocol) labels. It currently relies on xcolor
longdesc and LaTeX3.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/janstarke/traffic-light-protocol
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/traffic-light-protocol
catalogue-license apache2
catalogue-topics colour
catalogue-version 0.2

name trainmap
shortdesc Draw railway line schematics and transit network maps with TikZ
longdesc TrainMap is an open-source LaTeX package built on TikZ for
longdesc designing schematic railway line maps and public transport
longdesc networks. It abstracts complex vector graphics into high-level
longdesc declarative commands, allowing users to draw straight and
longdesc branching rail lines using pgfkeys styling. The package
longdesc provides native commands for rendering intermediate stations
longdesc with angled labels (45deg) and terminal stations highlighted
longdesc with bold typography and line-code badges. It includes custom
longdesc layout environments to prevent label overlap, built-in scaling
longdesc compatibility for multi-station lines, and a full
longdesc CTAN-compliant structure featuring LPPL v1.3c licensing,
longdesc automated build files, and comprehensive usage documentation.
catalogue-ctan /graphics/pgf/contrib/trainmap
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics diagram graphics pgf-tikz tagged-pdf-incompatible
catalogue-version 1.0.0

name trajan
shortdesc Fonts from the Trajan column in Rome
longdesc Provides fonts (both as Metafont source and in Adobe Type 1
longdesc format) based on the capitals carved on the Trajan column in
longdesc Rome in 114 AD, together with macros to access the fonts. Many
longdesc typographers think these rank first among the Roman's artistic
longdesc legacy. The font is uppercase letters together with some
longdesc punctuation and analphabetics; no lowercase or digits.
catalogue-ctan /fonts/trajan
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics font font-archaic font-mf font-type1 tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 1.1

name tram
shortdesc Typeset tram boxes in LaTeX
longdesc Tram boxes are highlighted with patterns of dots; the package
longdesc defines an environment tram that typesets its content into a
longdesc tram box. The pattern used may be selected in an optional
longdesc argument to the environment.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/bidi-tex/tram/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/bidi-tex/tram
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/tram
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics boxing decoration editorial
catalogue-version 0.2

