name tuzuk
shortdesc Turkish bylaws and regulations document class
longdesc The tuzuk class provides a standardized format for writing
longdesc bylaws and regulations in Turkish-governmental style. It
longdesc includes features for creating numbered articles, subsections,
longdesc and signature areas commonly found in legal documents.
longdesc Features: Easy creation of numbered articles with the \madde
longdesc command, Section titles with \bolumadi, Automatic lettered
longdesc lists with the fikra environment, Built-in signature area
longdesc formatting with \imzalar, Full Turkish language support. Built
longdesc originally for creating the regulation for Ozgur Yazilim
longdesc Dernegi (The Free Software Association in Turkey),
longdesc https://oyd.org.tr/. Explanation of the package name: tuzuk in
longdesc Turkish means regulations, as a document. For example, GDPR,
longdesc which stands for General Data Protection Regulation, translates
longdesc as Genel Veri Koruma Tuzugu. In Turkish law, the non-profit
longdesc associations have a tuzuk as their constitution-like governing
longdesc document.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/ooguz/latex-tuzuk/issues
catalogue-contact-development https://github.com/ooguz/latex-tuzuk/pulls
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/ooguz/latex-tuzuk
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/tuzuk
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics class legal turkish
catalogue-version 1.0.0

