catalogue-ctan /graphics/metapost/contrib/macros/venn
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics diagram-maths

name venndiagram
shortdesc Creating Venn diagrams with TikZ
longdesc The package assists generation of simple two- and three-set
longdesc Venn diagrams for lectures or assignment sheets. The package
longdesc requires the TikZ package.
catalogue-also venn
catalogue-contact-home https://www.dickimaw-books.com/
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/venndiagram
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics diagram-maths pgf-tikz tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 1.2

name venturisadf
shortdesc Venturis ADF fonts collection
longdesc Serif and sans serif complete text font families, in both Adobe
longdesc Type 1 and OpenType formats for publication. The family is
longdesc based on Utopia family, and has been modified and developed by
longdesc the Arkandis Digital foundry. Support for using the fonts, in
longdesc LaTeX, is also provided (and makes use of the nfssext-cfr
longdesc package).
catalogue-contact-home https://arkandis.tuxfamily.org/tugfonts.htm
catalogue-contact-repository https://codeberg.org/cfr/nfssext
catalogue-ctan /fonts/venturisadf
catalogue-license lppl1.3 other-free
catalogue-topics font font-otf font-type1 tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 2.0

name verbasef
shortdesc VERBatim automatic splitting of external files
longdesc The package allows you to input (subsections of a) file, print
longdesc them in verbatim mode, while automatically breaking up the
longdesc input lines into pieces of a given length, which are output as
longdesc figures. These figures are posted using the [H] specification,
longdesc which forces LaTeX to place the figure at the spot of
longdesc invocation, rather than floating the figures to the top of the
longdesc next page. The package requires the verbatim, here and vrbexin
longdesc packages.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/verbasef
catalogue-license gpl
catalogue-topics listing verbatim
catalogue-version 1.1

name verbatimbox
shortdesc Deposit verbatim text in a box
longdesc The package provides a verbbox environment (which uses
longdesc techniques similar to those of the boxedverbatim environment of
longdesc the moreverb package) to place its contents into a globally
longdesc available box, or into a box specified by the user. The global
longdesc box may then be used in a variety of situations (for example,
longdesc providing a replica of the boxedverbatim environment itself). A
longdesc valuable use is in places where the standard verbatim
longdesc environment (which is based on a trivlist) may not appear. The
longdesc package makes use of the verbatim package (which is a required
longdesc part of any LaTeX distribution).
catalogue-also fancyvrb
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/verbatimbox
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics boxing tagged-pdf-incompatible verbatim
catalogue-version 3.2

name verbatimcopy
shortdesc Make copies of text documents from within LaTeX
longdesc This package provides \VerbatimCopy{in}{out} that will enable
longdesc LaTeX to take a verbatim copy of one text file, and save it
longdesc under another name. The package provides a means to specify the
longdesc output directory to be used, but does no checking and may
longdesc therefore overwrite an important file if used injudiciously.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/verbatimcopy
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics verbatim
catalogue-version 0.06

name verbdef
shortdesc Define commands which expand to verbatim text
longdesc The package defines a single command \verbdef (which has a
longdesc *-form, like \verb). \verbdef will define a robust command
longdesc whose body expands to verbatim text. By using commands defined
longdesc by \verbdef, one can put verbatim text into the arguments of
longdesc commands; since the defined command is robust, it doesn't
longdesc matter if the argument is moving. (Full details of syntax and
longdesc caveats about use are in comments in the file itself.)
catalogue-also newverbs
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/LaTeX-Package-Repositories/verbdef
catalogue-contact-support https://github.com/LaTeX-Package-Repositories/verbdef/issues
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/verbdef
catalogue-license lppl1.1
catalogue-topics tagged-pdf verbatim
catalogue-version 0.2

name verbments
shortdesc Syntax highlighting of source code in LaTeX documents
longdesc The package provides an environment for syntax highlighting
longdesc source code in LaTeX documents. The highlighted source code
longdesc output is formatted via powerful Pygments library of the Python
longdesc language.
catalogue-also minted texments
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/verbments
catalogue-license lppl1.2
catalogue-topics listing
catalogue-version 1.2

name verifica
shortdesc Typeset (Italian high school) exercises
longdesc This class provides various environments and commands to
longdesc produce the typical exercises contained in a test. It is mainly
longdesc intended for Italian high school teachers, as the style is
longdesc probably more in line with Italian high school tests.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/verifica
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics class exam exercise
catalogue-version 2.0

name verifiche
shortdesc A LaTeX package to typeset (Italian) high school tests
longdesc The purpose of this package is to manage the exercises for a
longdesc test, their points, levels of difficulty, and solutions. Some
longdesc typical formats of exercises are already implemented: Plain
longdesc exercise Complete the Text True or false Closed questions Open
longdesc questions Find the error
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/verifiche
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics exam exercise
catalogue-version 9.4

name verifycommand
shortdesc Verifies definitions are unchanged, such as before patching
longdesc This package is intended for package authors who patch code
longdesc from other packages. To improve reliability, the verifycommand
longdesc package provides a way to verify that macros or environments
longdesc have not changed. This allows a package author to check before
longdesc patching a definition. If a definition is not as expected, a
longdesc warning is issued. At the end of the compile, a list of all
longdesc changed definitions is displayed.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/bdtc/verifycommand
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/verifycommand
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics package-devel tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 1.12

name verse
shortdesc Aids for typesetting simple verse
longdesc The package documentation discusses approaches to the problem;
longdesc the package is strong on layout, from simple alternate-line
longdesc indentation to the Mouse's tale from Alice in Wonderland.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/LaTeX-Package-Repositories/herries-press
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/verse
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics tagged-pdf-partially verse
catalogue-version 2.5

name version
shortdesc Conditionally include text
longdesc Defines macros \includeversion{NAME} and \excludeversion{NAME},
longdesc each of which defines an environment NAME whose text is to be
longdesc included or excluded from compilation. Although the command
longdesc syntax is very similar to that of comment, comment.sty is to be
longdesc preferred to version.sty for documents where significant chunks
longdesc of text may be excluded.
catalogue-also verbatim versions optional comment
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/version
catalogue-license other-free
catalogue-topics cond-comp tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 2.0

name versions
shortdesc Optionally omit pieces of text
longdesc Stephan Bellantoni's version has provided preamble commands for
longdesc selecting environments to be included/excluded. This package
longdesc does the same, but corrects, improves, and extends it in both
longdesc implementation and function.
catalogue-also version optional verbatim comment
catalogue-contact-support https://www.webdesign-bu.de/uwe_lueck/contact.html
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/versions
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics cond-comp tagged-pdf
catalogue-version 0.55

name versonotes
shortdesc Display brief notes on verso pages
longdesc This package allows you to place notes on the verso pages of an
longdesc otherwise single-sided document. If, in the run of text, you
longdesc include a call to the macro \versonote{This is a remark}, then
longdesc that text will be placed on the opposite (ie, verso) page,
longdesc lined up with the macro call.
catalogue-contact-home https://nxg.me.uk/dist/versonotes/
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/versonotes
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics notes tagged-pdf-incompatible
catalogue-version 0.5

name vertbars
shortdesc Mark vertical rules in margin of text
longdesc This package is an extension to lineno, replacing that
longdesc package's line numbers with bars to the left or right of the
longdesc text.
catalogue-also changebar
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/LaTeX-Package-Repositories/herries-press
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/vertbars
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics editorial tagged-pdf-incompatible
catalogue-version 1.0c

name vexillology
shortdesc Vexillogical symbols
longdesc This package implements symbols used by vexillologists (people
longdesc who study flags) to indicate certain aspects of flags, such as
longdesc where they are used, who uses them, and what they look like.
longdesc The package uses TikZ to draw the symbols, whose heights scale
longdesc with the font size.
catalogue-ctan /graphics/pgf/contrib/vexillology
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics graphics graphics-symb pgf-tikz text-symbol
catalogue-version 1.0.0

name vgrid
shortdesc Overlay a grid on the printed page
longdesc The package overlays a grid (whose spacing is \baselineskip,
longdesc which offers guidlines for considering the rhythm of the
longdesc document on the page.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/vgrid
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics layout-supp
catalogue-version 0.1

name vhistory
shortdesc Support for creating a change log
longdesc Vhistory simplifies the creation of a history of versions of a
longdesc document. You can easily extract information like the current
longdesc version of a list of authors from that history. It helps you to
longdesc get consistent documents. The package sets, which is used by
longdesc vhistory, allows you to use sets containing text. You can use
longdesc the usual operations to create the union of sets or the
longdesc intersection of sets etc.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/vhistory
catalogue-license lppl1.2
catalogue-topics version-control
catalogue-version 1.8.0

name visualfaq
shortdesc A Visual LaTeX FAQ
longdesc Having trouble finding the answer to a LaTeX question? The
longdesc Visual LaTeX FAQ is an innovative new search interface that
longdesc presents over a hundred typeset samples of frequently requested
longdesc document formatting. Simply click on a hyperlinked piece of
longdesc text and the Visual LaTeX FAQ will send your Web browser to the
longdesc appropriate page in the TeX FAQ.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/spakin/visualFAQ
catalogue-ctan /info/visualfaq
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics faq

name visualfaq-fr
shortdesc FAQ LaTeX visuelle francophone
longdesc (French version below.) The Visual LaTeX FAQ is an innovative
longdesc new search interface on LaTeX Frequently Asked Questions. This
longdesc version is a French translation, offering links to the
longdesc French-speaking LaTeX FAQ. Vous avez du mal a trouver la
longdesc reponse a une question sur LaTeX ou meme a trouver les mots
longdesc pour exprimer votre question? La FAQ LaTeX visuelle est une
longdesc interface de recherche innovante qui presente plus d'une
longdesc centaine d'exemples de mises en forme de documents frequemment
longdesc demandees. Il suffit de cliquer sur l'hyperlien qui correspond
longdesc a ce que vous souhaitez faire - ou ne pas faire - et la FAQ
longdesc LaTeX visuelle enverra votre navigateur web a la page
longdesc correspondante de la FAQ LaTeX francophone.
catalogue-contact-home https://www.latex-fr.net
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/jejust/visualFAQ-fr
catalogue-ctan /info/visualfaq-fr
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics faq french-doc

name visualpstricks
shortdesc Visual help for PSTricks based on images with minimum text
longdesc Visual help for PSTricks based on images with minimum text. One
longdesc image per command or per parameter.
catalogue-ctan /info/visualpstricks
catalogue-license gpl
catalogue-topics french-doc graphics-doc graphics-in-tex pstricks
catalogue-version 2.3

name visualtikz
shortdesc Visual help for TikZ based on images with minimum text
longdesc Visual help for TikZ based on images with minimum text: an
longdesc image per command or parameter. The document is in French, but
longdesc will be translated into English later.
catalogue-ctan /info/visualtikz
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics french-doc graphics-doc graphics-in-tex pgf-tikz
catalogue-version 0.65

name visualtoks
shortdesc Typeset TeXbook-style visualisations of token lists
longdesc This package provides the \visualtoks command to display
longdesc arbitrary list of tokens, for pedagogical or debugging
longdesc purposes, in a style inspired by Knuth's The TeXbook. The
longdesc package may be used in plain TeX or LaTeX.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/plante3/visualtoks/tree/main
catalogue-ctan /macros/generic/visualtoks
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics etex macro-demo macro-gen
catalogue-version 1.1b

