name xint
shortdesc Expandable arbitrary precision floating point and integer operations
longdesc Loading xintexpr provides \xinteval and \xintfloateval.
longdesc \xintfloateval evaluates numerical expressions. The floating
longdesc point precision defaults to 16 decimal digits and can be set by
longdesc user. Trigonometry, exponential and logarithms are implemented
longdesc up to a maximal precision of 62 decimal digits. \xinteval
longdesc computes exactly with integers, fractions, and decimal numbers
longdesc or numbers in scientific notation. Note though that multiplying
longdesc two floating point numbers will about double the number of
longdesc digits, and so on, because the algebra is done exactly. Both
longdesc are compatible with expansion-only context. Loading xintexpr
longdesc imports automatically various other modules that it depends
longdesc upon. Among them: xinttools: utilities such as expandable and
longdesc non-expandable loops, xint: macros implementing in particular
longdesc the basic operations on arbitrarily long integers, xintbinhex:
longdesc conversions between decimal and binary, octal, or hexadecimal
longdesc bases for arbitrarily long integers, xintfrac: macros
longdesc implementing in particular the basic operations on arbitrarily
longdesc large fractions, decimal numbers, or numbers in scientific
longdesc notation. Further modules of independent interest include
longdesc xintgcd, xintseries and xintcfrac. You can use xintexpr (and
longdesc the other components) with LaTeX (via \usepackage) or also with
longdesc Plain TeX, OpTeX, or ConTeXt (via \input xintexpr.sty). All the
longdesc components are documented in the file xint.pdf, which also
longdesc contains the commented source code.
catalogue-alias xintexpr
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/jfbu/xint/issues
catalogue-contact-home https://jfbu.github.io/xint
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/jfbu/xint
catalogue-ctan /macros/generic/xint
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics arithmetic calculation
catalogue-version 1.4o

name xint-regression
shortdesc Classic regressions, with xint
longdesc A package for determining classical regressions (linear,
longdesc quadratic, cubic, exponential, etc.) with calculations
longdesc performed by xint. Results (raw or rounded) can be stored in
longdesc customizable macros.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/cpierquet/latex-packages/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/cpierquet/latex-packages/tree/main/xint-regression
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/xint-regression
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics calculation maths
catalogue-version 0.1.4

name xintsession
shortdesc Interactive computing sessions (fractions, floating points, polynomials)
longdesc This package provides support for interactive computing
longdesc sessions with etex (or pdftex) executed on the command line, on
longdesc the basis of the xintexpr and polexpr packages. Once
longdesc xintsession is loaded, eTeX becomes an interactive computing
longdesc software capable of executing arbitrary precision calculations,
longdesc or exact calculations with arbitrarily big fractions. It can
longdesc also manipulate polynomials as algebraic entities. Numerical
longdesc variables and functions can be defined during the session, and
longdesc each evaluation result is stored in automatically labeled
longdesc variables. A file is automatically created storing inputs and
longdesc outputs.
catalogue-ctan /macros/plain/contrib/xintsession
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics calculation maths
catalogue-version 0.4alpha

name xistercian
shortdesc Cistercian numerals in LaTeX
longdesc This package allows you to use Cistercian numerals in LaTeX.
longdesc The glyphs are created using PGF and to a certain degree
longdesc configurable. You can use Cistercian numerals as page numbers
longdesc using \pagenumbering{cistercian}. The two main macros are:
longdesc \cistercian{<counter>} formats the LaTeX2e counter as a
longdesc Cistercian numeral, \cisterciannum{<integer>} formats the
longdesc integer (given as a string) as a Cistercian numeral.
catalogue-also cistercian
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/Skillmon/ltx_xistercian
catalogue-ctan /graphics/pgf/contrib/xistercian
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics graphics numbers pgf-tikz tagged-pdf-partially
catalogue-version 1.3

name xits
shortdesc A Scientific Times-like font with support for mathematical typesetting
longdesc XITS is a Times-like font for scientific typesetting with
longdesc proper mathematical support for modern, Unicode and OpenType
longdesc capable TeX engines, namely LuaTeX and XeTeX. For use with
longdesc LuaLaTeX or XeLaTeX, support is available from the fontspec and
longdesc unicode-math packages.
