name xkcdcolors
shortdesc xkcd names of colors
longdesc In the year 2010, Randall Munroe on posted a really funny and
longdesc nice article on xkcd. He made a very curious experiment:
longdesc showing colors to a lot of people and asking to name each one.
longdesc Afterward, he processed the data and sorted the names for each
longdesc color by popularity - that means, how many people gave the same
longdesc name to the same color. This package makes the collected color
longdesc names usable with LaTeX.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/Rmano/xkcdcolors/issues
catalogue-contact-home https://rlog.rgtti.com/2015/10/23/xkcd-color-list-for-latex-users/
