name xprintlen
shortdesc Print TeX lengths in a variety of units
longdesc The package defines a command, \printlen, to print TeX lengths
longdesc in a variety of units. It can handle all units supported by
longdesc TeX. The package requires that a reasonably up to date version
longdesc of the fp package be installed on you system.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/Liam0205/xprintlen
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/xprintlen
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics debug-supp doc-debug
catalogue-version 1.0

name xpunctuate
shortdesc Process trailing punctuation which may be redundant
longdesc The package provides commands enabling the user (or package
longdesc writer) to insert punctuation after a macro. The method is
longdesc similar to that of xspace, but goes further. The package
longdesc provides the commands \xperiod, \xcomma and \xperiodcomma,
longdesc which follow a similar procedure to that of \xspace, and insert
longdesc punctuation if and only if it is necessary. It also provides
longdesc \xperiodafter, \xcommaafter, \xperiodcommaafter and
longdesc \xspaceafter, which all take one argument, the word or phrase
longdesc to be punctuated. These then avoid problems with the spacing of
longdesc periods and commas after emphasised words.
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/xpunctuate
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics macro-supp
catalogue-version 2.0

name xq
shortdesc Support for writing about xiangqi
longdesc The package is for writing about xiangqi or chinese chess. You
longdesc can write games or parts of games and show diagrams with
longdesc special positions.
catalogue-ctan /fonts/xq
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics chess games tagged-pdf-unsupported
catalogue-version 0.4

name xreview
shortdesc Reviewing LaTeX documents made easy(er)
longdesc This package provides a simple way to review LaTeX documents.
longdesc It allows to highlight and/or hide changes to a document, and
longdesc to add comments to the text. This will help you to keep track
longdesc of the changes you make to a document, and to easily spot the
longdesc changes made by others, while always having the option of
longdesc compiling a clean version of the document. This package also
longdesc offers a way to include comments in the text, which can be
longdesc toggled on and off. This is useful for adding notes to the
longdesc text, or for leaving comments to other authors.
catalogue-contact-home https://github.com/LorenzoPeri17/xreview-latex
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/LorenzoPeri17/xreview-latex
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/xreview
catalogue-license mit
catalogue-topics review-document
catalogue-version 2.0

name xsavebox
shortdesc Saveboxes for repeating content without code replication, based on PDF Form XObjects
longdesc The package defines commands for saving content that can be
longdesc repeatedly placed into the document without replicating DVI/PDF
longdesc code in the output file, allowing for smaller file size of the
longdesc final PDF and improved content caching for faster display in
longdesc certain PDF viewers. The method makes use of Form XObjects
longdesc defined in the PDF specification. The user commands are
longdesc modelled after the standard LaTeX commands \savebox, \sbox,
longdesc \usebox and the lrbox environment. All common TeX engines and
longdesc back-ends are supported: pdfLaTeX, LuaLaTeX LaTeX - dvips -
longdesc ps2pdf/Distiller (Xe)LaTeX - (x)dvipdfmx
catalogue-contact-repository https://gitlab.com/agrahn/xsavebox
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/xsavebox
catalogue-license lppl
catalogue-topics adobe-distiller boxing pdf-feat tagged-pdf-incompatible
catalogue-version 0.18

name xsim
shortdesc eXercise Sheets IMproved
longdesc This package helps in creating exercises and the corresponding
longdesc solutions. It is the official successor of the exsheets package
longdesc and fixes/improves various long-standing issues.
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/cgnieder/xsim/issues
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/cgnieder/xsim/
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/xsim
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics exam exercise
catalogue-version 0.21

name xsipa
shortdesc Short XSAMPA-based commands for IPA transcription in LaTeX
longdesc This LaTeX package provides a lightweight phonetic
longdesc transcription system inspired by XSAMPA. It translates modified
longdesc XSAMPA sequences into proper IPA symbols, using either the tipa
longdesc package (for pdfTeX users) or Unicode IPA symbols via xunicode
longdesc (for XeTeX and LuaTeX users). The package was designed to
longdesc simplify phonetic transcription in LaTeX by offering concise
longdesc macros such as \xsE for \textepsilon, and \xs*...* as a
longdesc shortcut for multi-symbol sequences (e.g., \xs*EO* for eo).
longdesc These commands are modeled after XSAMPA but adapted for LaTeX
longdesc compatibility - including custom replacements for reserved
longdesc characters.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/dbjoshua/xsipa_package
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/xsipa
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics phonetic
catalogue-version 1.0

name xskak
shortdesc An extension to the skak package for chess typesetting
longdesc Xskak, as its prime function, saves information about a chess
longdesc game for later use (e.g., to loop through a game to make an
longdesc animated board). The package also extends the input that the
longdesc parsing commands can handle and offers an interface to define
longdesc and switch between indefinite levels of styles.
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/u-fischer/xskak
catalogue-contact-support https://github.com/u-fischer/xskak/issues
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/xskak
catalogue-license lppl1
catalogue-topics chess etex games tagged-pdf-incompatible
catalogue-version 1.5

name xstacks
shortdesc Dedicated global stacks implementations
longdesc This package aims at solving one problem: how to preserve some
longdesc values (tokens) beyond a variable number of nested groups. Four
longdesc alternative strategies are implemented.
